n your opinion on Genius, both as a general nerd who likes to hear people's thought process, and also in relation to things that might be worth looking at for Genius 2E.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T17:30:14-07:00","id":950326,"title":"","content":"Also interested in your thoughts. I'm in a similar boat when it comes to feelings toward the general concept of mad scientists, and have seen (and occasionally been annoyed by the omnipresence and force of) the praise for Genius as well, so I'm curious to hear whether or not it manages to capture your interests at all despite your rather sour introduction to it. Both as a general review and as a possible motivator to give it more than the partial skim of a year or two back.<br /> <br /> ... Aaand I'm intrigued by your choices in music, which is a lesser factor, but admittedly more relevant than it ought to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I've got a bit of a bad habit of extensively editing my posts after the fact. Please try and bear with me...<br /> In case you're comfortable being more friendly and casual about things, my name's Seren, or Es/Es for short. They/Them or Fae/Faer, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","name":"Sconce","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T17:39:06-07:00","id":950329,"title":"","content":"Good Intro section, Sean. I might be wrong, but I also thought an initial conflict with Genius coming out was with an internal conflict amongst the writers of Genius and/or other texts? I do not remember details or names or where I heard that from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T17:40:37-07:00","id":950331,"title":"","content":"(Also, full disclosure, my partner, who minored in Physics at Uni, likes Genius a lot. I'm not a fan.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T17:53:28-07:00","id":950335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=950329#post950329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good Intro section, Sean. I might be wrong, but I also thought an initial conflict with Genius coming out was with an internal conflict amongst the writers of Genius and/or other texts? I do not remember details or names or where I heard that from.</div> </div> </div> </div>In regards to writer conflicts, this was, as far as I know, an open source production developed over on RPG.net, that wretched hive of scum and villainy that was also the place we got Dave Brookshaw from, so mixed results. My default assumption is that internal conflict was basically pervasive throughout the entire process. The PDF only cites Kyle Marquis as writer, developer, and *cough* layout artist though, so it might have been smoother than expected.<br /> <br /> As for conflict with the rest of the texts in the ChroD canon....We'll talk about that when we get there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T17:57:39-07:00","id":950337,"title":"","content":"I will endeavor, by the way, to try and not make this entire thing nothing but one big &quot;Why the fuck isn't this just the science hack from Mage's Chroniclers Guide?&quot;, but I'ma say it now: Genius is fighting me hard on that front, and I imagine we're going to definitely talk about the Mage the Ascension Elephant as soon as we can to avoid choking the rest of the review with it, or at least to try to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T18:32:40-07:00","id":950355,"title":"","content":"I'm actually gonna be following this closely. Since the intent behind Mage: The Transgression is to fix the problems with Ascension, Awakening, and Transgression, it'll probably be quite helpful to see a very critical perspective, even if I'll probably disagree with a lot of it. <br /> <br /> Right out of the gate, for example, I just can't relate to Arc's disdain for the mad scientist. The mad scientist and Frankenstein's Monster have always been my favorite classic monsters, and it's always been one of my favorite, if not my favorite, fictional archetype.<br /> <br /> And that leads into the &quot;why not just use the Mage science hack&quot; issue. To someone like Arc, who doesn't really have a connection to the mad scientist archetype, it makes sense, but to someone who really loves mad scientists and their role in horror media, it just seems unfair that they should only be able to exist as part of an old Awakening sourcebook. And Genius gets that. I think it might actually have been better as its own thing, because it creates such a complete and versatile setting. And the brilliance of that setting, and why a Mage hack isn't enough, is that it wonderfully deconstructs the entire idea of &quot;mad science&quot; by creating a setting where science is treated the way fiction treats magic. Manes are a perfect example of that. They are, essentially, the ghosts of debunked scientific theories and superstitions, and that is WONDERFUL.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 08-13-2016, 09:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T18:33:16-07:00","id":950356,"title":"","content":"I played Genius once. Everything you point out as a mark against in your intro it is super accurate in my eyes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T18:36:14-07:00","id":950361,"title":"","content":"I was briefly interested in Genius when I first heard about it back in, oh, 2010? It didn't grab me, but not a lot did at the time. We'll see what this review enkindles within me, however.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T18:47:12-07:00","id":950367,"title":"","content":"So, quick thing on backgrounds, as an additional &quot;Where I'm coming from&quot;.<br /> <br /> I grew up spending my teenager years working on fan-made games over on the now dead and gone MSN Groups-I actually did that for about a decade of my life. Commentary on development is written less from research on Genius(have you seen that thread?) and more from my own experience with those games. But I do have a background in more or less open source development for amateur projects.<br /> <br /> Also, not that I'm gonna weigh this in much, but I have an Associates with a major in English Education and History Education, and a Bachelors with a major in Creative Writing English and a minor in Visual Communications. So, you know. I know a thing or two about this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 08-13-2016, 10:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T19:08:21-07:00","id":950374,"title":"","content":"As someone who's been running Genius for years, thinks it works perfectly well as a horror game, but who has heard the horror stories of people crowbarring Genius characters in (as pulp action heroes, no less) to other World of Darkness games to their severe detriment, this is going to be an interesting thread to watch.<br /> <br /> The mechanics are clunky, and I can't relate to the whole &quot;Awakening was shit, I'm going to make nWoD Ascension myself&quot; angle at all, but it's still in my top three gamelines. Something about these poor mad men and women searching through the detritus of dead ideas, so blinded by their own abilities and the light burning behind their eyes that they can't see it will all amount to nothing in the end is interesting to me. The whole concept of Jabir, as well. You can't relate to normal people; you can't even communicate your ideas to normal people, half because what you're saying is nonsense that only makes sense to your own worldview and half because just trying to do so burns away their own unique perspective to replace it <i>with</i> your own cracked worldview.<br /> <br /> I haven't heard of many others who play Genius for tragedy and horror, though, so hmm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","name":"Juhn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T20:26:00-07:00","id":950404,"title":"","content":"I'm in sort of an odd place in that I love the Sons of Ether and have generally been disappointed by the lack of a good analog for them in ChroD, but have simultaneously just never been turned on by Genius. I think it may just be that the Etherite concepts I enjoy don't fit well in Genius, despite their superficial similarities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T21:10:54-07:00","id":950426,"title":"","content":"I've read Genius, and found it to be very well-written, but the tone of the writing basically told me, &quot;This is not a WoD game,&quot; despite its trying very hard to fit into it.<br /> <br /> That said? De-contextualized from nWoD/CofD, Genius is the single most joyful RPG book I have ever read. It <i>cavorts</i> in its subject matter and revels in it to a degree that I had not seen before. Which made it special to me. It was excellent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T21:14:30-07:00","id":950429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=950426#post950426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've read Genius, and found it to be very well-written, but the tone of the writing basically told me, &quot;This is not a WoD game,&quot; despite its trying very hard to fit into it.<br /> <br /> That said? De-contextualized from nWoD/CofD, Genius is the single most joyful RPG book I have ever read. It <i>cavorts</i> in its subject matter and revels in it to a degree that I had not seen before. Which made it special to me. It was excellent.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is funny to me, because I can unashamedly admit at this point I question if the point of the opening story was somehow to anti-sell the game. <i>Verney</i> wasn't that pessimistic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T00:59:31-07:00","id":950471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius#post950278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In particular, it's that last part where the place for Genius finally came about. You had some fans who might be enjoying the differences Chronicles had, but missed out on how the things you well and truly valued no longer had a representation in the world, and that it was instead replaced by what they probably regarded as it's antithesis. As time went on, it became clear that wasn't a mistake worth fixing to White Wolf. There would be no Sons of Ether in Mage the Awakening. To them, it probably seemed like there would be no Sons of Ether in Chronicles of Darkness <i>period.</i><br /> <br /> So, an idea was sprung in the head of a guy names Kyle Marquis, TvTropes tells me. That person would <i>make</i> this slice of Mage the Ascension without it being Mage the Awakening, and fill the void that White Wolf had left in their fanbase.</div> </div> </div> </div>One thing you should keep in mind is that while Kyle Marquis was a long time Ascension fan, Genius isn'tjust an attempt to bring back the Sons of Ether and Virtual Adepts into the nWoD.<br /> <br /> In many ways it is a response to Ascension, a philosophical counter arguement if you will. The core premise is a rejection of core Ascension ideas like the secret world controlling masters, or &quot;enlightened&quot; people who can see secret truths that mortal men cannot. In fact Both the Traditions and the Technocracy's Genius counterparts are in Lemuria, the antagonist organisation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius#post950278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><u>I AM MAD SCIENTIST! IS SO COOL!-Biases, or &quot;Didn't I beat up this guy for lunch money?&quot;</u></b><br /> <br /> The lunch money comment might be going overboard, but I feel like it accurately conveys what I think of when I think &quot;mad scientist&quot;-largely, that I'm unimpressed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just wanted to say while that you draw a distinction between the Mad Scientists who superman beat up and the sane but dangerous scientists who cloned dinosaurs for Jurassic Park and find the mad scientists wanting. Genius does not make a distinction.<br /> <br /> Genius draws just as much, if not more, inspiration from Jurassic Park and similar works as it does from Superman (and when it does draw from Superman it's less goofy portrayals like the DCAU's Joker or Lex Luthor.<br /> <br /> In Genius a mad scientist's insanity is a bi-directional metaphor with the dinosaurs in Jurassic park breaking out of control. The loss of control over a Genius' own mind reflects the loss of control over the cloned dinosaurs. The loss of control over the cloned dinosaurs reflects the loss of control over a Genius' own mind.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=950335#post950335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In regards to writer conflicts, this was, as far as I know, an open source production developed over on RPG.net, that wretched hive of scum and villainy that was also the place we got Dave Brookshaw from, so mixed results. My default assumption is that internal conflict was basically pervasive throughout the entire process. The PDF only cites Kyle Marquis as writer, developer, and *cough* layout artist though, so it might have been smoother than expected.<br /> <br /> As for conflict with the rest of the texts in the ChroD canon....We'll talk about that when we get there.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's only one writer. (I did contribute some updated Prostasia rules but that was long after it was published)<br /> <br /> Genius' dev was basically an open dev. There was feedback and discussion, but in the end there was only one writer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=950429#post950429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is funny to me, because I can unashamedly admit at this point I question if the point of the opening story was somehow to anti-sell the game. <i>Verney</i> wasn't that pessimistic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I found it beautiful, in a nihlistic way. The line about spaceships rotting haunted me for a long while in a good way, it's just a beautiful visual.<br /> <br /> &quot;There's no purpose to anything&quot; sounds like a challenge to me, to create a purpose. It's that or lay down and wait to die.<br /> <br /> (I feel the same about real life, so that's probably why. If I recall you're religious Arc? Mormon wasn't it? Faith in a higher power with a hand on the rudder of the universe might result in you reading it very differently to me, and I <i>think</i> I'm reading it as intended. A core theme element is that nobody is in charge and nobody has a plan or any idea where we're going).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 08-14-2016, 04:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T01:16:49-07:00","id":950475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=950471#post950471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In many ways it is a response to Ascension, a philosophical counter arguement if you will. The core premise is a rejection of core Ascension ideas like the secret world controlling masters, or &quot;enlightened&quot; people who can see secret truths that mortal men cannot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which misses that Ascension already did that, indeed it's kinda the point. I know Ascension was pretty bad at explaining itself, but if you read the last edition, a character literally explains it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T07:58:12-07:00","id":950551,"title":"","content":"Is it bad that I'm interested in hearing about your take on Sword Art Online too? *cough*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T08:38:42-07:00","id":950571,"title":"","content":"As one of those people who got into WoD because of Genius, I'm also interested in seeing this review.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=950471#post950471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's only one writer. (I did contribute some updated Prostasia rules but that was long after it was published)</div> </div> </div> </div>That was you? That's cool.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8064-mp122984","name":"mp122984","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T10:38:14-07:00","id":950632,"title":"","content":"This will be interesting. For a long time, I used Geniuses instead of Mages in my game background. It seemed to me like you couldn't have both, and I did not *get* Mage. Then Dave came along with 2e open dev and I suddenly understood the Awakened, and never looked back. I'd agree that Genius loved itself. I'd also agree it wasn't nearly as good at horro as it was pulp. I also discovered it through TvTropes, so I had squat to do with the community that was apparently so toxic. In fact, this is the first I'm hearing about it.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I'm also going to try and do a read through at the same time as Arc, chapter by chapter, so I can give better responses. I'd strongly suggest others do too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":4433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","user":"Second Chances","date":". 08-14-2016, 02:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T11:52:33-07:00","id":950673,"title":"","content":"I'll also be following this thread- I've only gave Genius a brief look (I can barely convince my friends to play RPG at all. Convince them to play a fan game is almost impossible), and I've never exactly made my mind about it. The idea of playing a Mad Scientist did sounded as an interesting premise to me, but it have always felt to me like Mage with make up and a different dress, and I wonder how much of it is the case (and I'm too lazy to actually review it on myself :P )<br /> <br /> besides, I always like reading reviews. It's kinda a hobby of mine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T23:33:51-07:00","id":950951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=950475#post950475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which misses that Ascension already did that, indeed it's kinda the point. I know Ascension was pretty bad at explaining itself, but if you read the last edition, a character literally explains it.</div> </div> </div> </div>You'll have to go into more detail. I'm not an expert on Ascension but I understand that revised moved away from the Ascension War; I don't think it ever moved away from the idea that Mages saw secret truths that mortals did not.<br /> <br /> Even then, it said that secret world controlling masters were a bad thing, but Ascension Revised didn't say that actually the Technoracy never had that much influence in the first place. Did it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 08-15-2016, 02:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T02:27:42-07:00","id":950995,"title":"","content":"It's not that Ascension mages really &quot;see secret truths beyond the ken of normal people.&quot; Ascension mages just have access to things normal people didn't by virtue of their supernatural powers. Other supernaturals in the WoD are capable of seeing every truth a mage is, and with a supernatural showing it to them so could any mortal. In fact others doing it might be easier because Paradox. What separates mages from everyone else is their ability to directly interact with those truths (keeping in mind that in Ascension, virtually all mortals indirectly interact with them to shape reality), not a special kind of insight that only mages possess. Actually showing such things to mortals would be supremely dick move in most circumstances though.<br /> <br /> And Ascension has waffled a lot on how much influence the Technocracy was supposed to have. Though Revised cut their influence significantly (since their secret masters were stuck on the wrong side of the Avatar Storm as well), as well as having the Technocracy lose control of their biggest &quot;secret masters controlling everything,&quot; leverage point by losing control over Consensus to apathy. Basically, the Technocracy's own internal issues dead-ended their efforts to control reality, leaving them with plenty of ways to secretly control people, but far less in terms of guiding humanity along the Time Table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T03:36:56-07:00","id":951023,"title":"","content":"Thanks for that Heavy Arms. (and your reply on RPG.net)<br /> <br /> So to make sure I understand you correctly:<br /> <br /> 1) Mages see truths that the <i>average</i> mortal does not see. But there's no reason why a mortal can't bring themselves up to a Mage's level.<br /> 2) It's unclear how influential the technocracy are; but Revised Edition / the Avatar Storm reduces their influence through an in setting event; rather than retconning them to always have had less influence.<br /> <br /> That does seem like a contrast to Genius where<br /> <br /> 1) Geniuses are worse at understanding the truths of the world than the average mortal with a good grade in high school science, because they're crazy.<br /> 2) Lemuria's influence is also intentionally unclear but a lot of Geniuses speculate they were never particularly influential in the first place, and a close reading of the text leads me to assume those Geniuses were right.<br /> <br /> My interpretation is that Lemuria resembles the late era technocracy, running around purging stuff but utterly failing to actually direct humanity. That is, Lemuria looked like late era technocracy from at least 425 BC (possibly earlier) without any historical point where they resemble the Order of Reason who actually did manage to make their Paradigm domiment and basically were competent enough to get things done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 08-15-2016, 06:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T13:05:14-07:00","id":951263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=950551#post950551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it bad that I'm interested in hearing about your take on Sword Art Online too? *cough*</div> </div> </div> </div>The deepest regret Felix and I have is that we didn't realize what we might have on our hands when we started fighting over SAO. It's gonna take, like, a year to get to a point where we might be able to talk about the series with the same vigor as we did this time around.<br /> <br /> I might get out my side of it in the anime thread, but Genius is pulling on my sleeve.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T13:27:50-07:00","id":951274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=950471#post950471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Genius a mad scientist's insanity is a bi-directional metaphor with the dinosaurs in Jurassic park breaking out of control. The loss of control over a Genius' own mind reflects the loss of control over the cloned dinosaurs. The loss of control over the cloned dinosaurs reflects the loss of control over a Genius' own mind.<br /> <br /> (I feel the same about real life, so that's probably why. If I recall you're religious Arc? Mormon wasn't it? Faith in a higher power with a hand on the rudder of the universe might result in you reading it very differently to me, and I <i>think</i> I'm reading it as intended. A core theme element is that nobody is in charge and nobody has a plan or any idea where we're going).</div> </div> </div> </div>Addressing these two in reverse order.<br /> <br /> 1) Not a Mormon anymore. I couldn't keep justifying the bullshit as well as the sense of things outside of the church. But I am of a strongly spiritual bent. Of course, my spiritual humanism is an absurdist response, because nihilism is the thing that is pervasive in my life.<br /> <br /> Anyways, as it relates to Genius...are you seriously trying to tell me because I have belief in powers that be, I'm not gonna like Genius which posits nothing is in control? Me, who's main argument anytime cosmology comes up is &quot;Reality is, at best, a bunch of squabbling occult god-children-principles fighting over a toy with all the sound and sense of those children and at it's most realistic is this great abiding mystery that has no answer because it's very nature is unanswerable, indirectable, unguidable?&quot; You are literally telling the guy who has been saying <i>for years</i> that there is no order or reason or sense or knowing to the universe of ChroD that he might have a different reading because the book strongly stands by a universe that has no order or reason or sense or knowing.<br /> <br /> <i>Think who you're talking to</i>.<br /> <br /> 2) Jurassic's Parks theme was not mad scientists, but greedy corporate monguls who forced the hands of scientists out of a desire for profit. Jurassic Park was not anti-science, it was anti-corporate. Notice anyone with an inkling of scientific understanding comments on the insanity of this, at a minimum &quot;I'm not really sure I should be doing this&quot; to Ian Malcolm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 08-15-2016, 04:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T13:35:07-07:00","id":951279,"title":"","content":"Eagerly awaiting the other chapters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T13:38:06-07:00","id":951285,"title":"","content":"Spoiler: 488 pages of nothing but text is, in retrospect, a bad idea for a game book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T13:50:47-07:00","id":951293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=951285#post951285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spoiler: 488 pages of nothing but text is, in retrospect, a bad idea for a game book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Art requires artists (or at least artistic talent). If it was assembled by one person, that explains it.<br /> <br /> If I recall, neither Princess nor Leviathan have much in the way of art (though Leviathan has art notes).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T13:59:53-07:00","id":951299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=951293#post951293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Art requires artists (or at least artistic talent). If it was assembled by one person, that explains it.<br /> <br /> If I recall, neither Princess nor Leviathan have much in the way of art (though Leviathan has art notes).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll talk about this in the review, the problems of art and word count and other such things, but for now I am going to point out a case of &quot;Be careful what you wish for.&quot;<br /> <br /> For years, I have dealt with Genius fans who have wanted Genius treated as though it were an actual game from White Wolf/Onyx Path, to count it among the canon-hell, it was actually listed in the canon list of games on TvTropes for a time, if you can believe it.<br /> <br /> I could review this game as a fangame and give it a bunch of slack-an okay game from the fans is quite frankly an excellent result in my eyes.<br /> <br /> Or I could give what those fans wanted all along, and treat Genius as though it were a professionally made game.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure it's worth doing this just treating it as a fangame anyways.<br /> <br /> Be careful what you wish for, and don't make promises you can't keep.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 08-15-2016, 05:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T14:13:02-07:00","id":951308,"title":"","content":"Also worth noting:<br /> <br /> The credits have made it clear that there is only one guy who worked on it, but I'm going to talk about this project as though it had a team, for two reasons.<br /> <br /> 1) It's easier for me to just talk that way, I think of projects in terms of teams.<br /> <br /> 2) As has been pointed out a couple of times, Genius may have only been &quot;made&quot; by one guy, but the development of that game was open source, with Kyle Marquis taking in a bunch of advice and ideas in from the people at RPG.net. Therefore, I don't feel comfortable in criticisizing or praising(yes, believe it or not, I do have points of praise) Marquis alone, since it's really kind of the thought baby of everyone Kyle valued the opinion of over the course of it's creation. Marquis might be the one who made the book, but it was developed by a team of people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T14:14:52-07:00","id":951309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=951263#post951263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The deepest regret Felix and I have is that we didn't realize what we might have on our hands when we started fighting over SAO. It's gonna take, like, a year to get to a point where we might be able to talk about the series with the same vigor as we did this time around.<br /> <br /> I might get out my side of it in the anime thread, but Genius is pulling on my sleeve.</div> </div> </div> </div>Links, please, if you do. I'm kind of curious, since I have a lot of friends who like it. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T14:37:39-07:00","id":951315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=951274#post951274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You are literally telling the guy who has been saying <i>for years</i> that there is no order or reason or sense or knowing to the universe of ChroD that he might have a different reading because the book strongly stands by a universe that has no order or reason or sense or knowing.<br /> <br /> <i>Think who you're talking to</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Take Changeling. Changeling's cosmology might be a bunch of squabbling occult god children fighting over a toy, but it's about moving forward after surviving abuse. Genius is actually about the meaninglessness of the universe (among other things). Genius player characters should be confronted with that meaninglessness directly and if they're lucky, find inner peace through accepting it.<br /> <br /> To me comparing nihilism-as-setting-element to nihilism-as-core-theme is like comparing apples to oranges. But if you say your views on nihilism-as-setting-element transfer to nihilism-as-core-theme then I'll take your word for it. You know yourself far better than I ever will.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=951274#post951274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) Jurassic's Parks theme was not mad scientists, but greedy corporate monguls who forced the hands of scientists out of a desire for profit. Jurassic Park was not anti-science, it was anti-corporate. Notice anyone with an inkling of scientific understanding comments on the insanity of this, at a minimum &quot;I'm not really sure I should be doing this&quot; to Ian Malcolm.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Jurassic Park: the Lost World reveals John Hammond has a doctorate and in the video game Jurassic Park: Tresspasser he is explicitly described as a &quot;jovial mad-scientist&quot;.<br /> <br /> 2) Even if John Hammond wasn't a mad scientist Jurassic Park would still be a film about mad science. The very core of mad science is the fear of change caused by a new idea or new technology. A mad science story then takes those fears which are often highly abstract and complex (how will society change once cloning technology makes it possible to create babies without romance, sex, marriage or even parents?) and distils it down into into something understandable and comforting (our heroes vs dinosaurs). The mad scientist, the cackling man with bad hair and a labcoat, is not technically needed for a mad science story.<br /> <br /> 3) Nothing you said contradicts the idea of using Jurassic Park as an inspirational source for Genius anyway. Genius is not anti-science (I'm not sure if you meant to imply that or not. It's not anti-corporate either). The scientist characters trying to warn John Hammond is exactly how sane scientists would react to a Genius talking about their crazy schemes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=951293#post951293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Art requires artists (or at least artistic talent). If it was assembled by one person, that explains it.<br /> <br /> If I recall, neither Princess nor Leviathan have much in the way of art (though Leviathan has art notes).</div> </div> </div> </div>Sadly this is true. I am planning to include art found around the net for Leviathan 2ED if I can get permission.<br /> <br /> Also, If you know any interested fan artists do send them my way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 08-15-2016, 06:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T14:51:33-07:00","id":951318,"title":"","content":"Telling one of the writers of Changeling to consider Changeling? Ummm..... I think that Arcane is rather familar with that game, KingRaven.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T14:55:15-07:00","id":951322,"title":"","content":"Obviously. That's why I used it as an example.<br /> <br /> (Do let me know if I'm wrong when I say Changeling is about moving on after surviving abuse - I would have to reconsider a LOT)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 08-15-2016, 05:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T14:56:20-07:00","id":951323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=951315#post951315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) Even if John Hammond wasn't a mad scientist Jurassic Park would still be a film about mad science. The very core of mad science is the fear of change caused by a new idea or new technology. A mad science story then takes those fears which are often highly abstract and complex (how will society change once cloning technology makes it possible to create babies without romance, sex, marriage or even parents?) and distils it down into into something understandable and comforting (our heroes vs dinosaurs). The mad scientist, the cackling man with bad hair and a labcoat, is not technically needed for a mad science story.<br /> <br /> 3) Nothing you said contradicts the idea of using Jurassic Park as an inspirational source for Genius anyway. Genius is not anti-science (I'm not sure if you meant to imply that or not. It's not anti-corporate either). The scientist characters trying to warn John Hammond is exactly how sane scientists would react to a Genius talking about their crazy schemes.<br /> <br /> Sadly this is true. I am planning to include art found around the net for Leviathan 2ED if I can get permission.<br /> <br /> Also, If you know any interested fan artists do send them my way.</div> </div> </div> </div>JP stIll isn't about mad science. Girl Genius is mad science. Dozens of Frankenstein movies have mad science. Jurassic Park is a perfectly good source for Genius, but that is becuase it is about Transgression, and paying the consequences of transgression. Mad science is doing the impossible. Transgression is &quot;so busy thinking about if you could, that you never thought if you should.&quot; The two definitely overlap, but they aren't the same.<br /> <br /> On the art front, there are some are sources you can buy the license to on DriveThru. I'd also suggest contacting the editors of Wayfinder, since the fanzine is free, I'm pretty sure that people donate their art, but I'm not 100%. You may be able to get some contacts that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T14:57:57-07:00","id":951326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=951318#post951318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Telling one of the writers of Changeling to consider Changeling? Ummm..... I think that Arcane is rather familar with that game, KingRaven.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, never heard of it.<br /> <br /> *snorts*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T15:10:16-07:00","id":951336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=951323#post951323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">JP stIll isn't about mad science. Girl Genius is mad science.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we're using different definitions and since definitions are fundamentally subjective there's no point debating whose definition is more correct.<br /> <br /> Can you accept &quot;any story using fantasty to convert the fear of a new idea that disrupts a safe status quo into a simpler safer idea&quot; as a valid definition of mad science (distinct from mad scientist, and distinct from definitions about the inventions created by mad scientists) even if it's not the one you personally use?<br /> <br /> <br /> We can definitely agree that Jurassic park has transgression as a theme; and that it makes a good source for genius.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 08-15-2016, 06:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T15:27:50-07:00","id":951343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=951299#post951299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll talk about this in the review, the problems of art and word count and other such things, but for now I am going to point out a case of &amp;quot;Be careful what you wish for.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> For years, I have dealt with Genius fans who have wanted Genius treated as though it were an actual game from White Wolf/Onyx Path, to count it among the canon-hell, it was actually listed in the canon list of games on TvTropes for a time, if you can believe it.<br /> <br /> I could review this game as a fangame and give it a bunch of slack-an okay game from the fans is quite frankly an excellent result in my eyes.<br /> <br /> Or I could give what those fans wanted all along, and treat Genius as though it were a professionally made game.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure it's worth doing this just treating it as a fangame anyways.<br /> <br /> Be careful what you wish for, and don't make promises you can't keep.</div> </div> </div> </div>A third option might be to treat it as a fan game that wants to be adopted into canon - acknowledging the limitations that being a fan game puts on it, while still being frank about where it would stand if it were to undergo professional development.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T15:33:12-07:00","id":951345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=951343#post951343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A third option might be to treat it as a fan game that wants to be adopted into canon - acknowledging the limitations that being a fan game puts on it, while still being frank about where it would stand if it were to undergo professional development.</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine the end result will end up like that, but I can't deny my starting point.<br /> <br /> Also, &quot;The Inspired really are good at statistics. &quot;<br /> <br /> This section is a <i>treasure</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T15:36:14-07:00","id":951347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=951336#post951336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think we're using different definitions and since definitions are fundamentally subjective there's no point debating whose definition is more correct.<br /> <br /> Can you accept &quot;any story using fantasty to convert the fear of a new idea that disrupts a safe status quo into a simpler safer idea&quot; as a valid definition of mad science (distinct from mad scientist, and distinct from definitions about the inventions created by mad scientists) even if it's not the one you personally use?<br /> <br /> <br /> We can definitely agree that Jurassic park has transgression as a theme; and that it makes a good source for genius.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find that definition difficult, because for that is historically close to what real science and philosophy are and as Genius loves to point out, Genius aren't real scientists. But you are likely right that we are using different definitions. Not much we can do there but agree to disagree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T16:26:30-07:00","id":951365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=951322#post951322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obviously. That's why I used it as an example.<br /> <br /> (Do let me know if I'm wrong when I say Changeling is about moving on after surviving abuse - I would have to reconsider a LOT)</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, you're wrong! *Cough* *cough* *averts eyes* *slowly walks away while twiddling thumbs and whistling*<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T17:09:08-07:00","id":951387,"title":"","content":"Just how long is each section of that book anyway?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T17:21:00-07:00","id":951394,"title":"","content":"Chapter 1 is about 30 pages, which I find surprising. I'll get back to you on the rest, unless someone beats me to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T18:33:17-07:00","id":951422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=951322#post951322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obviously. That's why I used it as an example.<br /> <br /> (Do let me know if I'm wrong when I say Changeling is about moving on after surviving abuse - I would have to reconsider a LOT)</div> </div> </div> </div>As a survivor, this is how I personally see the game, BUT--and this is important--I don't speak for all survivors. I speak for myself, so please don't use me to defend this point of view for all survivors always and forever.<br /> <br /> I will say that--a lot of you probably remember this--first edition had specific lines that spoke about <i>Changeling </i>as abuse recovery metaphors, with specific lines saying that, in many cases, confinement included literal and metaphorical sexual abuse. I think there was a line about the True Fae abducting human child brides. But I know David Hill has been specifically trying to move away from keeping that so overt in the new edition. It's THERE--to me--but I think he's trying to deemphasize it.<br /> <br /> That being said, me, Hayley, specifically, does see <i>Changeling </i>as being about abuse recovery, and it was really instrumental and cathartic in my own, real life recovery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":3093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","user":"hm8453a","date":". 08-15-2016, 09:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T18:54:16-07:00","id":951428,"title":"","content":"Changeling is very clearly about abuse recovery. It's the heart of the game, what makes it so utterly beautiful.<br /> <br /> And Dave's not shying away from it. He keeps his metaphors soft, but he's very definitely refocusing and lasering in on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T18:58:18-07:00","id":951432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=951428#post951428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Dave's not shying away from it. He keeps his metaphors soft, but he's very definitely refocusing and lasering in on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Softer metaphors. As in less overt, like I said =P.<br /> <br /> (And yeah, I'm sure y'all have had more conversations on it. We spoke about it some with the Dark Era.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T19:02:50-07:00","id":951435,"title":"","content":"Soft does not mean less overt-the game has it a much clearer theme. it means...<br /> <br /> I dunno what I mean at this point, I'm too busy cutting up Genius.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T19:09:49-07:00","id":951438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=951435#post951435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Soft does not mean less overt-the game has it a much clearer theme. it means...<br /> <br /> I dunno what I mean at this point, I'm too busy cutting up Genius.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then let's debate the exact proper wording for this other thing later. I'm eager for your next review section.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T19:40:41-07:00","id":951451,"title":"","content":"Speaking as someone who has not been a subject of abuse (sexual or otherwise), Changeling 1e only ever spoke to me on a theoretical level. I understood why it was a powerful message, and I appreciated the way it allowed me to empathize with others' experiences with such abuse, but it was always vaguely impersonal to me. I have, however, experienced trauma, particularly related to interpersonal relationships, and a great deal of what I have seen of Changeling 2e has spoken to me personally and deeply in a way that 1e never quite did. Take that as you will, but personally I think 2e has broadened its metaphor, without necessarily softening its edge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T20:30:22-07:00","id":951468,"title":"","content":"So, I've read up to the Catalysts, having been taking notes as I read alongside several breaks to walk. Or more. I'm stopping for the night.<br /> <br /> You might be curious how I'm responding to Genius so far.<br /> <br /> You know, honesty moment-While I came in expecting to dislike it, it must be noted I actually don't like hating things. It's tiring and stressful and not-fun. It's part of the reason why I, in fact, refrained from reading Genius and watching Sword Art Online and the various other things that I did not like but somehow ended up experiencing anyways. And as a general rule, even if I walk away from a thing hating it(and I often know what I will hate), I walk away with an appreciation for certain parts-I find things that I like, even if I dislike the experience as a whole.<br /> <br /> So, what's Genius doing for me, what do I think of it so far, without going into proper review material?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vsg-i0Gh2Eg\" data-code=\"vsg-i0Gh2Eg\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/vsg-i0Gh2Eg/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Part 1 of the Chapter 1 Review is not going to be fun. Here's hoping the game picks up from here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T22:56:39-07:00","id":951512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=951451#post951451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking as someone who has not been a subject of abuse (sexual or otherwise), Changeling 1e only ever spoke to me on a theoretical level. I understood why it was a powerful message, and I appreciated the way it allowed me to empathize with others' experiences with such abuse, but it was always vaguely impersonal to me. I have, however, experienced trauma, particularly related to interpersonal relationships, and a great deal of what I have seen of Changeling 2e has spoken to me personally and deeply in a way that 1e never quite did. Take that as you will, but personally I think 2e has broadened its metaphor, without necessarily softening its edge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. I'm in the same situation, except with physical trauma and the resulting PTS. Changeling 2e is something I can relate to in a way 1e never could.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T23:12:17-07:00","id":951516,"title":"","content":"I don't have anything more to add on the Changeling topic. Though it is cool to hear that 2E improves it's portrayal of it's themes that well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=951347#post951347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find that definition difficult, because for that is historically close to what real science and philosophy are and as Genius loves to point out, Genius aren't real scientists. But you are likely right that we are using different definitions. Not much we can do there but agree to disagree.</div> </div> </div> </div>Presumably you didn't mean that the definition of real science is close to &quot;any story using fantasty...&quot;?<br /> <br /> But while I'm waiting for you to clarify. I would say that the fact the definitions are close is a feature not a bug.<br /> <br /> While real and mad science aren't the same thing, the stories of mad science are often inspired by real science and the fears real science creates in people. Aside from the fact one is a methodology for research and one is a style of fictional stories there should be an intimacy between the two.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 08-16-2016, 02:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T00:03:47-07:00","id":951525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=951299#post951299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For years, I have dealt with Genius fans who have wanted Genius treated as though it were an actual game from White Wolf/Onyx Path, to count it among the canon-hell, it was actually listed in the canon list of games on TvTropes for a time, if you can believe it.<br /> (...)<br /> Or I could give what those fans wanted all along, and treat Genius as though it were a professionally made game.<br /> <br /> Be careful what you wish for, and don't make promises you can't keep.</div> </div> </div> </div>I inderstand this perfectly. A lot of years ago, created a vampire game (written in Spanish) called EDITED (I prefer not saying its name publicy to avoid potential flame wars).<br /> <br /> Its followers irrumped in a lot of boards like a troll invasion (literally) in order to promote their game. They presented it as fairly better and superior than Masquerade, telling shit about how bad was Masquerade compared to their game. They generated a lot of savage flamewars in different boards for weeks.<br /> <br /> I felt what are you feeling. I could criticize it as a new and modest game that was trying to find domeone interested on it: was not as bad, it was an interesting take that could attract new players into roleplaying, but it was too simplistic for my tastes, both in its setting and in its rules. It was just about 30 pages (one of its virtues because reading was booooring accirding to them). Not my taste but ut had some porential.<br /> <br /> But they presented their game as a masterpiece of vampirism, soooo superior to Masquerade (an horrible and muserable game comoaring to theirs). So we criticized it according their highest standards, and the almost unanymous opinion was that it was a big piece if trash.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T00:37:59-07:00","id":951533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=951516#post951516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Presumably you didn't mean that the definition of real science is close to &quot;any story using fantasty...&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not speaking for <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4433_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4433\" data-vbnamecard=\"4433\">Second Chances</a> but I found that qualifier a bit... meaningless. &quot;Using fantasy,&quot; seems to have to include any sort of departure from the modern body of scientific theory to be valid, which also makes it so broad to really have trouble narrowing the definition for the purpose of discussion.<br /> <br /> How does Frankenstein &quot;use fantasy?&quot; It certainly is science fiction, in that it has technology that doesn't exist (and we know would have never worked), but the explanation for his success in-universe wasn't some supernatural force/etc. In the universe of the original novel science could do that. Where's the &quot;fantasy&quot; in Jurassic Park? Again, as science fiction there are liberties taken with what could have been accomplished for the sake of allowing the story, but there's nothing one would classify as &quot;fantasy genre elements,&quot; involved. How about the Isle of Doctor Moreau for something we haven't brought up yet?<br /> <br /> As well, a lot of stories about &quot;mad science,&quot; are not the author trying to convert fear of scientific advancement into acceptance of new ideas. A lot of those stories are in fact the opposite. They are cautionary tales where even if the author isn't siding with the fear of scientific possibilities, they're at least taking a position of caution and skepticism. Most stories about mad science are about how someone has taken science too far (either because what they're trying to do is wrong period in the authors mind, or the author thinks that they're pushing to far too fast and need to be brought down for their hubris), and in the end people reject the ideas rather than accept them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T01:47:12-07:00","id":951558,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=951533#post951533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not speaking for <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4433_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4433\" data-vbnamecard=\"4433\">Second Chances</a> but I found that qualifier a bit... meaningless. &quot;Using fantasy,&quot; seems to have to include any sort of departure from the modern body of scientific theory to be valid, which also makes it so broad to really have trouble narrowing the definition for the purpose of discussion.</div> </div> </div> </div> &quot;fantasy&quot; is an extremely broad qualifier, you're right about that. The definition of fantasy is &quot;the faculty or activity of imagining impossible or improbable things.&quot; and that definitely includes something like imagining that it's scientifically possible to clone dinosaurs. (I didn't intend it as &quot;fantasy genera elements&quot;)<br /> <br /> Thinking more on it. I put that definition there because I can't think of any counter examples of a mad science story that didn't use fantasy. But now I think more, I don't see any reason why you couldn't create a mad science story with a strict adherence to real science. So if you were to remove that part of the definition it should be fine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=951533#post951533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As well, a lot of stories about &quot;mad science,&quot; are not the author trying to convert fear of scientific advancement into acceptance of new ideas. A lot of those stories are in fact the opposite.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, you misunderstood me here. I actually agree with what you're saying in this paragraph.<br /> <br /> When I say they're trying to make it safer I'm not saying they're trying to create an acceptance of the new ideas. I'm saying they appealing to people's need for comfort.<br /> <br /> When the plucky hero defeats the robot uprising the story isn't saying that robots will be awesome and the public should look forward to robots becoming common. Rather the story provides comfort to people who're scared that robots might, for example, take their jobs by translating that fear into something simple and visceral which the hero can defeat.<br /> <br /> <br /> So basically, we're in agreement: The authors of mad science stories are often siding with the fear of scientific possibilities or taking a position of caution and skepticism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T05:29:38-07:00","id":951618,"title":"","content":"The one thing this discussion has made me is sad that there's not more mad science in Promethean. For a game based on one of the earliest entries into to the Science Fiction genre as a whole? And the mother of the Mad Scientist trope? Sadly lacking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T06:29:38-07:00","id":951651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=951618#post951618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The one thing this discussion has made me is sad that there's not more mad science in Promethean. For a game based on one of the earliest entries into to the Science Fiction genre as a whole? And the mother of the Mad Scientist trope? Sadly lacking.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, Demiurges and Alchemests pretty much fill the mad scientist role for me, and in a way that isn't too cartoonish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T06:37:30-07:00","id":951661,"title":"","content":"Did Demiurges get mechanics in 2E? Low powered mad scientist is a niche that's definately needs filling and Demiurges are a good place to put them.<br /> <br /> (Sorry I know this is off topic)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T07:13:43-07:00","id":951681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=951533#post951533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not speaking for <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4433_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4433\" data-vbnamecard=\"4433\">Second Chances</a> but I found that qualifier a bit... meaningless. &quot;Using fantasy,&quot; seems to have to include any sort of departure from the modern body of scientific theory to be valid, which also makes it so broad to really have trouble narrowing the definition for the purpose of discussion.<br /> <br /> How does Frankenstein &quot;use fantasy?&quot; It certainly is science fiction, in that it has technology that doesn't exist (and we know would have never worked), but the explanation for his success in-universe wasn't some supernatural force/etc. In the universe of the original novel science could do that. Where's the &quot;fantasy&quot; in Jurassic Park? Again, as science fiction there are liberties taken with what could have been accomplished for the sake of allowing the story, but there's nothing one would classify as &quot;fantasy genre elements,&quot; involved. How about the Isle of Doctor Moreau for something we haven't brought up yet?</div> </div> </div> </div>So, we don't have to stick with the following definition, but the main distinction I've been exposed to academically (in undergrad, I was, for a while, a double major in history AND literature) is that science-fiction sets up Rules of the Universe that are moderately based in fact, while fantasy does not provide explanations. For example, in Through the Looking Glass, no one goes on a rant when Alice gains and loses body mass. We accept that it's fantasy and we keep reading. In sci-fi, there's an expectation for some grounding science, even if it's taken to a pseudo-science place, or somewhere speculative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T07:48:15-07:00","id":951705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=951618#post951618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The one thing this discussion has made me is sad that there's not more mad science in Promethean. For a game based on one of the earliest entries into to the Science Fiction genre as a whole? And the mother of the Mad Scientist trope? Sadly lacking.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's always hope for a section in a Storyteller's Guide or an entry in a Night Horrors book at least. Would fit in well enough with the hypothetical return of clones or the Zeka lineage.<br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\"><s>staying hopeful that the latter manage to come back there's still room for the precious glowy boom-zombie-babies</s></span><br /> <br /> - - - - - - -<br /> <br /> On topic... sounds like we can look forward to a fair amount of Arc Snark in the next part of the review.<br /> <br /> Following along skimming the first chapter-ish, and... mind if I chime in a little while we wait? Because I'm already getting weird, mixed feelings about this one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I've got a bit of a bad habit of extensively editing my posts after the fact. Please try and bear with me...<br /> In case you're comfortable being more friendly and casual about things, my name's Seren, or Es/Es for short. They/Them or Fae/Faer, please.","edited":{"userid":3946,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","user":"Sconce","date":".  missed a word 08-16-2016, 11:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","name":"Sconce","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T11:37:49-07:00","id":951874,"title":"","content":"Comment as you will.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T12:25:56-07:00","id":951917,"title":"","content":"I'm looking forward to this thread, if for no other reason than because I love reading your essay posts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T12:34:08-07:00","id":951923,"title":"","content":"Extra Credits has a good analysis of science in purely fictional settings. Basically Science Fiction is based on a technology that is demonstrably real (like television, just to give one example) and tries to create an alternative history or world where it possesses a capability that it lacks in the &quot;real world&quot; in order to explore the consequences of your television suddenly engaging you in a philosophical conversation regarding it's purpose in life, while future fantasy lacks a single technology that has sentience instead being granted to a unified thematic technology (a future fantasy based on communication = telephones, telegraphs, etc., based on travel = cars, planes, transportation, etc., based on military = weapons, armor, trenching tools, etc.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/885-bwgustaf","name":"bwgustaf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T13:13:19-07:00","id":951956,"title":"","content":"Ah, thanks for the clearance, Arc; didn't want to risk stepping on any toes. Fleshed some of my notes out real quick.<br /> <br /> - - - - - - - - - - -<br /> <br /> <br /> At the start, I'm getting a mixed sense of not just being an &quot;alternative&quot; to Awakening, but being almost a &quot;stealth parody&quot; of it, and all the while it seems like it's also trying to borrow from the quirk/horror tone from settings such as Deadlands (I've admittedly caught myself thinking of said setting's Junkers more than once while reading). Not sure how to feel about this atmosphere yet, aside from starting to understand comments about it possibly working better as a standalone setting; it honestly feels like it half-wants to do that anyhow, and at least for me it might &quot;sit&quot; more comfortably if it had from the start. Still, I'm crossing my fingers that that particular feeling changes before long.<br /> <br /> The statistics section and bits of the history section alike feel too rigid and... <i>certain</i> of aspects of the nature of Geniuses and history, for something (maybe) ostensibly in the same weird, generally-obscured world as the other Things That Go Bump. Even when taking the Genius mentality into account, concrete details like these feel out-of-place for something some have called for as an official Chronicles setting. Maybe that's partly the Ascension/WoD influence bleeding through, though... can't honestly say I'm familiar with what lurks in those particular shadows yet.<br /> <br /> A stray thought crossed my mind around the bottom of page 34 or so: the theme of impossibility not being a factor, the blatant defiance of reason and natural law, echoes not just mages, but something <i>else</i>. Between rejected theories that <i>just should not work, but do</i>, absurd connections and leaps of logic occurring frequently, loss of ability to work with regular, sound scientific methods as their very way of thinking shifts in impossible manners, the emphasis that the ideas seem to come from <i>somewhere else</i>... I'm honestly not sure which came first, and scouring search engines doesn't definitively reveal anything, but at points it feels almost like an incidental &quot;echo&quot; of The Nemesis Continuum from the Intruders book, or of abyssal intrusions in general. Granted, the infectiousness of impossible physics is swapped out for a contagious ability to <i>ignore</i> physics and an equally contagious inability to work meaningfully within those laws, but the parallels are there, probably unintentionally. Still, can't yet shake the feeling that an Awakened hearing of the Inspired condition might at least suspect ties to the Abyss in some fashion, unless they were close enough to scrutinize either the Genius or their works with Mage Sight and saw traces of something more mundane... or <i>weirder</i>. We'll see if this silly little idea holds up as the material goes on though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I've got a bit of a bad habit of extensively editing my posts after the fact. Please try and bear with me...<br /> In case you're comfortable being more friendly and casual about things, my name's Seren, or Es/Es for short. They/Them or Fae/Faer, please.","edited":{"userid":3946,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","user":"Sconce","date":". 08-16-2016, 04:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","name":"Sconce","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T13:48:33-07:00","id":951983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sconce</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=951956#post951956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even when taking the Genius mentality into account, concrete details like these feel out-of-place for something some have called for as an official Chronicles setting. Maybe that's partly the Ascension/WoD influence bleeding through, though... can't honestly say I'm familiar with what lurks in those particular shadows yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say it's mostly Ascension/cWoD influence bleeding through, though there is in-setting justification too.<br /> <br /> Wonders are really good at gathering info and their culture is <u>heavily</u> influenced by the Peerage's origins as a Zoroastrian philosophy cult that was founded to oppose historical revisionism. So they have a motive to publish and share that info with even the most inexperienced Genius.<br /> <br /> Still. if I had to guess I'd say it's mostly Ascension/cWoD infleunce.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T14:06:50-07:00","id":952004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=951558#post951558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &amp;quot;fantasy&amp;quot; is an extremely broad qualifier, you're right about that. The definition of fantasy is &amp;quot;the faculty or activity of imagining impossible or improbable things.&amp;quot; and that definitely includes something like imagining that it's scientifically possible to clone dinosaurs. (I didn't intend it as &amp;quot;fantasy genera elements&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Thinking more on it. I put that definition there because I can't think of any counter examples of a mad science story that didn't use fantasy. But now I think more, I don't see any reason why you couldn't create a mad science story with a strict adherence to real science. So if you were to remove that part of the definition it should be fine.<br /> <br /> Ah, you misunderstood me here. I actually agree with what you're saying in this paragraph.<br /> <br /> When I say they're trying to make it safer I'm not saying they're trying to create an acceptance of the new ideas. I'm saying they appealing to people's need for comfort.<br /> <br /> When the plucky hero defeats the robot uprising the story isn't saying that robots will be awesome and the public should look forward to robots becoming common. Rather the story provides comfort to people who're scared that robots might, for example, take their jobs by translating that fear into something simple and visceral which the hero can defeat..</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> pretty much nailed my feelings. I'll go one step further and say that scientific Bond Villains have always been kinda archetypal Mad Scientists for me. No fantasy, minimal Sci-Fi, still very mad. But that's me and it will probably be the last I have to add on this stream of thought (not the thread though). We clearly have different definitions, which is totally cool, and I don't want to spend the last of days of vacation debating it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T14:10:30-07:00","id":952010,"title":"","content":"What are we commenting on?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 08-16-2016, 05:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T14:14:18-07:00","id":952018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=952004#post952004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> pretty much nailed my feelings. I'll go one step further and say that scientific Bond Villains have always been kinda archetypal Mad Scientists for me. No fantasy, minimal Sci-Fi, still very mad. But that's me and it will probably be the last I have to add on this stream of thought (not the thread though). We clearly have different definitions, which is totally cool, and I don't want to spend the last of days of vacation debating it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd agree that scientific Bond Villains are mad scientists - as I said earlier I'm drawing a distinction between mad science as a genre of stories and mad scientists as a charachter archetype - so seeing a mad scientist charachter show up in a non mad science story is perfectly normal.<br /> <br /> And now we've both had our final word on this subthread I'll wish you an enjoyable end of vacation <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Save</span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T14:18:59-07:00","id":952022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=951983#post951983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say it's mostly Ascension/cWoD influence bleeding through, though there is in-setting justification too.<br /> <br /> Wonders are really good at gathering info and their culture is <u>heavily</u> influenced by the Peerage's origins as a Zoroastrian philosophy cult that was founded to oppose historical revisionism. So they have a motive to publish and share that info with even the most inexperienced Genius.<br /> <br /> Still. if I had to guess I'd say it's mostly Ascension/cWoD infleunce.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough (and something I'll need to note for when I do start reading through the Classic material). Still can't help but question the inclusion of over a full page's worth of fairly precise values in laying out the setting instead of a paragraph or two explaining roundabout figures or comparative terms, though. Seems a bit... mechanical, like it doesn't quite fit a flowing narrative. Maybe if the author had had some images on-hand and someone to lay the book out more like official WW/OP material, the numbers could've been slipped in on the likeness of a document or open book to drive home the atmosphere instead of feeling jarring and overly exposition-y. Buuut that'd be the limitations of a one-person project dropping in to say hi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I've got a bit of a bad habit of extensively editing my posts after the fact. Please try and bear with me...<br /> In case you're comfortable being more friendly and casual about things, my name's Seren, or Es/Es for short. They/Them or Fae/Faer, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","name":"Sconce","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T14:25:56-07:00","id":952026,"title":"","content":"Each to their own I guess. This is a game about scientists, if mad ones. Having statistics feels setting appropriate to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T15:06:12-07:00","id":952058,"title":"","content":"I like the statistics as fluff, but it does bother me a bit when I think about it. I find it strains credibility a bit to have that many Geniuses doing their thing and yet the masquerade has made it this far. I imagine most other supernatural populations are similar, but having the hard numbers out there makes it stick out more for me, if that makes sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8064-mp122984","name":"mp122984","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T15:29:05-07:00","id":952085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mp122984</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=952058#post952058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the statistics as fluff, but it does bother me a bit when I think about it. I find it strains credibility a bit to have that many Geniuses doing their thing and yet the masquerade has made it this far. I imagine most other supernatural populations are similar, but having the hard numbers out there makes it stick out more for me, if that makes sense.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It does call out though that most Genii never get off the ground. They lack funding, or just plain common sense, enough to never really amount to anything other than quacks. A Mage can resculpt reality with only their mind - a Genius actually needs to build something to be anything other than a delusional mortal (in most cases).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T17:03:12-07:00","id":952141,"title":"","content":"As someone who's crossover chronicle includes Genius material and whose had to make many tweaks to it to fit the setting I'm very intrigued. Reading Transgression for free back in 2010 was what got me to buy and read every core book in OWOD and NWOD, it opened my eyes to the possibilities of role playing and I'm thankful for that even if it is wonky. I was never exposed to its fan base but it doesn't really surprise me to hear that its defensive, fan projects are enormously difficult to get off the ground and they can develop a cultish and insular following around them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11643-corax","name":"Corax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T21:20:23-07:00","id":952272,"title":"","content":"The writing begins.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T22:35:32-07:00","id":952323,"title":"","content":"Inspired by this thread, I've started a new topic about how I'd handle <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/952302-mad-science\">Mad Science</a> in the ChroD. With that said, I'll return to my seat and await Arcane's next stage of the read-through.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T22:50:49-07:00","id":952329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mp122984</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=952058#post952058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the statistics as fluff, but it does bother me a bit when I think about it. I find it strains credibility a bit to have that many Geniuses doing their thing and yet the masquerade has made it this far. I imagine most other supernatural populations are similar, but having the hard numbers out there makes it stick out more for me, if that makes sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>WoD humans are not the same as real life humans.<br /> <br /> In real life the majority of people (at least in the USA) believe Ghosts are real despite Ghosts probably not existing. In the WoD the majority of people believe there is nothing supernatural despite having personally encountered the supernatural.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T23:25:15-07:00","id":952344,"title":"","content":"I will simply point out that the above assertion (that people in the Chronicles of Darkness don't believe in the supernatural) is not true. It was maybe true in the classic games, but it's never been true in the Chronicles. Everyone knows monsters exist, they just hope they'll go away.<br /> <br /> The difference is indicative of just one of Genius' many problems when it tries to be a nWoD/CofD game, but It's an important one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T23:34:54-07:00","id":952351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=952344#post952344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will simply point out that the above assertion (that people in the Chronicles of Darkness don't believe in the supernatural) is not true. It was maybe true in the classic games, but it's never been true in the Chronicles. Everyone knows monsters exist, they just hope they'll go away.<br /> <br /> The difference is indicative of just one of Genius' many problems when it tries to be a nWoD/CofD game, but It's an important one.</div> </div> </div> </div>And it runs <i>deep.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T23:45:52-07:00","id":952354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=952344#post952344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will simply point out that the above assertion (that people in the Chronicles of Darkness don't believe in the supernatural) is not true. It was maybe true in the classic games, but it's never been true in the Chronicles. Everyone knows monsters exist, they just hope they'll go away.<br /> <br /> The difference is indicative of just one of Genius' many problems when it tries to be a nWoD/CofD game, but It's an important one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really?<br /> <br /> When I read the question &quot;What has your character forgotten&quot; from the Breaking Points section of Chronicles of Darkness I read the word forgotten as implying that mortals outright suppressed memories of the supernatural rather than simply hoped they'd go away. And if that in turn implied that they didn't believe in monsters, why else would they be suppressing memories if not to protect disbelief?<br /> <br /> Still, no need to blame Genius for my misunderstanding. Genius doesn't actually say that mortals don't believe in mad science, just that exposing them to it causes trouble. The opposite actually, Hoffnungs are mentioned as often being aware of the Inspired before the Breakthrough.<br /> <br /> <br /> (It actually feels nice to be on this side of the argument <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> normally I'm the one saying mortals see and forget monsters while the people I'm talking too are saying that mortals never see monsters in the first place)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 08-17-2016, 02:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T00:05:56-07:00","id":952366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=952085#post952085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It does call out though that most Genii never get off the ground. They lack funding, or just plain common sense, enough to never really amount to anything other than quacks. A Mage can resculpt reality with only their mind - a Genius actually needs to build something to be anything other than a delusional mortal (in most cases).</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not just this though. Let's start with the Genius numbers.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Genius Pg. 38</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Estimates of the genius population before 1990 or so guessed that one person in a million was a genius, giving a total world genius population of a few thousand. That was wrong: once the Inspired got online, superior communication allowed for a revised estimate: there were, probably, at least a million geniuses out there, and many of them wanted to talk to one-another. The Internet was a revolution, and it continues to be so: there are now a million Inspired online (though many probably have no idea what they are), with estimates of the total genius population being anywhere from twice to ten times that.</div> </div> </div> </div>So (just doing crude estimates) that puts the Genius population at 1/3 per 1000 to 5/3 per 1,000 (If we round down to six billion). It might just be an idiosyncracy of mine, but when I hear those numbers can't help but apply that to other types of supernaturals. Vampires, werewolves, changelings, mages - Putting them at those numbers I have a hard time wrapping my head around either a setting where the supernatural hides from an unknowing mundane or one where the mundanes willingly hide the supernatural that they know from themselves. And Genius is on shakier grounds because 1) The mechanics Genius uses to keep Geniuses under a masquerade are iffy, being mostly societal as opposed to innate and 2) Most Geniuses by their very nature are not disposed to stay in the shadows. This might sound unfair to Genius, but let me put it this way; weird as it sounds, I'm okay with a setting that has two to ten million Geniuses. I'm a lot less okay with the setting saying <i>explicitly</i> that there are two to ten million Geniuses, because that invites me to start thinking too hard about that.<br /> <br /> I like a lot about Genius, but this has always been one of the things that bothered me about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8064-mp122984","name":"mp122984","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T00:14:46-07:00","id":952367,"title":"","content":"The statistics section of Genius Chapter 1 is one of the worst things I have ever read in an RPG book.<br /> <br /> There are some things you should not try to make concrete, for the consequences are more explosive than you imagine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T00:31:20-07:00","id":952372,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8064-mp122984\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8064\" data-vbnamecard=\"8064\">mp122984</a> I dug out an old email chain between Moochava and AlgaeNymph on this for you - and it appears that the numbers you're quoting are basically a bug. Moochava intended Geniuses to be less common. That's in addition to what Vent0 said. Also Geniuses are intended to be an usually populous group of supernaturals so I wouldn't apply the numbers to other groups directly.<br /> <br /> Here's the full email chain:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AlgaeNymph</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The high estimate for Inspired in the world (p.27) is 1:5000 (which is /a lot/, fanon population estimates for metanormals are ~1:50K-100K), but what are the typical and the low estimates?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moochava</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The typical estimate is around 1:15,000, while lowball drops down to 1:40,000. There are almost certainly more geniuses than other types of metanormals. However, many of these are lonesomes. Many of *those* in turn don't even have any Axioms; they just have a dot of Inspiration and ten points of Mania: they're intuitive code-breakers, gonzo hackers, car mechanics who can work miracles, and other people whose abilities are so close to baseline humans that they're even less strange, mechanically, than the psychics and cultists that inhabit the World of Darkness. Other lonesomes have figured out how to build a few wonders but don't really understand what Inspiration is or can do. They haven't read the &quot;game rules,&quot; basically. Geniuses who are as aware and experienced as the typical starter vampire are comparatively rarer.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AlgaeNymph</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Ooo, interesting. Percentage estimates?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moochava</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Up to 50% of the genius population are entirely unconnected. This number is dropping fast, though; probably by 1% per year--it's just an increasingly connected world. About half of these lonesomes, maybe a little less--according to estimates--are below starting PC genius level, mostly just people with a few tricks. Even among known geniuses, there's strong clustering on the lower end of the scale. The more unremarkable mad scientists will go their whole lives at Inspiration 1 or 2 and a few dots in one narrowly-focused Axiom, repeating the same experiments over and over. These pathological types aren't encountered too often because they aren't such great PCs, and they tend to sequester themselves, working alone or in small, tight groups of like-minded folks.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AlgaeNymph</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> A comment on genius population statistics -- according to p.32, <b>[Note, this is referring to the 1.0 pdf. It's the same text as the p38 bit you're referring too]</b> the genius/mortal ration is explicitly ~1:6707 at minimum. You may want to emphasize how most of them have only a dot of Inspiration, don't know what they are, and so forth.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moochava</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Yeah, I'll consider making the population statistics more explicit, though I really want to avoid anything that'll close off people's ideas of the games.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sadly that bit never got patched.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 08-17-2016, 03:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T00:40:42-07:00","id":952375,"title":"","content":"To put the issue into a bit of perspective:<br /> <br /> 10 million Genii, if they were their own country, would be around the ~90th by population (they're almost the population of Portugal!) depending on which list of recognized countries you use (keeping in mind that there are ~200 recognized sovereign nations on Earth, again with some variation depending on recognition status and such). If it was an independent religion it would fall between Judaism and Bahai in population. <br /> <br /> Obviously the idea is that they're not organized by a single location or a common ethnic/social structure like those, but that's the kind of numbers we're talking about here. The idea they're supposed to be unknown to most people just doesn't work at those levels.<br /> <br /> If it was a game that didn't bother with a &quot;hidden shadow world that most people don't recognize exists all around them,&quot; and just went with them being a thing? OK. Sure. 10 million works as large enough to be a thing most people know exists, but rare enough that you might not know one if there just aren't any near you, and a &quot;quiet&quot; one could blend in fairly easily without anything to explicitly single them out to normal people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T01:02:38-07:00","id":952380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=952375#post952375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">10 million works as large enough to be a thing most people know exists, but rare enough that you might not know one if there just aren't any near you, and a &quot;quiet&quot; one could blend in fairly easily without anything to explicitly single them out to normal people.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's probably what Genius should be going for.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T02:02:09-07:00","id":952394,"title":"","content":"I can see that. I'd probably respond better to the game if that was the case, but that also means it would be aimed at not being a game to slot into the default CofD as well, since the default CofD maintains the idea of things looking normal on the surface.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T02:06:15-07:00","id":952395,"title":"","content":"To me the quoted bit sounds similar to what DaveB said earlier, in your opinion what's the difference between the two?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T04:06:09-07:00","id":952418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=952354#post952354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really?<br /> <br /> When I read the question &quot;What has your character forgotten&quot; from the Breaking Points section of Chronicles of Darkness I read the word forgotten as implying that mortals outright suppressed memories of the supernatural rather than simply hoped they'd go away. And if that in turn implied that they didn't believe in monsters, why else would they be suppressing memories if not to protect disbelief?</div> </div> </div> </div> Every game has built in &quot;you will forget!&quot; measures. Quintessence, for instance. The mind-blurring effect of the Kiss. Lunacy. Angels of the God-Machine. And so on. Its not that people WANT to forget, its that they're forcefully made to forget. The occult is forcefully hidden from reality. And that's on top of supernaturals that go out of the way to debunk existing measures to make people doubt. (*cough*MIB*cough*)<br /> <br /> Then, there's also the Cthulhu-effect of Integrity. Exposure to the supernatural tends to be tramatic, unsurprising for a horror game. At best, the occult aspects of the game are neutral towards humanity, while a good chunk are actively harmful. Seeing a vampire chew on your best friends neck and covered in his blood? A werewolf taking on an inhuman form that strikes primordial fear in your heart? Fae that rip out the very strength of will from your soul? Humanity tends to be <i>prey</i> for most supernaturals. Suppressed memories tend to be a human reaction to spotting scary things.<br /> <br /> People are constantly exposed to the supernatural, and implicitly acknowledge it, but there's this nagging fear that happens. If you don't look directly at the scary thing, it won't look back, and you'll be safe. Open acknowledgement is not safe. Humans are not blind and dumb.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 08-17-2016, 07:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T07:28:29-07:00","id":952502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=952375#post952375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To put the issue into a bit of perspective:<br /> <br /> 10 million Genii, if they were their own country, would be around the ~90th by population (they're almost the population of Portugal!) depending on which list of recognized countries you use (keeping in mind that there are ~200 recognized sovereign nations on Earth, again with some variation depending on recognition status and such). If it was an independent religion it would fall between Judaism and Bahai in population.<br /> <br /> Obviously the idea is that they're not organized by a single location or a common ethnic/social structure like those, but that's the kind of numbers we're talking about here. The idea they're supposed to be unknown to most people just doesn't work at those levels.<br /> <br /> If it was a game that didn't bother with a &quot;hidden shadow world that most people don't recognize exists all around them,&quot; and just went with them being a thing? OK. Sure. 10 million works as large enough to be a thing most people know exists, but rare enough that you might not know one if there just aren't any near you, and a &quot;quiet&quot; one could blend in fairly easily without anything to explicitly single them out to normal people.</div> </div> </div> </div>And the &quot;50% of Genii are near-indistinguishable from every-day people&quot;? For most, it doesn't <i>matter</i> if they are a Genius if they don't do Genius things. Especially with a world of brain parasites, sentient rats, vampires, etc. Crazy Lou is <i>normal</i> until/unless he builds a death ray.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=952418#post952418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Every game has built in &quot;you will forget!&quot; measures. Quintessence, for instance. The mind-blurring effect of the Kiss. Lunacy. Angels of the God-Machine. And so on. Its not that people WANT to forget, its that they're forcefully made to forget. The occult is forcefully hidden from reality. And that's on top of supernaturals that go out of the way to debunk existing measures to make people doubt. (*cough*MIB*cough*)</div> </div> </div> </div>Geist doesn't. Changeling really doesn't either. With Genius, people either don't understand why something is impossible, they do and the Wonder starts falling apart as it &quot;should&quot;, or they turn Beholden/Inspired and the issue is moot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T08:11:24-07:00","id":952527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=952502#post952502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Geist doesn't. Changeling really doesn't either.</div> </div> </div> </div> Actually, they very much do. Changeling especially has powers of illusion and dreams that specifically hide the fae nature of things behind veils that people are mentally coerced to believe are actually mundane. The Mask directly works by twisting people's minds and senses. As for Geist? Well, to be honest, there's not much for them to forget - the overwhelming majority of innate SE abilities simply can't be seen by mundane people. Can't make people forget what they don't see to begin with.<br /> <br /> Either way, the point is that supernaturals are, by their very nature, hiding from casual scrutiny. That's why people forget - because there's not much for them to build on in their memories, and over time it gets distorted. Its the intent behind that Integrity question - what kind of supernatural event have you witnessed, but faded from your mind for various reasons? You've already encountered the supernatural, but didn't quite register right. What was it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 08-17-2016, 11:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T08:28:20-07:00","id":952537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=952527#post952527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Actually, they very much do. Changeling especially has powers of illusion and dreams that specifically hide the fae nature of things behind veils that people are mentally coerced to believe are actually mundane. The Mask directly works by twisting people's minds and senses. As for Geist? Well, to be honest, there's not much for them to forget - the overwhelming majority of innate SE abilities simply can't be seen by mundane people. Can't make people forget what they don't see to begin with.<br /> <br /> Either way, the point is that supernaturals are, by their very nature, hiding from casual scrutiny. That's why people forget - because there's not much for them to build on in their memories, and over time it gets distorted. Its the intent behind that Integrity question - what kind of supernatural event have you witnessed, but faded from your mind for various reasons? You've already encountered the supernatural, but didn't quite register right. What was it?</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Changelings</i>, yes. A guy calling out to fire or wind or lightning and it appearing, not so much. And as for Geist, sure you might not <i>see</i> the super-Ghost setting someone on fire, but spontaneous combustion, or someone detaching and reattaching their arms is noticeable.<br /> <br /> I <i>guess</i> people could just write it off as &quot;just a psychic&quot; but that presumes psychics are believed in. More likely is that Changelings hide themselves, and Sin-Eaters are rare. But this doesn't really contrast Genius all that much, since people can't see what makes a Genius different unless they actually make something the person knows is impossible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T10:16:22-07:00","id":952593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=952395#post952395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me the quoted bit sounds similar to what DaveB said earlier, in your opinion what's the difference between the two?</div> </div> </div> </div>Open acknowledgement vs. just trying to ignore the strange weird stuff so you don't get wrapped up in it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=952502#post952502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the &quot;50% of Genii are near-indistinguishable from every-day people&quot;? For most, it doesn't <i>matter</i> if they are a Genius if they don't do Genius things. Especially with a world of brain parasites, sentient rats, vampires, etc. Crazy Lou is <i>normal</i> until/unless he builds a death ray.</div> </div> </div> </div>Far more than 50% of Jews are indistinguishable from anyone else unless they do uniquely Jewish things in front of other people.... there's only ~15-16 million of us globally (and vastly concentrated in the USA and Israel), but Judaism is still part of the cultural landscape of many countries (even ones where pretty much zero Jews live any more).<br /> <br /> The existence of 5 million Genii that are powerful enough to stand out, would create an fear of &quot;Crazy Lou&quot; because who knows if he's the next death ray guy if he's acting a bit like the 50% of Genii that aren't so easily overlooked?<br /> <br /> And the game also says that thanks to the Internet the 50% of Genii that don't realize what they are (and thus don't know what they can really do, keeping them in this barely special state) is constantly shrinking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T10:28:41-07:00","id":952600,"title":"","content":"I haven't read the book in a while, but I vaguely remember a lot of the content being pretty ableist, to be honest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T10:38:00-07:00","id":952605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=952593#post952593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Open acknowledgement vs. just trying to ignore the strange weird stuff so you don't get wrapped up in it.</div> </div> </div> </div> Fair enough. I read your post as saying just trying to ignore...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=952593#post952593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Far more than 50% of Jews are indistinguishable from anyone else unless they do uniquely Jewish things in front of other people.... there's only ~15-16 million of us globally (and vastly concentrated in the USA and Israel), but Judaism is still part of the cultural landscape of many countries (even ones where pretty much zero Jews live any more).</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't think that's a fair comparason though.<br /> <br /> It's not the minority of Jews doing obviously Jewish things that give us such a disproportionate cultural impact. It's things like being in the right place at the right time to become a huge part of Hollywood and being targeted by various world leaders.<br /> <br /> A quick Wikipedia puts the Romani population at 2 to 20 million. Yet comparing their cultural impact to ours shows that it takes more than just raw numbers to distort the cultural landscape.<br /> <br /> <br /> So basically. We don't need the number of Geniuses, we need the number of Geniuses who're both willing and able to do something stupid like attack the city with a giant robot.<br /> <br /> In my opinion the ability to attack the city with giant robots or similar attention grabbing schemes is inversely proportional to willingness to do so. A Genius who's crazy is crazy enough to do something that stupid is probably too crazy to find a stable and very large source of income that they'll need to buy the tons of titanium, moon rocks, uranium, etc that they need to build a giant robot.<br /> <br /> <br /> Geniuses probably would have a bigger cultural impact than, say, Changelings. But I don't think it's unreasonably for them to be treated like other WoD monsters - people know they're out there and hope they'll leave them alone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=952600#post952600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't read the book in a while, but I vaguely remember a lot of the content being pretty ableist, to be honest.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never got that impression.<br /> <br /> (Cards on the table: Formally diagnosed with Aspergers and Dyslexia)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T11:35:36-07:00","id":952642,"title":"","content":"I think <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3093_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3093\" data-vbnamecard=\"3093\">hm8453a</a> is using &quot;ableist&quot; here to mean &quot;stigmatizing mental illness&quot;. This is the second time recently I've heard from a neuro atypical person that such stigmas don't strike them as a problem of ableism, and might even be harmful to conflate the two. I agree that the stigmatization of mental illness is a problem in a lot of RPG books (and part of the reason I have never cared to look into Genius), but it occurs to me that &quot;ableist&quot; might be a poor choice of words to describe that issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T12:02:27-07:00","id":952650,"title":"","content":"I also thought hm3458a was using &quot;ableist&quot; to mean &quot;stigmatizing mental illness&quot;. And like I said I never got the impression that Genius was stigmatizing mental illness.<br /> <br /> Quite the opposite really. Rather than stigmatizing mental illness it humanises it. It deconstructs mad scientists like Doctor Frankenstein and shows that they're not an Other that can or should be defeated, but a metaphor for fears inherent to human existence, fears that in the end we have to make peace with because making peace or living in perpetual fear are literally the only options.<br /> <br /> Moving past the metaphorical. The PC organisations promote a healthy attitude, encouraging Geniuses to find self-acceptance, manage their condition and support each other. I've got plenty of friends who're also nero-atypical and a couple of them have told me that the fact I can casually mention my Aspergers like it's not a big deal (I even have it on a t-shirt) was revelatory and helpful to them. Messages of self-acceptance are important.<br /> <br /> In addition the book presents a wide range of mad scientist characters, both heroic and monstrous, which shows that Geniuses are not defined by their madness.<br /> <br /> <br /> I mean, Moochava isn't the next great philosopher writing profound wisdom about the human Condition. I don't think Genius would qualify as reading material in a therapy session. But the messages it has are solid.<br /> <br /> <br /> (I do however think the term &quot;ableist&quot; is too accusatory due to the cultural context surrounding any word suffixed with -ist. Mental illness is a ridiculously broad and complex topic that's not fully understood by experienced professionals. Expecting the man on the street to understand fully is unreasonable and there's no need to make people defensive over it).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 08-17-2016, 03:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T12:06:41-07:00","id":952653,"title":"","content":"The ableism is-<br /> <br /> Look, disclosure, this book has been one hot mess so far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T12:45:50-07:00","id":952679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=952367#post952367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The statistics section of Genius Chapter 1 is one of the worst things I have ever read in an RPG book.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I've not been following Arc's quixotic ride into mad science too closely, but I did get a little curious and thumb through the setting chapter, and I fully endorse this statement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T12:47:12-07:00","id":952682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=952679#post952679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've not been following Arc's quixotic ride into mad science too closely, but I did get a little curious and thumb through the setting chapter, and I fully endorse this statement.</div> </div> </div> </div>You should see my notes on the section. It's pretty much solid screaming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T12:47:15-07:00","id":952683,"title":"","content":"And, I mean, if we need to put cards on the table, I am also disabled, both physically and mentally (some might have been able to deduce the latter from my experience with CSA), and I've also worked in mental health. In ED recovery, to be specific.<br /> <br /> Also, please call me Hayley, if you'd prefer.<br /> <br /> Also also I'm just going to let Sean cover how, for now, as I don't have the spoons to pick up the text again and defend the assertion.<br /> <br /> Also also also I DID mean ableist as in stigmatizing mental illness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":3093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","user":"hm8453a","date":". 08-17-2016, 03:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T13:03:43-07:00","id":952693,"title":"","content":"I might not be able to properly do it. There's just.....sooooooo......<i>much</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T13:04:49-07:00","id":952695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=952693#post952693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I might not be able to properly do it. There's just.....sooooooo......<i>much</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> New spoons every day. Let's see how I feel once you're done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T13:14:39-07:00","id":952703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=952605#post952605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not the minority of Jews doing obviously Jewish things that give us such a disproportionate cultural impact. It's things like being in the right place at the right time to become a huge part of Hollywood and being targeted by various world leaders.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's sort of where I'm going with this though. All of the millions of &quot;invisible Jews,&quot; are still impacted by the relatively small number of them that get associated with things like Hollywood or banking, to create very strong stereotypes around them. There are pernicious conspiracy theories about how Jews control the media and the banks... because a few Jews made it rich in those markets. That's just residual cultural bigotry at work. Jews don't have a small minority of people that can build kill-bots. Once Genii start doing big showy things, and it becomes clear that that's a thing, the &quot;invisible&quot; Genii are going to start feeling the effects of that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A quick Wikipedia puts the Romani population at 2 to 20 million. Yet comparing their cultural impact to ours shows that it takes more than just raw numbers to distort the cultural landscape. </div> </div> </div>That... feels like a fairly USA-centric bit of thinking. In Europe there's a still a huge problem with how the Romani people are treated, and a very nasty level of cultural bigotry is still very present. <br /> <br /> If the Romani are a fair comparison over the Jews... I think it still makes my point just fine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We don't need the number of Geniuses, we need the number of Geniuses who're both willing and able to do something stupid like attack the city with a giant robot. </div> </div> </div>Agreed. The point was always the setting numbers in stone isn't good, and looking at the implications of the numbers given was meant to illustrate why that's the case.<br /> <br /> -------<br /> <br /> As the person Charlaquin's mentioning about the whole ableism thing, I don't recall feeling it much when I read Genius a while ago. Though I think part of it is that Genius is a game about the Mad Scientist trope, and I don't really expect it to be an academic text on aneurotypical issues. It has to touch on &quot;madness&quot; because of the subject matter, so I'm predisposed to some artistic license with such things as long as they're not too problematic and serve the game well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T13:17:26-07:00","id":952705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=952693#post952693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I might not be able to properly do it. There's just.....sooooooo......<i>much</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can do it! You can suffer for our benefit!<br /> <br /> But in all reality, if you don't wanna slog through a game like this, you shouldn't on our account.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T13:32:02-07:00","id":952710,"title":"","content":"I'ma gonna do it. Someone has to say it.<br /> <br /> Besides, there's principles at work here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T13:45:52-07:00","id":952718,"title":"","content":"Much appreciated. You've got backup if you need help, too!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T14:08:24-07:00","id":952729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=952703#post952703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's sort of where I'm going with this though. All of the millions of &quot;invisible Jews,&quot; are still impacted by the relatively small number of them that get associated with things like Hollywood or banking, to create very strong stereotypes around them. There are pernicious conspiracy theories about how Jews control the media and the banks... because a few Jews made it rich in those markets. That's just residual cultural bigotry at work. Jews don't have a small minority of people that can build kill-bots. Once Genii start doing big showy things, and it becomes clear that that's a thing, the &quot;invisible&quot; Genii are going to start feeling the effects of that.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well sure.<br /> <br /> But the question remains. How much tension will the &quot;visible Geniuses&quot; bring upon the heads of the Genius community in comparason to how much tension lies upon other supernatural communities. And simply looking at the relative sizes of the populations can't tell us the answer.<br /> <br /> <br /> Geniuses are definately more populous than Mummies. But every last Mummy has a cult and cults have a habit of getting into trouble, and while not all Mummies have Utterances capable of mass destruction, the ones who do can use it without large amount of funds and a long career advancing in power. Are Mummies going to be causing more acts of large scale destruction than Geniuses? I have no clue.<br /> <br /> Vampires and Beasts both have universal need to feed upon mortals Geniuses don't. Does that mean Vampires and Beasts create more Tension than Geniuses? I don't know.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=952703#post952703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That... feels like a fairly USA-centric bit of thinking. In Europe there's a still a huge problem with how the Romani people are treated, and a very nasty level of cultural bigotry is still very present.</div> </div> </div> </div> I am European, brexit didn't change that.<br /> <br /> There is nasty bigotry with Romani but even over here Jews have had a far bigger cultural impact than Romani.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=952703#post952703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As the person Charlaquin's mentioning about the whole ableism thing, I don't recall feeling it much when I read Genius a while ago. Though I think part of it is that Genius is a game about the Mad Scientist trope, and I don't really expect it to be an academic text on aneurotypical issues. It has to touch on &quot;madness&quot; because of the subject matter, so I'm predisposed to some artistic license with such things as long as they're not too problematic and serve the game well.</div> </div> </div> </div>A good attitude to have <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T21:21:14-07:00","id":952971,"title":"","content":"Making good progress on this review. Hopefully it's coherent.<br /> <br /> By the way, Genius 2nd think-tank, if Chuubo's Marvelous Wish Granting Engine isn't listed as an inspiration, particularly in regards to Chuubo and that grand master of mad scientists who we should all aspire to be even though that's a terrible idea, Leonardo de Montreal, I'ma be pissed. Make it happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T00:49:02-07:00","id":953025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=952971#post952971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, Genius 2nd think-tank, if Chuubo's Marvelous Wish Granting Engine isn't listed as an inspiration, particularly in regards to Chuubo and that grand master of mad scientists who we should all aspire to be even though that's a terrible idea, Leonardo de Montreal, I'ma be pissed. Make it happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if you'd buy me a copy of Chuubo's <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T09:24:17-07:00","id":953234,"title":"","content":"I'm just gonna say, y'all, Sean's not even halfway done with chapter 1 and if he were being paid for what he's already written, he'd be paid a lot. Not enough, but a lot. More than three hundred dollars. And he's only halfway done with chapter 1, so all I'm saying is, even if you don't like what he's written, please try to actually engage with it, and not just wave it down, because he's spending a lot of time on this, and he could be doing paid contracts instead. Sean didn't ask me to say this, I'm just baffled by how much is already written.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T09:39:14-07:00","id":953244,"title":"","content":"<i>You're</i> baffled by how much I've written? Imagine how <i>I</i> feel!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T09:42:22-07:00","id":953247,"title":"","content":"IF YOU CONTINUE AT THIS PACE YOUR REVIEW MIGHT BE AS LONG AS THE BOOK","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T09:47:07-07:00","id":953249,"title":"","content":"I KNOW. I DON'T KNOW HOW IT HAPPENED.<br /> <br /> WHY ARE WE YELLING?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T09:51:24-07:00","id":953250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=953249#post953249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I KNOW. I DON'T KNOW HOW IT HAPPENED.<br /> <br /> WHY ARE WE YELLING?</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps topically, you are both going... mad?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T09:53:01-07:00","id":953252,"title":"","content":"It's a distinct possibility.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T10:10:53-07:00","id":953262,"title":"","content":"We're all a little mad here. #rabbithole","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T10:11:33-07:00","id":953263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=953234#post953234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm just gonna say, y'all, Sean's not even halfway done with chapter 1 and if he were being paid for what he's already written, he'd be paid a lot. Not enough, but a lot. More than three hundred dollars. And he's only halfway done with chapter 1, so all I'm saying is, even if you don't like what he's written, please try to actually engage with it, and not just wave it down, because he's spending a lot of time on this, and he could be doing paid contracts instead. Sean didn't ask me to say this, I'm just baffled by how much is already written.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait. People get paid for writing?<br /> <br /> Looks at his fanwork <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T10:16:03-07:00","id":953267,"title":"","content":"Speaking of ableism, please please pleeeeeease let's stop trivializing mental illness. Please. Mad is not a fun, neutral thing to call someone. Crazy is not a filler word.<br /> <br /> None of us is a bad person, and if it would be helpful for me to talk about the long-term forced sterilization and mass murder of the mentally and physically disabled, I can do that. You're not a bad person for using those words. I recognize they've entered the cultural consciousness as just words. I get you don't mean it badly. I get it. But as recently as this decade, there was been forced sterilization justified with these kinds of terms. I'm sorry I'm ranting, I'm sorry, I don't mean to be yelling, but this is so important, and we don't even think about it. Sometimes, I do it myself, I use words like &quot;crazy&quot; and &quot;mad&quot;. We all do it. I'm not calling you a bad person. But this is just the first step of what I'm talking about in the game.<br /> <br /> Again, I'm sorry for yelling at you, and for ranting, but this still affects people every single day. Please, please, please, try to be aware. One in five adults in the US has a mental illness. Let's not trivialize it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T10:18:53-07:00","id":953270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=953263#post953263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait. People get paid for writing?<br /> <br /> Looks at his fanwork <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh gosh. My baby, my favorite thing, what I write to make myself happy and when I don't have paid contracts, is a Star Wars fanfiction about institutional failure and gender roles in the Old Republic, the Empire, and the New Republic. Your art is valid, paid or not. You are valid. And your writing is good. If you write three words a day, you are improving more than someone who didn't write those three words. Your art is valid, and you are valid, no matter what.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T11:23:28-07:00","id":953311,"title":"","content":"I love writing. Even if my ideas are terrible, its cathartic to put words on paper and see characters come alive. I just love it when a character I made starts doing things I have no idea that they would do. Its a thing of beauty when they start surprising you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T11:42:48-07:00","id":953329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=953267#post953267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of ableism, please please pleeeeeease let's stop trivializing mental illness. Please. Mad is not a fun, neutral thing to call someone. Crazy is not a filler word.<br /> <br /> None of us is a bad person, and if it would be helpful for me to talk about the long-term forced sterilization and mass murder of the mentally and physically disabled, I can do that. You're not a bad person for using those words. I recognize they've entered the cultural consciousness as just words. I get you don't mean it badly. I get it. But as recently as this decade, there was been forced sterilization justified with these kinds of terms. I'm sorry I'm ranting, I'm sorry, I don't mean to be yelling, but this is so important, and we don't even think about it. Sometimes, I do it myself, I use words like &quot;crazy&quot; and &quot;mad&quot;. We all do it. I'm not calling you a bad person. But this is just the first step of what I'm talking about in the game.<br /> <br /> Again, I'm sorry for yelling at you, and for ranting, but this still affects people every single day. Please, please, please, try to be aware. One in five adults in the US has a mental illness. Let's not trivialize it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Genius isn't trivializisng mental illness any more than Vampire is trivialising abuse.<br /> <br /> It does use the words &quot;mad&quot; and &quot;crazy&quot;, but the English language being as it is, it would probably be impossible to create literature about mental illness without those two words. And it's important to encourage art about mental illness because art is one of humanity's most useful (if not the outright most useful) tools for creating empathy and understanding. And ultimately empathy and understanding is what's needed: I've seen friends (I'm far from the only person in my friend-circle who's neuro-atypical) loose their job and become depressed because their employer didn't understand and support them. (I'm lucky, I have great managers)<br /> <br /> And well, if I'm honest, I think that focusing on language is actually a step backwards. Out of all my friends the one's who've had it hardest are the ones who felt the need hide their mental illnesses rather than come out the closet. It took them seeing me and how casually I'd talk about my issues for them to even realise that you even <i>could</i> talk openly about mental health. That makes me think that what we need is just more people (real or fictional) being open. Ordinary people who can talk about their mental health, in all the imprecise and colloquial ways that ordinary people talk.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T11:48:05-07:00","id":953332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=953329#post953329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Genius isn't trivializisng mental illness any more than Vampire is trivialising abuse.<br /> <br /> It does use the words &quot;mad&quot; and &quot;crazy&quot;, but the English language being as it is, it would probably be impossible to create literature about mental illness without those two words. And it's important to encourage art about mental illness because art is one of humanity's most useful (if not the outright most useful) tools for creating empathy and understanding. And ultimately empathy and understanding is what's needed: I've seen friends (I'm far from the only person in my friend-circle who's neuro-atypical) loose their job and become depressed because their employer didn't understand and support them. (I'm lucky, I have great managers)<br /> <br /> And well, if I'm honest, I think that focusing on language is actually a step backwards. Out of all my friends the one's who've had it hardest are the ones who felt the need hide their mental illnesses rather than come out the closet. It took them seeing me and how casually I'd talk about my issues for them to even realise that you even <i>could</i> talk openly about mental health. That makes me think that what we need is just more people (real or fictional) being open. Ordinary people who can talk about their mental health, in all the imprecise and colloquial ways that ordinary people talk.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm just going to post this. It addresses all of your claims, including the ones that misrepresented my own. I will not address the logical failings of your claims--they're on the same page as people who say that people who talk about race keep racism alive. I don't have the spoons, but this article addresses far more than just words to avoid, it tells you why, and it addresses the arguments you've made:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.autistichoya.com/p/ableist-words-and-terms-to-avoid.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.autistichoya.com/p/ableis...-to-avoid.html</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T13:03:54-07:00","id":953369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=953329#post953329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Genius isn't trivializisng mental illness any more than Vampire is trivialising abuse.<br /> <br /> It does use the words &quot;mad&quot; and &quot;crazy&quot;, but the English language being as it is, it would probably be impossible to create literature about mental illness without those two words. And it's important to encourage art about mental illness because art is one of humanity's most useful (if not the outright most useful) tools for creating empathy and understanding. And ultimately empathy and understanding is what's needed: I've seen friends (I'm far from the only person in my friend-circle who's neuro-atypical) loose their job and become depressed because their employer didn't understand and support them. (I'm lucky, I have great managers)<br /> <br /> And well, if I'm honest, I think that focusing on language is actually a step backwards. Out of all my friends the one's who've had it hardest are the ones who felt the need hide their mental illnesses rather than come out the closet. It took them seeing me and how casually I'd talk about my issues for them to even realise that you even <i>could</i> talk openly about mental health. That makes me think that what we need is just more people (real or fictional) being open. Ordinary people who can talk about their mental health, in all the imprecise and colloquial ways that ordinary people talk.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not instead of saying &quot;Mad&quot; or &quot;Crazy&quot;, people just said &quot;sick&quot; or &quot;ill&quot;?<br /> <br /> And I'll believe the mad scientist trope isn't trivializisng mental illness the second my depression allows me to build a time machine. It trivializes it the same way the mainstream society demonizes the medication I need to take to function normally by claiming it saps away creativity and drive and turns me into a robot. Society punishes people for being mentally ill but it dangles the idea that suffering your illnesses builds character or gives you creativity that gives you worth. Jared Leto rode the &quot;playing joker makes you crazy&quot; myth that came into existence when Heath Ledger killed himself as a<i> marketing gimmick</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T13:15:36-07:00","id":953375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=953332#post953332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm just going to post this. It addresses all of your claims, including the ones that misrepresented my own. I will not address the logical failings of your claims--they're on the same page as people who say that people who talk about race keep racism alive. I don't have the spoons, but this article addresses far more than just words to avoid, it tells you why, and it addresses the arguments you've made:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.autistichoya.com/p/ableist-words-and-terms-to-avoid.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.autistichoya.com/p/ableis...-to-avoid.html</a></div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't find that link convincing, I didn't even feel that it addresses the points I was making let alone counters them.<br /> <br /> There's nothing in there about the distinction between different ways and contexts words can be used. There is certainly nothing in there talking about the trade-offs between demanding precision in language and gaining more representation, which was my key point.<br /> <br /> But I certainly don't appreciate your dismissivness. If you don't have the spoons that's fine, but my disabilities are no less (and no more) valid than yours and I have as much right to my life experiences and opinions as you do to yours. If you disagree or wish to take a break you can do so without comparing me to people who say that people who talk about race keep racism alive.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=953311#post953311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love writing. Even if my ideas are terrible, its cathartic to put words on paper and see characters come alive. I just love it when a character I made starts doing things I have no idea that they would do. Its a thing of beauty when they start surprising you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually prefer worldbuilding to writing characters.<br /> <br /> The fact worldbuilding comes far more naturally to me is probably a large part of that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T13:38:58-07:00","id":953398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TidyGamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=953369#post953369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why not instead of saying &quot;Mad&quot; or &quot;Crazy&quot;, people just said &quot;sick&quot; or &quot;ill&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Lacks precision/accuracy. Say &quot;sick scientist&quot; and people assume they have a pathogen.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TidyGamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=953369#post953369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I'll believe the mad scientist trope isn't trivializisng mental illness the second my depression allows me to build a time machine. It trivializes it the same way the mainstream society demonizes the medication I need to take to function normally by claiming it saps away creativity and drive and turns me into a robot. Society punishes people for being mentally ill but it dangles the idea that suffering your illnesses builds character or gives you creativity that gives you worth. Jared Leto rode the &quot;playing joker makes you crazy&quot; myth that came into existence when Heath Ledger killed himself as a<i> marketing gimmick</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not seeing the logic here. Does Changeling trivialize abuse or abduction? It features it, and those subjected to it gain &quot;powers&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 08-18-2016, 04:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T13:43:11-07:00","id":953403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=953375#post953375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I didn't find that link convincing, I didn't even feel that it addresses the points I was making let alone counters them.<br /> <br /> There's nothing in there about the distinction between different ways and contexts words can be used. There is certainly nothing in there talking about the trade-offs between demanding precision in language and gaining more representation, which was my key point.<br /> <br /> But I certainly don't appreciate your dismissivness. If you don't have the spoons that's fine, but my disabilities are no less (and no more) valid than yours and I have as much right to my life experiences and opinions as you do to yours. If you disagree or wish to take a break you can do so without comparing me to people who say that people who talk about race keep racism alive.</div> </div> </div> </div>I apologize for saying that. What I meant to do is irrelevant, and I don't think you're like those people. I think the claims are similar claims, and it is my fault that I wasn't clear enough in how I framed my statement.<br /> <br /> Your experiences are yours, and I have said throughout this thread that I know not everyone with a disability agrees with me, and that those disagreements are completely legitimate. I've given caveats throughout this thread that my experiences and opinions are mine, and that I don't speak for anyone else. I don't see where I devalued your experience and propped up mine, but you are upset, so what I think I did is irrelevant--your feelings are valid, and I am sorry that I hurt you.<br /> <br /> I do have thoughts on trade-offs in the name of representation (namely that representation is not inherently positive), but first I want to make sure that you are all right.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T13:44:55-07:00","id":953407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=953398#post953398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not seeing the logic here. Does Changeling trivialize abuse or abduction? It features it, and those subjected too it gain &quot;powers&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>And society also dangles the idea that abduction gives power. E.G. Starlord from Guardians of the Galaxy who's abduction from a loving family and upbringing by ruthless pirates made him into an awesome swashbuckling space rogue.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=953403#post953403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do have thoughts on trade-offs in the name of representation (namely that representation is not inherently positive), but first I want to make sure that you are all right.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm fine. A bit offended but forum posts aren't going to actually hurt me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 08-18-2016, 05:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T14:03:57-07:00","id":953416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=953398#post953398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lacks precision/accuracy. Say &quot;sick scientist&quot; and people assume they have a pathogen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Saying that someone who is <i>mentally ill</i> is &quot;sick&quot; or &quot;ill&quot; (both things that they actually ARE) somehow lacks precision compared to calling them vague things like &quot;Mad&quot; and &quot;Crazy&quot; that are shorthand for &quot;not normal&quot;?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not seeing the logic here. Does Changeling trivialize abuse or abduction? It features it, and those subjected too it gain &quot;powers&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Changeling is about abuse victims, yes, but these abuse victims have escaped it and are drawing strength from their recovery (sometimes this strength comes in the form of magic powers). The characters who have the opinion that being tied to their abusers is a good thing and they should go back to arcadia are antagonists. The mortals who see all the magical powers and ignore the cost are antagonists. Every Changeling is a victim, but it doesn't glorify victimhood.<br /> <br /> Mad Science, conversely, glorifies mental illness by associating it with getting magical powers that normal people can't understand. It says that a major component to being creative is being mentally ill and you are betraying something special if you try to stabilize yourself while also punishing people who don't because the normals can't understand them and react with fear to their creations (but don't worry, after they kill you and destroy your work, they'll feel bad if there's a moral to the story).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T14:17:52-07:00","id":953421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TidyGamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=953416#post953416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and you are betraying something special if you try to stabilize yourself</div> </div> </div> </div> The Geniuses who try and stabalise themselves as much as possible at the protagonists. The Geniuses who glorify their Inspiration are antagonists.<br /> <br /> Genius is doing the same thing as Changeling.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TidyGamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=953416#post953416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> while also punishing people who don't because the normals can't understand them and react with fear to their creations</div> </div> </div> </div>In Genius there's no rule that normal people have to react with fear and while they cannot understand how a Wonder works that's because nobody understands how a Wonder works, not even the Genius who built it.<br /> <br /> Genius outright says there's nothing wrong with telling your mortal family that you're a mad scientist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 08-18-2016, 05:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T14:21:15-07:00","id":953422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=953263#post953263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait. People get paid for writing?<br /> <br /> Looks at his fanwork <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well I'd definitely consider supporting a version of the Genius review once it's complete. I really like Genius, so seeing where it falls flat will be really informative.<br /> <br /> I'd like to say I'd support Princess the same way if I could but to be honest I'd probably be supporting the Vocation version.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8064-mp122984","name":"mp122984","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T15:29:15-07:00","id":953448,"title":"","content":"Alms for the poor are accepted.<br /> <br /> And if Genius isn't ableist, then why is the one word that sums up all it's ideas about insanity &quot;cliche&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T19:35:52-07:00","id":953587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TidyGamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=953416#post953416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Saying that someone who is <i>mentally ill</i> is &quot;sick&quot; or &quot;ill&quot; (both things that they actually ARE) somehow lacks precision compared to calling them vague things like &quot;Mad&quot; and &quot;Crazy&quot; that are shorthand for &quot;not normal&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Mad/Crazy is exclusively related to mental, while Ill/Sick encompasses both mental and physical ailments. Mentally Ill Scientist would have been more accurate, but it's also longer and doesn't have as much traction as Mad Scientist.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TidyGamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=953416#post953416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changeling is about abuse victims, yes, but these abuse victims have escaped it and are drawing strength from their recovery (sometimes this strength comes in the form of magic powers). The characters who have the opinion that being tied to their abusers is a good thing and they should go back to arcadia are antagonists. The mortals who see all the magical powers and ignore the cost are antagonists. Every Changeling is a victim, but it doesn't glorify victimhood.<br /> <br /> Mad Science, conversely, glorifies mental illness by associating it with getting magical powers that normal people can't understand. It says that a major component to being creative is being mentally ill and you are betraying something special if you try to stabilize yourself while also punishing people who don't because the normals can't understand them and react with fear to their creations (but don't worry, after they kill you and destroy your work, they'll feel bad if there's a moral to the story).</div> </div> </div> </div>Except, Genii don't get powers by being crazy, they get powers that <i>make</i> them crazy. You could have the same mental issues as a Genius, but they've got Inspiration and can do things that you still can't. It's pretty much a similar thing as what's been said about Pyros - working with it isn't conductive to cognitive balance. But Genii <i>work through</i> that. It <i>isn't</i> all fun and shrink rays. For an actual scientist, <i>it sucks</i>. It might be similar to being an avid reader or author and acquiring Aphasia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 08-18-2016, 10:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T19:59:24-07:00","id":953602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=953421#post953421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The Geniuses who try and stabalise themselves as much as possible at the protagonists. The Geniuses who glorify their Inspiration are antagonists.<br /> <br /> Genius is doing the same thing as Changeling.<br /> <br /> In Genius there's no rule that normal people have to react with fear and while they cannot understand how a Wonder works that's because nobody understands how a Wonder works, not even the Genius who built it.<br /> <br /> Genius outright says there's nothing wrong with telling your mortal family that you're a mad scientist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are there any protagonist factions that bend their talents to curing themselves of their mental illnesses, even if that gets rid of their magical insight/powers? Or would removing a Genius' special-ness due to mental illness be considered a bad thing by protagonist factions?<br /> <br /> And don't mortals observing mad science in action run the risk of going insane themselves or becoming igors who risk death if they don't attach themselves to a mad scientist?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T20:14:55-07:00","id":953612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TidyGamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=953602#post953602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any protagonist factions that bend their talents to curing themselves of their mental illnesses, even if that gets rid of their magical insight/powers?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, Scholastics, at least (who knows how many Lonesomes). About the same success rate as Vampires (that is, none so far).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TidyGamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=953602#post953602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or would removing a Genius' special-ness due to mental illness be considered a bad thing by protagonist factions?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ha! That's a trade <i>most</i> would make (out of the Protagonist factions, at least). Remember again - it isn't the mental illness that makes them Inspired. That just comes unasked for with Inspiration.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TidyGamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=953602#post953602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And don't mortals observing mad science in action run the risk of going insane themselves or becoming igors who risk death if they don't attach themselves to a mad scientist?</div> </div> </div> </div>A regrettably valid worry. And why it is better to Tell but not Show, in this case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 08-18-2016, 11:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T01:34:23-07:00","id":953716,"title":"","content":"I feel like using the words sick or ill to dance around the issue of other words like &quot;mad&quot; or &quot;crazy&quot; is going against the spirit of the idea, if not the letter. I don't have an answer for the question of how to do it right, but I think the root of the problem has a lot to do with intention as well as the specifics of the language, and using coded language for it (much as we see in other domains) may ostensibly solve the short term problem but fails to address the long term one.<br /> <br /> This isn't to say to just keep using those words, I just mean it's probably good to meditate on whether the problem is for one to call a group of people &quot;crazy&quot; or if the negative implication of divergence in the use of language like sick or ill renders their usage not much better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T02:00:57-07:00","id":953722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TidyGamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=953602#post953602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any protagonist factions that bend their talents to curing themselves of their mental illnesses, even if that gets rid of their magical insight/powers? Or would removing a Genius' special-ness due to mental illness be considered a bad thing by protagonist factions?</div> </div> </div> </div> The protagonist factions would wouldn't consider a cure a bad thing because it removes &quot;special-ness&quot;, and are unified in their belief that a Genius should not think of themselves as having &quot;special-ness&quot; because that leads to hubris and tragedy.<br /> <br /> However the protagnoist factions think that a cure is impossible and thus they aren't looking for one. Though individual Geniuses in the Peerage are bound to try anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TidyGamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=953602#post953602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And don't mortals observing mad science in action run the risk of going insane themselves or becoming igors who risk death if they don't attach themselves to a mad scientist?</div> </div> </div> </div>The risk is actually small.<br /> <br /> Firstly you need to spend Mania equal to their Willpower, so simply demonstrating your cool jetpack won't do it. It takes either a rather large demonstration of mad science or prolonged exposure to mad science. One of the suggested modifiers for the roll to create a Beholden is <i>&quot;the subject has gone on some &quot;grand adventure&quot; with the genius&quot;</i>. That's an entire &quot;grand adventure&quot; before you even roll. It's not as simple as taking one look at the robot and becoming Beholden.<br /> <br /> Secondly a genius needs an Exceptional Success to turn an unwilling mortal into an Igor, and it's a tough dicepool to increase (Inspiration + Presence). On a regular Success, if the mortal doesn't want to be Beholden they just spend a point of Willpower to resist it. (As for why a person might want to be an Igor, just watch Doctor Who. With the exception of Rory Williams, River Song, and possibly Donna Noble all the Doctor's companions are Beholden)<br /> <br /> The Peerage encourages Geniuses to play it safe, because, well why would you take the risk? Telling your family is fine and can even encouraged because they'll keep you grounded. Letting them into the lab is discouraged.<br /> <br /> That said it is entirely possible for Geniuses and mortals to work together, for example it's mentioned that large Skafoi wonders often have specially built compartments for mortals to stay in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 08-19-2016, 05:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T23:04:02-07:00","id":954243,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=950279#post950279\">Part 1 of the Genius Opening Review is up.</a><br /> <br /> Hey guys, promise me that if you read through the entire thing, you'll do the same when I set up my Patreon for writing serials and light novels. You can read that mass, you can read masses of text that are, you know, not balls of anger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T01:42:12-07:00","id":954275,"title":"","content":"<u>On nihilism and the failure to be anything</u><br /> <br /> You have a very strict definition of how to do nihilism (a bit ironic isn't it?). \u201cyou have to establish the illusion for people to believe in first\u201d, then you tear down that illusion.<br /> <br /> You also say Genius doesn't ask any questions. Both statements are wrong.<br /> <br /> In Genius nihilism is the question, not the answer. \u201cYou live in a vast meaningless cosmos, what are you going to do about it?\u201d. Genius is so up-front about it's nihilism because it's a starting point, not an ending.<br /> <br /> So if you'll forgive me for being blunt. Your section &quot;But Arc, you don't get it-that's the point!&quot; didn't give me the impression you understood what the point was. The point wasn't \u201cthe world is nihilistic\u201d, it's \u201cwhat are you going to do about it\u201d?<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>On science fetishism</u><br /> <br /> There's two questions I want to answer here.<br /> <br /> 1) Why aren't Geniuses scientists?<br /> 2) Why do Geniuses act like scientists.<br /> <br /> If you de-construct the mad scientist as an idea it's not actually about science in the first place. The mad scientist trope represents the fear of new ideas that challenge the established order. There's nothing that says those ideas need to be scientific or technological in nature. Jesus Christ challenging the religious orthodoxy at the time provokes the same fears as modern artificial intelligences who challenge our ideas about what it means to be human.<br /> <br /> Moochava recognises that and allows you to have mad theologians, mad alchemists, mad playwrights, etc. A Genius can practice any field of study where scary new ideas are born. It doesn't have to be scientific. Heck Doctor Frankenstein himself was an alchemist, not a scientist.<br /> <br /> <br /> Secondly, why do they act like scientists. Simple: Because nihilism is the question. Geniuses live in a vast uncaring cosmos and, being human, they hate that. Thus they're drawn to and arise from fields that promise the power to explain and pronounce meaning on the cosmos. In modern times science is the hip new thing, but go back in history and Geniuses use predominantly occult or theological aesthetics.<br /> <br /> The self-aware Geniuses know it's just a comforting lie, the doomed believe they are actually practising the fields they claim to, and the best Geniuses rise above the need for comforting lies and make their peace with a nihilistic universe.<br /> <br /> <br /> The in character astehtics of the Inspired community is one of my favourite things. The history of the Inspired follows the history of the mad scientist character archetype. Just as the modern mad scientist is descended from the mad alchemist character archetype through Dr Frankenstein, modern mad scientist Geniuses are descended from mad alchemists, occultists, theologians, etc like the pre-ARPANET Scholastics, Oracles, Numinologists, and Dharmists.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>On Failure</u><br /> <br /> Why do anything if you know you're going to fail? Why do failures matter if the stakes are so low?<br /> <br /> Why, in real life, do I bother doing anything since I know I will eventually die and my Self will cease to exist and nothing that happens in my life will matter to me beyond that point. Why do I care about failure since death is inevitable and my failures will no longer matter to me after I'm gone?<br /> <br /> Why do anything? Why care about anything? Why not just lie down and wait for death?<br /> <br /> The complaints you have about Genius' views on failure are what make it so relevant and interesting to me. Answering the question of why do anything is the whole theme of Genius, it's also basically the biggest question I have about in my life.<br /> <br /> Also look at Rick and Morty<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Rick destroys the entire Earth and buggers of to an alternative dimension with no consequences for himself (and two episodes later Morty is recovered and giving a great speech about accepting nihilism to Summer). <br /> <br /> Despite that Rick is a deep, interesting and relatable character. What gives him stakes is not the potential consequences for his failure, but our hope for his development along the way.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And that's as far as I got. I'll read the rest later when I feel like it.<br /> <br /> But seriously, if you want to grock Genius you've got to grock the idea of nihilism as a starting point or question rather than nihilism as an answer.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T01:58:58-07:00","id":954278,"title":"","content":"Only made it up to the point of switching from Elephant 2 to Elephant 1, but I think you've hit the nail on the head about things that bother me with genius. Maybe when Ivwas using it, science fetishism didn't bother me as much. Now that I'm a science educator, it drives me nuts. I totally agree with the lack of questions too. The setting just kinda falls flat and feels... empty, at least at this point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T03:19:59-07:00","id":954291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=954243#post954243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=950279#post950279\">Part 1 of the Genius Opening Review is up.</a><br /> <br /> Hey guys, promise me that if you read through the entire thing, you'll do the same when I set up my Patreon for writing serials and light novels. You can read that mass, you can read masses of text that are, you know, not balls of anger.</div> </div> </div> </div>oh, but I like balls of anger! besides, it can't be that ba- OMG MY EYES! MY EYES! IT BURNS! oh, Arc, why did you did it to yourself?... <br /> <br /> (I'm still in the middle of it, but considering the huge amount of text I feel I must thank you for that effort, and that I promise you it was not in vain :P )","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T04:16:52-07:00","id":954301,"title":"","content":"So much babble. Sorry man, I tried to wade through your frothing rants about a poorly-written fan game, but I just can't. So much anger and babble. I think Genius has infected you.<br /> <br /> I've never read Genius (and never will), but I can't do the review either. My advice? Just stop before your whole brain turns to mush.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T04:33:55-07:00","id":954303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=954275#post954275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Genius nihilism is the question, not the answer. \u201cYou live in a vast meaningless cosmos, what are you going to do about it?\u201d. Genius is so up-front about it's nihilism because it's a starting point, not an ending.</div> </div> </div> </div>But as Arc spends plenty of time on, the question of, &quot;what are you going to do now?&quot; is smoke and mirrors because the book is already telling you that no matter how you answer it, you'll fail sufficiently that trying had no point.<br /> <br /> The question the book poses is not, &quot;You live in a vast meaningless cosmos, what are you going to do about it?&quot; but, &quot;You live in a vast meaningless cosmos, what are you going to do about it keeping in mind that all answers are equally stupid because none of them do anything that matters?&quot;<br /> <br /> It's a meaningless question given the rest of the context.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why do anything if you know you're going to fail? </div> </div> </div>Arc addressed this pretty fully... because failure of an action isn't failure of the whole.<br /> <br /> I have a marvelous streak in my (brief) scientific career: zero experiments that supported my hypotheses. In essence, they all failed. It's kind of frustrating even if I'm OK with it. Do I feel like a failure as a scientist? Nope. I showed that a species that's commonly used to estimate the health of specific biomes is not indicative of specific conditions (which is important, because you need to know what your tests can and can't tell you), and expanded two analytic techniques other people can use to do more science with even if what I was measuring the forced me to come up with new protocols didn't pan out.<br /> <br /> Others can learn from my failures (and I pretty much took experiments doomed to fail because I don't have a career riding on getting published with successful experiments to worry about), and even if they never know it was me, someone somewhere might discover something important because I cobbled together a different way of looking at things and told other people about it.<br /> <br /> That's legacy. That's meaning. That's why people do things, even if they know failure is the most likely result. That's why eventually dying doesn't matter, because contributions to the species and civilization outlast one lifetime. <br /> <br /> But that's the problem with Genius as described: failures can't leave a legacy, robbing them of any point.<br /> <br /> Regardless of what philosophic or scientific reasoning you want to explain human legacy building, it's something that's clearly part of our biological behaviors. We have a drive to create things that out last us. That drive pushes us even in the face of failure as long as there's a chance of success. No chance of success? No reason to bother.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also look at Rick and Morty </div> </div> </div>Eh? I don't really think your reasoning on Rick is accurate. What makes Rick a compelling character is his ultimate refutation of his own nihilism/fatalism/uncaring attitude as nothing more than a defense mechanism erected after seeing and experiencing too much. He cares - deeply - and is looking for a way to express it safely despite a lifetime of experience saying there is no safe way to do so. Yet he tries to with his grandkids, knowing how much it could just hurt him all over again. We don't need to hope for Rick to 'develop' we hope for him to find the emotional reward he's been denied for so long (often by his own purposeful doing).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But seriously, if you want to grock Genius you've got to grock the idea of nihilism as a starting point or question rather than nihilism as an answer. </div> </div> </div>I don't think Arc has any problems understanding this. His bile is for the games inability to sell this as a compelling question the game will actually explore when it basically is saying, &quot;here's a great question, now don't play with it because that's dumb.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T05:00:34-07:00","id":954308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=954303#post954303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But as Arc spends plenty of time on, the question of, &quot;what are you going to do now?&quot; is smoke and mirrors because the book is already telling you that no matter how you answer it, you'll fail sufficiently that trying had no point.<br /> <br /> The question the book poses is not, &quot;You live in a vast meaningless cosmos, what are you going to do about it?&quot; but, &quot;You live in a vast meaningless cosmos, what are you going to do about it keeping in mind that all answers are equally stupid because none of them do anything that matters?&quot;<br /> <br /> It's a meaningless question given the rest of the context.</div> </div> </div> </div> In the real world our attempts to have a meaingful effect on the cosmos are inherently doomed to failure. If we're lucky we can leave a legacy to fellow humans, but once we're dead and cease to exist; legacy or no leagacy will be exactly the same to us.<br /> <br /> Every choice we make, every stroke of misfortune or fortune, it's all <u>exactly</u> the same to us after we're dead.<br /> <br /> We still have to decide to get out of bed in the morning and decide to live despite that.<br /> <br /> A game which asks us to confront that inevitability isn't &quot;smoke and mirrors&quot; or wrong because it doesn't offer any way to defy that futility. There is no way to defy that futility, not in the real world and thus not in Genius.<br /> <br /> I suppose you can justifiably say that makes all the answers &quot;equally stupid&quot;, but you still have to choose one, and there's nothing wrong with making a game about making that choice and how you justify it to yourself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Morty</b>: On one of our adventures, Rick and I basically destroyed the whole world. So we bailed on that reality and we came to this one. Because in this one, the world wasn't destroyed. And in this one, we were dead. So we came here, a-an-an-and we buried ourselves and we took their place. And every morning, Summer, I eat breakfast 20 yards away from my own rotting <i>corpse</i>!<br /> <b>Summer</b>: So\u2026you're not my brother?<br /> <b>Morty</b>: I'm <i>better</i> than your brother. I'm a version of your brother you can trust when he says, &quot;Don't run.&quot; Nobody exists on purpose. Nobody belongs anywhere. Everybody's gonna die. <i>[beat]</i> \u2026Come watch TV? </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=954303#post954303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh? I don't really think your reasoning on Rick is accurate. What makes Rick a compelling character is his ultimate refutation of his own nihilism/fatalism/uncaring attitude as nothing more than a defense mechanism erected after seeing and experiencing too much. He cares - deeply - and is looking for a way to express it safely despite a lifetime of experience saying there is no safe way to do so. Yet he tries to with his grandkids, knowing how much it could just hurt him all over again. We don't need to hope for Rick to 'develop' we hope for him to find the emotional reward he's been denied for so long (often by his own purposeful doing).</div> </div> </div> </div> You're not wrong, but what you're saying actually agrees with Genius.<br /> <br /> We hope for rick to find that emotional reward. But at the same time, Ricks multiverse is still vast and uncaring. No matter what he achieves there will still be another parallel universe where he tried the exact same thing and failed. And so far all the victories we've cheered Rick on for, they've all been small. Connecting with his family.<br /> <br /> Ricks grand plans of rebellion against the galactic federation already failed. The council of Ricks became the kind meddlesome governing body it was originally supposed to be an alternative against. I doubt future seasons will change that.<br /> <br /> All this means Rick is basically the definition of a well done Genius charachter.<br /> <br /> In Genius your grand designs like overthrowing the galactic federation are doomed to failure. But a genius who accepts that and makes peace with it can still find an emotional reward in bonding with their family or playing tourist across all of time and space. Rick is a charachter who's accepted that grand plans are doomed to failure, and now we're cheering him on as he moves towards making peace with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 08-20-2016, 08:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T05:37:21-07:00","id":954314,"title":"","content":"Thank you for the review. I admit to being surprised over the vemon this subject engenders, but hopefully you feel a bit better now. Sorry that it kind of broke your mind a bit.<br /> <br /> Two quick comments that are only tangentally related to your review. First, could you tell me what anime that little &quot;Okay! This pisses me off!&quot; pic came from? It looks recognizable, but I can't place it for the life of me. <br /> <br /> And two, a note about mad scientists and wizards being antithesises of each other. That's kind of an idea that I find to be uncomfortable. Modern western culture does suggest that science, the arcane and the divine are all separate things. But, if we dig into the past a bit, or outside? There are no differences. They're all the same thing - priests-wizards who advanced human knowledge prior to the advent of the Scientific Process. Alchemists and herbalists who were labeled as dabblers of the occult. Ascension tapped into all three of those pillars, as well as attempting to tap into some from outside of Western Culture. These aren't antithetical of each other - they really are the same thing, and as much as I don't like a lot of Awakening, this is one part that I think they got right. Everything is blended together to the point of being indistinguishable. Artificial divides are artificial.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T05:39:51-07:00","id":954317,"title":"","content":"So <i><u><b>many</b></u></i> windmills...<br /> <br /> But to replies:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=954303#post954303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But as Arc spends plenty of time on, the question of, &quot;what are you going to do now?&quot; is smoke and mirrors because the book is already telling you that no matter how you answer it, you'll fail sufficiently that trying had no point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which isn't actually true... The Failure talked about is regarding the big, transcendent goals many Genii aspire to. Individual accomplishments are fully possible. And, as TKR stated, realizing that is an important growth step for a Genius. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=954303#post954303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The question the book poses is not, &quot;You live in a vast meaningless cosmos, what are you going to do about it?&quot; but, &quot;You live in a vast meaningless cosmos, what are you going to do about it keeping in mind that all answers are equally stupid because none of them do anything that matters?&quot;<br /> <br /> It's a meaningless question given the rest of the context.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not accurate, see above.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=954303#post954303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Arc addressed this pretty fully... because failure of an action isn't failure of the whole.<br /> <br /> I have a marvelous streak in my (brief) scientific career: zero experiments that supported my hypotheses. In essence, they all failed. It's kind of frustrating even if I'm OK with it. Do I feel like a failure as a scientist? Nope. I showed that a species that's commonly used to estimate the health of specific biomes is not indicative of specific conditions (which is important, because you need to know what your tests can and can't tell you), and expanded two analytic techniques other people can use to do more science with even if what I was measuring the forced me to come up with new protocols didn't pan out.<br /> <br /> Others can learn from my failures (and I pretty much took experiments doomed to fail because I don't have a career riding on getting published with successful experiments to worry about), and even if they never know it was me, someone somewhere might discover something important because I cobbled together a different way of looking at things and told other people about it.<br /> <br /> That's legacy. That's meaning. That's why people do things, even if they know failure is the most likely result. That's why eventually dying doesn't matter, because contributions to the species and civilization outlast one lifetime.</div> </div> </div> </div>And you've reached the same answer here. It also applies to Genius.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=954303#post954303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that's the problem with Genius as described: failures can't leave a legacy, robbing them of any point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except, thing like the Axioms exist. And Lemuria, and the Peerage. And Foundations. Etc. Genii leave <i>lots</i> of Legacies. And that's just to other Inspired. It is beyond scope to mention how all the individual lives were altered by plans, failed or successful. You aren't going to herald a new age of space exploration (the Failure), but you efforts to do so can shape lives and outcomes.<br /> <br /> If you want the inability to leave a lasting legacy, that's Leviathan.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T06:52:16-07:00","id":954351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=954314#post954314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Modern western culture does suggest that science, the arcane and the divine are all separate things. But, if we dig into the past a bit, or outside? There are no differences.</div> </div> </div> </div>A fact that Genius fully gets. Go back in history to the times when mortals saw less division between science, arcane and divine and you'll see the Inspired also blending the three. The modern dominance of &quot;mad science&quot; over alternative possibilities like occult studies and theology is fully acknowledged to be a purely cultural thing; with plenty of Geniuses who personally buck the trend or are actively challenging the culture.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T08:21:08-07:00","id":954392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=954243#post954243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=950279#post950279&quot;\">Part 1 of the Genius Opening Review is up.</a><br /> <br /> Hey guys, promise me that if you read through the entire thing, you'll do the same when I set up my Patreon for writing serials and light novels. You can read that mass, you can read masses of text that are, you know, not balls of anger.</div> </div> </div> </div>Holy crap, Arts. I read the whole thing and boy was it a ride. You confirmed all of my suspicions about Genius that made me think it wouldn't be for me, showed me even more reasons to hate it that I never would have imagined, and then <i>turned it around and got me hyped for the potential a Genius 2e has to be awesome</i>. I really hope you can do more of these in the future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 08-20-2016, 01:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T09:13:22-07:00","id":954429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=954351#post954351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A fact that Genius fully gets. Go back in history to the times when mortals saw less division between science, arcane and divine and you'll see the Inspired also blending the three. The modern dominance of &amp;quot;mad science&amp;quot; over alternative possibilities like occult studies and theology is fully acknowledged to be a purely cultural thing; with plenty of Geniuses who personally buck the trend or are actively challenging the culture.</div> </div> </div> </div> I disagree - <br /> Genius is nothing more than an attempt to make another Mage game with a focus on Victorian Sons of Ether. The game didn't &quot;get&quot; it, it copied Ascension while maintaining a hate-on for mages, actually exasperating the divide with things like Inspiration-real science being incompatible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T10:06:58-07:00","id":954462,"title":"","content":"By the way, for those of you who &quot;couldn't get through it&quot; or read part and plan to come back later. <b>Read the whole thing</b>. Or if you can't or won't read the whole thing, at least read the last section. But really, you should read the whole thing. If you stop half way through, you'll only see the hate, but there's more to this review than Sean ranting about how much he hates Genius. Rarely have I seen <i>such</i> a scathing review of a thing be so constructive, or so honest about the fact that it's just one person's biased opinion and should be taken as such.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T10:08:07-07:00","id":954463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=954392#post954392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Holy crap, Arts. I read the whole thing and boy was it a ride. You confirmed all of my suspicions about Genius that made me think it wouldn't be for me, showed me even more reasons to hate it that I never would have imagined, and then <i>turned it around and got me hyped for the potential a Genius 2e has to be awesome</i>. I really hope you can do more of these in the future.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that, ladies and gentlemen, is how you shit on a game if you need to.<br /> <br /> Again, I'm not crazy about mad scientists, but there is no reason Genius 2nd shouldn't be the coolest thing the fandom ever put out.<br /> <br /> Until Princess 2nd, anyways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T10:09:13-07:00","id":954464,"title":"","content":"There is a TL;DR section folks. At that point, I stop the ranting and just give a hits list of what I think could make the game awesome.<br /> <br /> I thought ahead!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T10:10:22-07:00","id":954465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=954301#post954301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So much babble. Sorry man, I tried to wade through your frothing rants about a poorly-written fan game, but I just can't. So much anger and babble. I think Genius has infected you.<br /> <br /> I've never read Genius (and never will), but I can't do the review either. My advice? Just stop before your whole brain turns to mush.</div> </div> </div> </div>Turns out not all reviews can be for all people too. Happens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T10:14:26-07:00","id":954468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=954314#post954314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you for the review. I admit to being surprised over the vemon this subject engenders, but hopefully you feel a bit better now. Sorry that it kind of broke your mind a bit.<br /> <br /> Two quick comments that are only tangentally related to your review. First, could you tell me what anime that little &quot;Okay! This pisses me off!&quot; pic came from? It looks recognizable, but I can't place it for the life of me.<br /> <br /> And two, a note about mad scientists and wizards being antithesises of each other. That's kind of an idea that I find to be uncomfortable. Modern western culture does suggest that science, the arcane and the divine are all separate things. But, if we dig into the past a bit, or outside? There are no differences. They're all the same thing - priests-wizards who advanced human knowledge prior to the advent of the Scientific Process. Alchemists and herbalists who were labeled as dabblers of the occult. Ascension tapped into all three of those pillars, as well as attempting to tap into some from outside of Western Culture. These aren't antithetical of each other - they really are the same thing, and as much as I don't like a lot of Awakening, this is one part that I think they got right. Everything is blended together to the point of being indistinguishable. Artificial divides are artificial.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Madoka Magica. Kyoko Sakura is best girl, but that's just, like, my opinion man.<br /> <br /> 2) It is true that the divides are artificial, but Genius wants it to be a point, and honestly, it's not a point I care to take away. Hell, I sort of used it a center point for the idea of the better world, whether it's usable or not.<br /> <br /> I mean, it doesn't have to, but then Genius runs the risk of relying too much on Mage-isms, and I'm fairly sure Genius fans are tired of the comparisons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T10:17:39-07:00","id":954471,"title":"","content":"Rick from Rick and Morty is not a nihilist, he's an anarchist, and in a way, that might make him the perfect scientist, mad or otherwise.<br /> <br /> There's a PBS Ideas Channel video on the subject, you should go look it up. EDIT: Or I can link it <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XZLN1PN3L4I\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 08-20-2016, 01:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T10:29:18-07:00","id":954478,"title":"","content":"To TKR's credit though, Morty does have a very nihilist response to some of the horrors of adventuring with Rick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T10:34:37-07:00","id":954481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=954478#post954478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To TKR's credit though, Morty does have a very nihilist response to some of the horrors of adventuring with Rick.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is true. But Morty is not the scientist of the two.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T10:57:31-07:00","id":954494,"title":"","content":"I have to digest the text more, but I read it and liked what I read.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=950279#post950279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Bind Them to Humanity.</b> Long before you get to the mechanics, you have to convince me that Geniuses need to be involved with humanity. it doesn't have to be &quot;OH MY GOD, I LOVE THEM&quot;, but there should be a distinct variety of feeling asides from disdain, from amusement to exasperation to love to fear to sorrow. But while you make Geniuses conflicted with Humanity, convince me there's a reason they don't abandon them. Love them or hate them, there has to be a reason Geniuses keep coming back instead of hopping on Asteroid M.</div> </div> </div> </div>This little bit got me thinking though. What if, looking back to your suggestions for <b>Make Inspiration the Divine Fire </b>and <b>Commit to Science </b>and <b>Break the World</b>, the game took the stance that Wonders are actual literal normal tech that functions according to an understanding of natural law that's a couple to a dozen degrees more comprehensive than what currently exists in the world. Only, the purpose of Inspiration is to <i>Inspire</i> and the split between the Antagonist and Protagonist factions is a ideological split on <i>how</i> that inspiration should take place. Antagonists take the stance that the best way to inspire the masses is to set themselves up as the masters of the world where they can control and shape how technology and science advance. They want to bottle and control inspiration to take it to undreamt of heights of possibility in a controlled manner. The protagonist factions take the stance that Inspiration inspires by it's very existence and that trying to control it will do more harm to human creativity than good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T11:23:24-07:00","id":954507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=954429#post954429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I disagree -<br /> Genius is nothing more than an attempt to make another Mage game with a focus on Victorian Sons of Ether.</div> </div> </div> </div>Factually untrue.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=954471#post954471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rick from Rick and Morty is not a nihilist, he's an anarchist</div> </div> </div> </div> I would argue that Morty's a true nihilist.<br /> <br /> Rick is an anarchist in his heart and a nihilist in his head. Deep down Rick still believes in the principles of anarchy, but he's aware that the universe is vast and uncaring, he's accepted that he wont be able to overthrow the Galactic Federation, and so he uses his nihilist-in-his-head to armour a very very scared emotional heart.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rick</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about the reality where Hitler cured cancer, Morty? The answer is: Don't think about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Morty's attitude is an example of what a Genius who completed their charachter development could be like. He enjoys the adventures, he enjoys the gadgets, he accepts that the universe is vast and uncaring, and he's at peace with it. <br /> <br /> Rick is an example of a Genius who denied that they were in a game about failure, and kept on denying it until it almost destroyed him, then when he was right on the brink he pulled back and tried to turn things around before it was too late thanks to a new touch stone.<br /> <br /> <br /> (On the subject of Genius 2E. Touchstones is something Genius needs, along with possibly another minor template that's an alternative to Beholden. Beholden represents Igor and most Doctor Who companions well, but Genius should also have something for the Mortys and Rory Williams.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=954481#post954481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is true. But Morty is not the scientist of the two.</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't stop Morty being a useful example of how a Genius could react to the nihilstic setting they find themselves in.<br /> <br /> That said, if you want Genius example rather than a Mortal-in-a-Genius-game I'd point you to The Doctor. I'm not sure if he fully qualifies as a nihilist, but his absolute refusal (and arguably fear) of holding any sort of power in favour of basically playing tourist across time and space is a great example of a Genius who's accepted that grand cosmic designs are a doomed and bad idea and does something emotionally fuiling instead.<br /> <br /> (As The Waters of Mars shows, the Doctor is one bad day from declaring himself a god and deciding to rearanage the timeline and the laws of time as he pleases. The writers make it clear that this is a bad idea)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=954471#post954471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a PBS Ideas Channel video on the subject, you should go look it up. EDIT: Or I can link it <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XZLN1PN3L4I\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>This should be interesting, I'll give it a watch.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=954463#post954463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Until Princess 2nd, anyways.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically Princess 2nd is already out. It came out around the time Vampire 2nd did.<br /> <br /> However unlike Genius or Leviathan Princess was in constant development up to the release of the GMC rules update pdf, so there was no years long break and return with fresh ideas, it was an incremental update.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T11:59:18-07:00","id":954526,"title":"","content":"So i read your TLDR and, well it wouldn't be Genius if you did that.<br /> <br /> Ultimately genius is a very personal game where the characters' learn that they're powerless before a vast cosmos and make peace with that fact. Or they fail to learn that lesson and suffer the consequences.<br /> <br /> Your TLDR made it sound like a game of scientific heroes who tie Chuthulu up in chains formed of newly created scientific laws, before blasting him, then publishing a cure for cancer on the flight home.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that's a bad game. Heck you'd arguably get something very similar if you took the Marduk Society I wrote for Leviathan and made a whole game about them. I'd probably play it.<br /> <br /> I'm just saying that's not Genius and a Genius 2E should be an even better portrayal of the origonal themes rather than their opposite.<br /> <br /> <br /> P.S. Genius can and do Break the World. Take Karl Marx (not Inspired, but a great example), he's a failure in the sense that he never built that worker's paradise. But he broke the world by accidentally fathering a Stalinist dystopia.<br /> <br /> P.S.2. Genius' history is basically a retelling of the history of scientific methodology from Hasan Ibn al-Haytham to somewhere between Victorians and 1960 world. In the real world that history does focus on the middle east and Europe; but at the same time, I like how it's based on the real world. Rather than redo the entire history I'd just add a few Dark Eras and a city book or two set outside the Anglosphere. I'd definitely like one set in pre-European contact Polynesia focusing on shipbuilding and exploring Bardos (there's a really cool Maoi shipbuilder in the sample Antagonists). <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Save</span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 08-20-2016, 03:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T12:26:44-07:00","id":954542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=954526#post954526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So i read your TLDR and, well it wouldn't be Genius if you did that.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is pretty much the response I expected to Arc's suggestions from Genius fans, and to be honest... Yeah. You're right, I don't like Genius, and the changes that would &quot;fix&quot; Genius for me would make it not Genius anymore. I've been on the opposite side of this argument about other games (most notably Promethean), and I'll stand by what I've said in those discussions. If my problem with Genius is that I disagree with such fundamental aspects of the game, then the most logical solution is to play a different game. That's fair, and I'll gladly accept that Genius is not the game for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T12:36:37-07:00","id":954548,"title":"","content":"Well, yeah. Of course it wouldn't be a nonsensical, offensive, cheap self-congratulatory inspiration porn piece.<br /> <br /> I fail to see the problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T12:37:08-07:00","id":954549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=954462#post954462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, for those of you who &quot;couldn't get through it&quot; or read part and plan to come back later. <b>Read the whole thing</b>. Or if you can't or won't read the whole thing, at least read the last section. But really, you should read the whole thing. If you stop half way through, you'll only see the hate, but there's more to this review than Sean ranting about how much he hates Genius. Rarely have I seen <i>such</i> a scathing review of a thing be so constructive, or so honest about the fact that it's just one person's biased opinion and should be taken as such.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally. I'm still wavering on the whole thing, partLy because of time, but I made sure to read the tl;dr. Super constructive, super helpful, and may just help me improve my own writing. It alone is worth the price of admission.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TidyGamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=954494#post954494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to digest the text more, but I read it and liked what I read.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This little bit got me thinking though. What if, looking back to your suggestions for <b>Make Inspiration the Divine Fire </b>and <b>Commit to Science </b>and <b>Break the World</b>, the game took the stance that Wonders are actual literal normal tech that functions according to an understanding of natural law that's a couple to a dozen degrees more comprehensive than what currently exists in the world. Only, the purpose of Inspiration is to <i>Inspire</i> and the split between the Antagonist and Protagonist factions is a ideological split on <i>how</i> that inspiration should take place. Antagonists take the stance that the best way to inspire the masses is to set themselves up as the masters of the world where they can control and shape how technology and science advance. They want to bottle and control inspiration to take it to undreamt of heights of possibility in a controlled manner. The protagonist factions take the stance that Inspiration inspires by it's very existence and that trying to control it will do more harm to human creativity than good.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would totally love this as a game. Although maybe I could use Heirs to Hell to do something similar \ud83e\udd14","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":4433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","user":"Second Chances","date":". 08-20-2016, 03:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T12:47:20-07:00","id":954556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TidyGamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=954494#post954494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to digest the text more, but I read it and liked what I read.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This little bit got me thinking though. What if, looking back to your suggestions for <b>Make Inspiration the Divine Fire </b>and <b>Commit to Science </b>and <b>Break the World</b>, the game took the stance that Wonders are actual literal normal tech that functions according to an understanding of natural law that's a couple to a dozen degrees more comprehensive than what currently exists in the world. Only, the purpose of Inspiration is to <i>Inspire</i> and the split between the Antagonist and Protagonist factions is a ideological split on <i>how</i> that inspiration should take place. Antagonists take the stance that the best way to inspire the masses is to set themselves up as the masters of the world where they can control and shape how technology and science advance. They want to bottle and control inspiration to take it to undreamt of heights of possibility in a controlled manner. The protagonist factions take the stance that Inspiration inspires by it's very existence and that trying to control it will do more harm to human creativity than good.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would play that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T12:54:04-07:00","id":954560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=954463#post954463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that, ladies and gentlemen, is how you shit on a game if you need to.<br /> <br /> Again, I'm not crazy about mad scientists, but there is no reason Genius 2nd shouldn't be the coolest thing the fandom ever put out.<br /> <br /> Until Princess 2nd, anyways.</div> </div> </div> </div>After all that I'm almost afraid to ask for your opinion of Princess the Hopeful.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T13:03:20-07:00","id":954562,"title":"","content":"Ok, in general, I think there's a bit of forgetting that the review is only over the introduction/first chapter. Whether or not Genius &quot;gets&quot; thins by the end of the book doesn't matter to the current critiques, if it fails to communicate &quot;getting&quot; it where it is supposed to communicate that it gets it. My response, and this response, are about the failings communicated in Arc's review about one chapter, counter-arguments that don't actually stem from things communicated in the chapter miss the point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=954317#post954317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which isn't actually true... The Failure talked about is regarding the big, transcendent goals many Genii aspire to. Individual accomplishments are fully possible. And, as TKR stated, realizing that is an important growth step for a Genius.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, Genius is a game about realizing you can tie your own shoe laces without needing a machine that runs on rare crystals that cost a small fortune and only last for a few days if you're lucky.<br /> <br /> Again, the issue is stakes and meaning. You can fail and succeed at inconsequential things. Things that matter? Those you fail at. Not just grand things either. Science fails around you. You fail at just having money to fund doing what you're trying to do even if it would be profitable if not for Inspiration.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not accurate, see above. </div> </div> </div>&quot;You're wrong because I said so,&quot; is not a compelling argument to make people want to reevaluate their impression of something.<br /> <br /> If you care about people finding that any negatives in Genius are outweighed by the positives, focus on demonstrating where the game does things right.<br /> <br /> As it is, it feels like this is already heading into the annoying place that has been well discussed where reactive defense of the game trumps actually engaging with what people are trying to say.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And you've reached the same answer here. It also applies to Genius. </div> </div> </div>How? Genius tells me that if I were a Genius all of that work I did would have been a complete waste because my experiments would have been inherently skewed by Inspiration to the point where none of my failed hypotheses could have generated actual science for others to build on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you want the inability to leave a lasting legacy... </div> </div> </div>Not in the way you're twisting my words no.<br /> <br /> I bring up legacy as an example to refute of the &quot;nihilism is the question the game explores answers to,&quot; claim. The larger point is the meaningless of success and failure when steaks are removed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=954308#post954308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> In the real world our attempts to have a meaingful effect on the cosmos are inherently doomed to failure. If we're lucky we can leave a legacy to fellow humans, but once we're dead and cease to exist; legacy or no leagacy will be exactly the same to us.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm neither a nihilist or a fatalist. Even if I were, I'd be rather annoyed at the idea that you're asserting philosophic positions as facts.<br /> <br /> You're not going to get anywhere with me if I have to accept nihilism as truth in my life to see why Genius is awesome.<br /> <br /> I'm a biologist, and it heavily informs my opinions of certain things. One of those things is the philosophy of individualism. The idea that what matters is the individual human bucks the essentials of the biological imperative. We are not individuals. We are not islands floating on a sea as other islands float past us. We are a species; connected on a fundamental and essential level. Not even in some spiritual sense. Just in a basic biological compulsive sense. The idea that the individual is somehow special is silly from this perspective. Of course we die and after we're dead we have no additional impact on those still alive. But the impact we had in life matters because our role while alive in the species matters; it's what we're genetically programed to do.<br /> <br /> So I don't care about when I'm dead. Maybe I completely cease to exist and get to have no appreciation of anything. Maybe spiritualism is right and I can get to see how I did in hindsight. In the meantime, how I contribute to the species is ultimately more important because it's what matters; not whether I get to muse about it after I die.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A game which asks us to confront that inevitability isn't &quot;smoke and mirrors&quot; or wrong because it doesn't offer any way to defy that futility. </div> </div> </div>Where does the game ask us to actually confront that inevitability? Because the game doesn't do so in the first chapter. It basically sets forth two end states: acceptance and delusion. There's no struggle, no narrative conflict, and thus not confrontation. We're not challenged with inevitability, we're told the correct answer is just accept it and move on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...and there's nothing wrong with making a game about making that choice and how you justify it to yourself. </div> </div> </div>Nope. That doesn't mean this game does it correctly though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You're not wrong, but what you're saying actually agrees with Genius. </div> </div> </div>Where does Genius say this?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All this means Rick is basically the definition of a well done Genius charachter. </div> </div> </div>I'd argue you have this backwards. Rick is the character Genius is trying to make happen, but it fails to do so. Rick is what happens if you apply all of the advice Arc offers for improving Genius, not what you get out of Genius as written. Rick is a scientist. Rick is not a walking anti-science field. Rick's choices have stakes that matter to the narrative of his story that aren't undermined by the universe for Reasons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In Genius your grand designs like overthrowing the galactic federation are doomed to failure. </div> </div> </div>So is your portal gun that you repeatedly use in front of muggles.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But a genius who accepts that and makes peace with it can still find an emotional reward in bonding with their family or playing tourist across all of time and space. Rick is a charachter who's accepted that grand plans are doomed to failure, and now we're cheering him on as he moves towards making peace with it. </div> </div> </div>Here's the thing. Grand designs and plans aren't doomed to failure in the Rick and Morty narrative. <i>One</i> of Rick's plans (and his most emotionally important one) failed because other people planned harder than him. He didn't fail because a force in the universe made him fail. He failed because the other side won. He wasn't fighting some universal nihilistic constant. He was fighting an organization. The Galactic Federation had the power to triumph, so it did. Not because Rick's science failed him at dramatic moments. Or some moral sense of right and wrong. Or Rick being doomed to failure. Just simple dynamics of war.<br /> <br /> Rick's greatest failing in his choices in that regard is failing to recognize that order is good for most people. His anarchism is spurned by being restrained by order, but he has no pitch to the 99% of sapient species that are elevated by order instead of held back by it, so the majority of people were never going to see him as a freedom fighter while he was tearing down the system making their lives better. He left himself open to being labelled a terrorist because he never had a case to convince everyone he was trying to free them from &quot;control&quot; when none of them felt controlled beyond reasonable levels for social continuity. And you can't win a rebellion if the people don't care about your cause enough to fight with you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T13:34:01-07:00","id":954585,"title":"","content":"I guess it just boils down to me not seeing any kind of horror in &quot;you don't matter and nothing you do matters&quot; angle that people seem to be trying to explain is the central horror aspect of Genius. All I see is magical powers tied to mental illness being granted to people with no rhyme or reason, but they get to ride around on jetpacks and shoot death rays while fighting the moon nazi/hollow earth nazi alliance in space as a consolation prize. In that equation, all I'm seeing is that the horror aspect is characters getting slapped with &quot;suddenly you're crazy&quot; brush, which I find as insulting as I think a lot of people would if a game's horror element was being slapped with the &quot;suddenly you're queer&quot; brush<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=954556#post954556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would play that.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could even go as far as having the antagonist faction being founded two hundred years in the future as a result of some Inspired cataclysm. Antagonist faction keeps pointing out that the protagonist faction's <i>Laissez</i>-<i>faire</i> stance on inspiration has serious repercussions, while the protagonist faction claims that knowing about the potential for the cataclysm in question has already made it so it won't happen in the new timeline. Both sides probably have just as much evidence for their theories and against their opponents, so it sort of boils down to which side of the &quot;They want to take my jetpack away&quot; debate you come down on.<br /> <br /> Re-tool the central premise of Genius to Individualism vs Collectivism, I guess. Reminds me of Firefly, kind of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":7195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","user":"TidyGamer","date":". 08-20-2016, 04:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T14:09:34-07:00","id":954606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=954560#post954560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After all that I'm almost afraid to ask for your opinion of Princess the Hopeful.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like Princess the Hopeful. It's not perfect, but I'd definitely play it. Sensitivity and Shadows are probably among my favorite mechanics in games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 08-20-2016, 05:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T14:13:29-07:00","id":954607,"title":"","content":"I may be a white guy, but I have no problem with not mattering and having nothing I do mattering. For Pete's sake, I'm a writer. You don't go far in that field until you accept the fact you'll probably amount to nothing. That's not horrific to me, that's life.<br /> <br /> Speaking of white, I very nearly had a section on how this must speak to the horror of white people as they begin to understand that they aren't the center of the universe, but to it's credit, Genius didn't really load me up on that sort of ammo.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I did sort of sleep-read the history section.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T14:34:33-07:00","id":954618,"title":"","content":"Like, actually, let me rephrase a huge section down into something very simple to convey my problem about the horror of not mattering.<br /> <br /> I consider one of the most important points of actualization in my life, a series of experiences that made me a better person with a broader understanding and appreciation for the universe and people around me, was realizing <i>I was an unimportant, unimpressive shithead</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T14:38:41-07:00","id":954621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=954618#post954618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like, actually, let me rephrase a huge section down into something very simple to convey my problem about the horror of not mattering.<br /> <br /> I consider one of the most important points of actualization in my life, a series of experiences that made me a better person with a broader understanding and appreciation for the universe and people around me, was realizing <i>I was an unimportant, unimpressive shithead</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'm with you there. Nihilism doesn't work as a horror element for me because I find it liberating, comforting, and inspiring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T14:42:23-07:00","id":954624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=954607#post954607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I may be a white guy, but I have no problem with not mattering and having nothing I do mattering. For Pete's sake, I'm a writer. You don't go far in that field until you accept the fact you'll probably amount to nothing. That's not horrific to me, that's life.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. The <i>overwhelming</i> majority of people only meaningfully matter to a fractional handful of people that live in their city. If I died right now, the only people who will really be impacted by that are my mother, sister and maybe a dozen friends and associates all told. The idea lacks the sense of urgency or dread that I think Genius assumes it should.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T15:23:14-07:00","id":954648,"title":"","content":"I read the review of the first chapter. Skimmed the thread too. Here's what I have to say.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind I have only ever glanced at the Genius fansplat (the tone of which I found quite defensive), so my comments are in regards primarily to your review.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> First, a triggering element: in your description of Genius's approach as scientific smut (for lack of a better summary) you claim that Philosophy is the cornerstone of the humanities and thus is not a science. I feel the need to defend Philosophy in this regard.<br /> <br /> Philosophy is the purest science; it is the approach to the universe which allows the formulation of questions. Additionally, all humanities are ALSO sciences; the division between the two 'disciplines' is rather arbitrary and is used primarily to create dueling senses of superiority (Science majors believe they're smarter for not pursuing humanities, and humanities majors believe they're smarter for not pursuing sciences).<br /> <br /> In order of scientific purity (from most pure to most applied), scientific disciplines may be categorized:<br /> Philosophy -&gt; Logic -&gt; Mathematics -&gt; Physics -&gt; Chemistry (and Geoscience) -&gt; Biology -&gt; Psychology (and Computer Science) -&gt; Anthropology (and Sociology) -&gt; Engineering (and Theology) -&gt; Philosophy<br /> <br /> Logic is applied Philosophy. Biology is applied Chemistry, which makes it applied applied applied applied applied Philosophy.<br /> <br /> That Philosophy is both the start and end of the line of scientific purity isn't a mistake, either. All science relies [EDIT: How did that 'p' get in there?] on a leap of faith (the assumption that we have the ability to question) which in itself is an act of Philosophy. This creates an interesting logic loop; one science being true results in all sciences being true, but we can't definitively confirm that one is true. Each scientific discipline builds on an initial assumption which is taken to be true (it is the foundation of the implication, a core tool in proving the boolean state of a phenomenon). This could perhaps be the reason the writers of the fansplat pursued science in the fleeting manner they did; if you cannot make that initial assumption all that remains is the void. They may have come to such a conclusion subconsciously and simply failed to present the idea clearly. As it was an amateur production instead of an officially sanctioned product, I'm inclined to give leniency in this regard. For those clamoring for the book to BE official, though, you are correct that this topic should be addressed more clearly.<br /> <br /> <b>TL, DR (This section):</b> Philosophy is science. Humanities are science. All science requires an initial assumption, which may or may not be true.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Second (regarding the conversation in this thread, and this is just a personal pet peeve of mine): Every time this sort of conversation comes up, everybody goes on and on about Genius, Princess, and Leviathan. Those aren't the only fansplats! Demon the Redemption was the second to get a PDF treatment, and Embers had a full book (albeit not a great one) WAY before Leviathan did and before Princess was even on the map. That Demigod one has been on the top of the page for months now too, not to mention Pathogen and who knows how many others. These other fansplats have more hours of labor logged and more contributors than Genius, which has remained relatively static since its initial release (save the recent drive to push it into the second edition ruleset). It's like &quot;This is the first shack ever, isn't it great?&quot; &quot;They're building a skyscraper over there.&quot; &quot;Isn't this little shack great?&quot;. In that sense I suppose I agree with you; I don't get the hype.<br /> <br /> I feel that discussions like these need to be kept within the confines of the splat being examined. This review is about Genius. The conversation should stick to Genius. Maybe if players stopped trying to compare fan splats against each other their creators wouldn't be pressured into making their own material compatible with fanon and the quality of the resulting efforts would improve.<br /> <br /> <b>TL, DR (This section):</b> To people responding to this review; stick to Genius. Don't compare to other fan lines, since each fan line is designed to (and must) stand on its own two feet.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Third, car engines ARE demons! (Sorry, needed some humor in here)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Fourth, in defense of a fan book not having pictures, I can relate. A picture says a thousand words, and if the picture is wrong for the book the words it says can contradict the message the ACTUAL words are attempting to convey. Onyx Path Publications are fortunate to have astounding supernatural artwork. Conversely, fan projects are forced to scrape the barrel of the lead's talent (generally writers aren't great illustrators, so this resolves the work to stick figures and/or doodles) or shell out hundreds of dollars on professional artwork (a subject which not only complicates the legal situation of a fan work but which is also difficult to justify considering fan works can never make back the fiscal losses generated by such purchase). Walls of text with no breaks are hard to justify, but a picture of a grinning guy with crazy hair whose limbs are disproportionate and whose background defies three-point perspective will chase off prospective audiences before they even read the text. Genius at least recognized that risk and chose to let the words do the work.<br /> <br /> Reading about your call to go to the internet and find it, nothing is more generic than a bunch of public domain open license artwork. It might improve the quality in the short term but would become a point of contention as the project ages. Learning skills, on the other hand, is a good process. My own artwork improved greatly as I practiced and acquired tools to make it more consistent. Granted, they're still cartoons, but the act of working on a fan project improved my own marketable skills.<br /> <br /> <b>TL, DR (This section):</b> Fan projects don't have an art budget. Bad artwork can clash with theme. So no art may have been a good thing.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Fifth:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So it's not impossible to do a game of mad science. You just have to stick to it and be willing to work to justify things as science. Maybe when you use Mania to build Wonders, you enter into a state of reverie where your information processes these arcane physics absurdly fast, and in the flow of inspiration, you build or exploit branches of science hundreds of years ahead of where we're at. When you snap out of the reverie, you've defied current understanding, but you don't know how except for bits and snippets of information-nothing that makes sense yet, but you know it has place in the models. But because you were caught in the act of doing, these ideas are often just done, without the scrutiny needed to ensure these things can last or work perfectly. Bam, You can maintain the game as is while still talking about it in terms of future science and the manifestation of questions of &quot;What if?&quot;. </div> </div> </div>This. Is. Awesome. If that was the pitch Genius had made, I would have read the whole book instead of briefly skimming and dismissing it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And that's probably the one of the big problems Genius had in it's writing. In Ascension, all you had to do was bullshit, and reality did the rest. In Genius, that framework of &quot;clap your hands if you believe in Tesla's Death Ray&quot; doesn't exist, and the game had no idea whether it wanted it to be there or not. Was it science or was it the magic of belief? No one knew. I'm not even sure they thought about it. </div> </div> </div> This would have been cool too, and can easily be framed in the scope of science. Extradimensional reality doesn't have to follow the established (and accepted) ideas of physics; an alternate dimension might have entirely different physical laws. Genius could have tapped into that by having inspiration rip dimensional tears, temporarily letting these alternate physical laws into the World of Darkness. The result is the same: a clap of the hands summons a bolt of lightning. There is--however--nothing magical about it. The phenomenon can be explained within the confines of science... just not by the genius exploiting the phenomenon.<br /> <br /> Fan project leads can be divided into two categories. There are those who have an idea for a mechanic (or character type) and try to build a world around it. And then there are those who have an idea for a world and try to affix mechanics to it. Individuals rarely have the ability to fill in the missing component on their own; that is why projects like these (both professional and amateur) employ teams to bridge the gaps. Weakest link mentality doesn't apply here; more voices means more feedback which means a better result.<br /> As far as I am aware the production of Genius was entirely from the hands of a single individual. Gauging by its presentation he was a &quot;mechanics first, story later&quot; type of guy. That could mean the gameplay is very engaging but the plot is not. Since the review has only progressed through the first chapter that may be the case, which would mean many people enjoy Genius in SPITE of the setting rather than BECAUSE of the setting.<br /> <br /> <b>TL, DR (This section):</b> One guy on a project can only play to his strengths. Setting may not have been his strength. The issues found may be a result of your own strengths, and can be fixed by opening the project to team iteration (as it is currently).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Sixth:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Second off, the predominance of failure doesn't build to anything. This is actually a big point in science itself, as scientists spend a majority of their time trying to do something to get a result and coming back with a negative. This isn't a problem in that field, because science operates on the &quot;I found a thousand ways not to make a lightbulb&quot; principle, using the failures to help refine an answer that will inevitably remain, and finding ways to use the negative results in interesting and useful ways. Genius emphasizes it's failures, but never posits that that failure might serve a point, that it builds into a climatic point. Instead of telling a story of failing upwards into violation, it maintains a steady flat land of failure. And that's disappointing, because as a narrative there's a lot of cool to be found in failing upwards, and if I believed Genius did anything interesting with it's mechanics, I would be excited at the possibility of failing as a way to earn Inspiration Experience to possibly make a Wonder stick in the same ways Prometheans can calcify their Alembics. </div> </div> </div>Perhaps it's not an indication of &quot;Mad&quot; scientists but rather &quot;Bad&quot; scientists, but an inverted approach to the scientific method might be a more engaging premise.<br /> <br /> You START with a success. The first experiment results in a favorable outcome. But it was a field experiment. You try to recreate the results and try to put all of the variables in order to produce the phenomenon again, but the second time it fails. And it continues to fail. There's a variable in the mix that isn't right, and the &quot;Bad&quot; scientist can't find out what it is. Convinced by the anecdotal fluke that the foundation of the theory is correct, the scientist rants to peers and is decried as a quack.<br /> <br /> And they are, because they aren't eliminating scenarios which break their original hypothesis. Instead they are trying fanatically to convince others they are right, regardless of the clearly limited practicality of their results (which clearly require absurdly specific conditions).<br /> Again, if the game had presented itself like that I think I'd have given it a more thorough examination.<br /> <br /> <b>TL, DR (This section):</b> Starting with success and then peppering the 'lockdown' of the scientific method (experiment, observe, revise) with failures might have been a better approach to plot graph structure. The game starts to slow down? Throw in a success in another discovery, seemingly building off the first but impossible to reproduce. That's some Hadron Collider style frustration there, with quantum entropy's low particle count making nature unpredictable.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Seventh:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, apparently Geniuses go insane really easily, I guess. Disregarding the ableism for now, the problem is that the book doesn't really sell this problem too well. It never feels like a consequence, namely because it doesn't posit a reason why it happens. Maybe if I knew that the longer a Genius sits there not building wonder, the more and more his brain breaks, that'd be something. Hell, that would be cool, building Wonders is literally a stress relief mechanism, done to tire and weaken the connection to Inspiration for a while for some peace and quiet. But as is, Geniuses just kind of go insane because they go insane. It is bound to Inspiration, but it just feels like a thing that happens, much like the rest of this game. </div> </div> </div>This gave me a neat idea, built around my own issues with insomnia. Usually when I can't sleep it's because I have an idea in my head I need to get on paper. If I try to table it it gives me a headache. I become uncomfortable holding the idea in its ethereal form.<br /> It could be interesting if a Genius didn't sleep. Instead, they work on wonders. Making a wonder is thus the only way for them to regain Willpower (because hey, no sleep).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Eighth, it's really hard to write a thorough response in a popular thread (More funny, sorry. The replies keep flowing in)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Ninth:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> See, the reason that your &quot;large, oppressive organization&quot; enemy type that is often the playable antagonists is not also your &quot;individual or small group of radically deviated perspectives with radical, unusual powers&quot; is because the idea is that the &quot;radically deviated perspective&quot; is so unique and personal that is can't work in a larger harmony-in fact, that's why it's so strong, because it is unique and personal and a surprising one-hit KO in terms of shock value. Large organizations need to agree on something, and people who are invested in their own personal mythologies to the exclusion or all else don't really work in structured organizations. You might have Marauders running the Technocracy(although it's actually the Nefandi, yes, I know), but the Technocracy is not made up of insane people because insane people don't really work together well. The same goes for every other pairing of that sort you might imagine. </div> </div> </div>I agree. These Unmada sound more like a protagonist archetype, actually. If a player character believes machines function more effectively when they're coated with powder blue enamel (something which might actually be true in the weird bubble of science they've created), that's a cool thing. But a larger social construct isn't going to build up around that notion, especially if the individuals comprising that construct believe green, pink, and yellow are better respectively.<br /> <br /> And you're right, the hand-waving for it is painful. If the Lemuria came across some universal truth their individual realities should have collapsed into this consolidating black hole. They should all work from the foundation of one order of physics; one set of physical laws. They might not be the ones widely accepted by the general public, but they should be consistent. In fact, perhaps that should be their goal. If the reality-bending power of a wonder requires understanding of the science behind it (one which a normal person cannot comprehend), should not the goal of the Lemurians be to induct everyone into their numbers? Reveal the secrets to everyone? Burn the unbelievers? If reality is solipsistic, popular opinion should be their goal. And if they truly are mad and wicked, force should be the means to that end.<br /> <br /> But I must diverge from you here. While these Lemurians could represent some unified truth between them (like minds are more productive) they should not be so world-encompassing and universal. There should be conflicting &quot;one truths&quot; that different factions raise as their banners in their war of zealotry. These antagonists should not be a single force but many, fighting themselves as much as the player base.<br /> <br /> <b>TL, DR (This section):</b> I agree, it sounds like the Lemurian Unmada and the Genius should trade boots.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Tenth (I made it to ten?), I have to disagree about your interpretation of that one quote from the book. I think you may be overreacting, partially due to building stress from disagreements with the text and potentially due to other factors. While I agree the writer seems to have gotten the Lemurian and the Genius turned around (the wrong one's the organization, the wrong one's the focus), I don't believe the statement is advocating for oppression. It is calling for leadership.<br /> Service is not slavery. A soldier has to follow orders and may even have to die doing so, but the soldier is not a slave to the commanding officer. He/she entered the service willingly, is entitled to an explanation of the reason for the orders if something goes wrong, and is waived liability to the commanding authority if that happens.<br /> If the antagonists of this fan splat were switched (Lemurians have an agreed consensus on reality and force it upon everyone, whereas a Genius sees the potential for that consensus and rebels against it), you might not have even tripped on that paragraph (even if the wording was identical).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Eleventh, I thought writing points as I read the review was a good idea. I probably should have taken notes and organized this better. Oh well, at least it's chronological.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Twelfth... I've reached the end of the review for the first chapter. So I guess this is the TL, DR for my whole response.<br /> ...That's a hefty responsibility. Hmm....<br /> Philosophy IS science. Actually, all thought is science.<br /> [Readers, not review] Threads about a fansplat should stick to that fansplat (for instance, this thread is about Genius and should stick to Genius). Don't cross-compare gamelines.<br /> &lt;3rd point is a Joke&gt;<br /> Bad and generic artwork can do more harm than good. Be careful what you wish for.<br /> Projects assembled by one person will have weaknesses which team projects will not. Genius appears to be mechanic-oriented and not plot-oriented.<br /> An initial success followed by an experiment unable to be replicated (Anecdotal Observation, false hypothesis, failed experiment) might be a better format for Genius character plots than &quot;Everything fails&quot;.<br /> Geniuses could suffer perpetual insomnia, recovering Willpower through the construction of Wonders. Mechanics to drive connection to plot and power work well.<br /> &lt;8th point is a joke&gt;<br /> Lemurian and the player characters should change function. Players should be the Unmada, while the Lemurian have made a consensus on reality and intend to force it down everyone's throats. Also, the Lemurians should be more fractured organizations; reduce the scope of their influence and add infighting.<br /> Service and Slavery are different things; there is a difference between willingly agreeing to follow someone and being forced to do so. That difference should be emphasized: the Lemurians force others to think the way they do whereas a Genius invites others to think the way they do.<br /> &lt;11th point is a realization my response is disorganized. Sorry.&gt;<br /> &lt;12th point is this TL, DR&gt;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> One last thing; I hope your feedback and that of others in this discussion helps the developers of the Genius 2e CHroD update. I like seeing fan projects evolve and succeed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":610,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","user":"CJC","date":".  Relies, not Replies [Typo] 08-20-2016, 06:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T15:35:29-07:00","id":954656,"title":"","content":"There are a lot of good points in there in regards to things I got wrong or may have blown out of proportion. Thanks for sharing! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T15:39:23-07:00","id":954659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=954621#post954621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I'm with you there. Nihilism doesn't work as a horror element for me because I find it liberating, comforting, and inspiring.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm with you 100% there. When playing Planescape, one of my favourite factions is the Bleak Cabel, because they believe that the universe doesn't give a shit, and that is completely okay. They'll run soup kitchens and feed the homeless not just in spite of the universe's indifference, but because of it. If the universe doesn't care, but we choose to do something about it, that is the power we have. The difference may not last in the long run, but it makes a difference for someone today. It doesn't need to last forever.<br /> <br /> It also ties into one of the best speeches by a scientist ever.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale Blue Dot by Carl Sagan, 1994</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Earth is a very small stage in a vast cosmic arena. Think of the rivers of blood spilled by all those generals and emperors so that, in glory and triumph, they could become the momentary masters of a fraction of a dot. Think of the endless cruelties visited by the inhabitants of one corner of this pixel on the scarcely distinguishable inhabitants of some other corner, how frequent their misunderstandings, how eager they are to kill one another, how fervent their hatreds.<br /> <br /> Our posturings, our imagined self-importance, the delusion that we have some privileged position in the Universe, are challenged by this point of pale light. Our planet is a lonely speck in the great enveloping cosmic dark. In our obscurity, in all this vastness, there is no hint that help will come from elsewhere to save us from ourselves. [...]<br /> <br /> It has been said that astronomy is a humbling and character-building experience. There is perhaps no better demonstration of the folly of human conceits than this distant image of our tiny world. To me, it underscores our responsibility to deal more kindly with one another, and to preserve and cherish the pale blue dot, the only home we've ever known.</div> </div> </div> </div>It occurs to me that this may be why I don't &quot;get&quot; Genius anymore. Nihlism isn't terrifying to me. It's reality. Hell, I've looked so deep into the uncaring nature of the universe that it sweeps straight back around into humanism that leaves me deeply involved and caring for the people and world around me. Nihlism has undoubtedly allowed me to continue to be a kind and caring person even though I know my choices make no difference on the grand scale. I got brought to this place by science. The thing that Geniuses can't do anymore. Maybe that's why I don't see them as mad scientists at all, because real scientists faced unending nihilism in the face already and found the answers. Sagan may not have the toys of Geniuses, but he faced off squarely with the central theme of Genius and WON.<br /> <br /> That likely will mean I stick with the &quot;play somethings else Principle.&quot; Hopefully it won't exclude me from contributing constructively to this discussion, becuase it's getting interesting.<br /> <br /> (Also, as I postscript, I do love that you can be something like a mad composure in Genius. I think that you don't have to lose that bit to make Genuises back into real scientists)<br /> <br /> EDIT: Solid critique on the review CJC. As an individual with a degree in Biology and History, who studied the history of Science, Religion and Philosophy, and who educates in all of those areas, I heartily agree with your assertion that Philosophy is Science. You stated it much more eloquently than what I tried to come up with in my head.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":4433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","user":"Second Chances","date":". 08-20-2016, 06:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T15:45:27-07:00","id":954661,"title":"","content":"Going back to the &quot;If you did all that, it wouldn't be Genius&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> I just recognized what sort of plea this is, and, well.<br /> <br /> The problem is that Genius isn't anything. This isn't like Promethean, where trying to change it to fit transhumanist defies it's humanist core that literally everything else is built on top of. Genius tries to say it has a core, an idea, a theme, but it doesn't. It has nothing that makes up an identity. It is a game about People Doing Things and it Works until it Doesn't for Reasons.<br /> <br /> I took some of the things that are said, ideas patched around that void, and tried to offer ideas on how give them roots, how to make it reach down and create an identity. Because right now, Genius isn't anything other than a really badly handled GURPs. And I'm already not impressed with GURPs.<br /> <br /> I don't have to worry about Genius not being Genius, because Genius isn't even Genius. This is a game that tells you your mad scientists aren't doing science. You have to solve that fallacy first before that argument works.<br /> <br /> Mind you, if I want mad scientists, I have tons of games for that. it is not a mark in Genius's favor that I would happily leave it alone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 08-20-2016, 06:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T15:48:24-07:00","id":954662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TidyGamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=954585#post954585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess it just boils down to me not seeing any kind of horror in &quot;you don't matter and nothing you do matters&quot; angle that people seem to be trying to explain is the central horror aspect of Genius. All I see is magical powers tied to mental illness being granted to people with no rhyme or reason, but they get to ride around on jetpacks and shoot death rays while fighting the moon nazi/hollow earth nazi alliance in space as a consolation prize. In that equation, all I'm seeing is that the horror aspect is characters getting slapped with &quot;suddenly you're crazy&quot; brush, which I find as insulting as I think a lot of people would if a game's horror element was being slapped with the &quot;suddenly you're queer&quot; brush</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think Genius is aiming at &quot;nothing you do matters&quot;, exactly. I take the intended tension in the game to be this: a mad scientist wants, above all else, to have his theories acknowledged as true, and his inventions valued, by ordinary people; but that's the one thing mad scientists cannot ever have. Mad science can achieve anything imaginable, except the mad scientist's true desire.<br /> <br /> One of the problems Genius has is that while this frustration (<i>you must acknowledge my brilliance!</i>) is part of the mad scientist trope, it's not the thing that makes mad scientists monstrous. The mad scientist becomes a monster because he steps beyond the limits of human knowledge and morality to seize power; he rushes in where angels fear to tread, and leaves disaster in his wake. Genius doesn't look at the horrors its characters can inflict on other people - it shows its world from their perspective, and tries to generate horror from their mental states. (In that respect, it <i>is</i> rather like a canon CofD game: Beast the Primordial. But since that's generally seen as a flaw in Beast, putting Genius in its category isn't exactly flattering...) As a result it falls flat, because the frustration of not being seen as brilliant isn't particularly horrific.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=954606#post954606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like Princess the Hopeful. It's not perfect, but I'd definitely play it. Sensitivity and Shadows are probably among my favorite mechanics in games.</div> </div> </div> </div>*phew*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T15:51:08-07:00","id":954663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=954662#post954662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think Genius is aiming at &amp;quot;nothing you do matters&amp;quot;, exactly. I take the intended tension in the game to be this: a mad scientist wants, above all else, to have his theories acknowledged as true, and his inventions valued, by ordinary people; but that's the one thing mad scientists cannot ever have. Mad science can achieve anything imaginable, except the mad scientist's true desire.<br /> <br /> One of the problems Genius has is that while this frustration (<i>you must acknowledge my brilliance!</i>) is part of the mad scientist trope, it's not the thing that makes mad scientists monstrous. The mad scientist becomes a monster because he steps beyond the limits of human knowledge and morality to seize power; he rushes in where angels fear to tread, and leaves disaster in his wake. Genius doesn't look at the horrors its characters can inflict on other people - it shows its world from their perspective, and tries to generate horror from their mental states. (In that respect, it <i>is</i> rather like a canon CofD game: Beast the Primordial. But since that's generally seen as a flaw in Beast, putting Genius in its category isn't exactly flattering...) As a result it falls flat, because the frustration of not being seen as brilliant isn't particularly horrific.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Very well put.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T15:52:16-07:00","id":954664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=954662#post954662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think Genius is aiming at &quot;nothing you do matters&quot;, exactly. I take the intended tension in the game to be this: a mad scientist wants, above all else, to have his theories acknowledged as true, and his inventions valued, by ordinary people; but that's the one thing mad scientists cannot ever have. Mad science can achieve anything imaginable, except the mad scientist's true desire.<br /> <br /> One of the problems Genius has is that while this frustration (<i>you must acknowledge my brilliance!</i>) is part of the mad scientist trope, it's not the thing that makes mad scientists monstrous. The mad scientist becomes a monster because he steps beyond the limits of human knowledge and morality to seize power; he rushes in where angels fear to tread, and leaves disaster in his wake. Genius doesn't look at the horrors its characters can inflict on other people - it shows its world from their perspective, and tries to generate horror from their mental states. (In that respect, it <i>is</i> rather like a canon CofD game: Beast the Primordial. But since that's generally seen as a flaw in Beast, putting Genius in its category isn't exactly flattering...) As a result it falls flat, because the frustration of not being seen as brilliant isn't particularly horrific.<br /> <br /> <br /> *phew*</div> </div> </div> </div>A constant refrain of mine with friends while I was taking notes and writing was &quot;The horror of the mad scientist is not that he fails, but that he might succeed.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T16:01:26-07:00","id":954668,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar610_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"610\" data-vbnamecard=\"610\">CJC</a> <br /> <br /> Excellent post but two small things:<br /> <br /> 1) I think it's equally fair to say that rather than Philosophy is Science, that Science is a Philosophy. Philosophy is ultimately broader than just science, but science is irrevocably tied to philosophy as philosophy is the foundation that makes everything science builds stable.<br /> <br /> 2) The art thing is fair in the abstract, but at the same time the main creator of Genius is a webcomic artist, and maintained (I have no idea if he still does) a not-Tumblr of collecting &quot;mad science&quot; images. Bad art can be harmful, but the game also started in the hands of someone that should have understood the ability to get good enough art even if not professional paid for level art.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T16:05:02-07:00","id":954671,"title":"","content":"Really, the art complaint is just a jab at the people who think Onyx Path should pick it up as an official game. &quot;What, you want them to pick it up when it doesn't even have pictures? What, are people supposed to read it?&quot;<br /> <br /> Or at least, that was the joke before I actually read it.<br /> <br /> (The more I learn, the more I wanna punch the guy who specifically said that Onyx Path should buy the rights.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 08-20-2016, 07:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T16:17:06-07:00","id":954673,"title":"","content":"Something to chew on, for a Genius 2nd Edition...<br /> <br /> If you use Mage: the Awakening as a start, and use the Second Edition for the new Paradox rules as a start...that'll put you on fairly solid ground. But to my further point...<br /> <br /> I can see Geniuses being,in many ways, the opposite of Mages. Mages latch into the Supernal world. What if Geniuses are designed (somewhat haphazardly) to hook into the Abyss? <br /> <br /> The Abyss is where all the stuff deemed &quot;impossible&quot; dwells. What if Geniuses tap into that impossibility to build what they build? What if they're supposed to do that, in some sort of ecological way, bleeding the Abyss in and filtering it as a way to neutralize it, recycle it? Their Axioms measure how much &quot;impossibility&quot; they can safely manage, but they'd have the option of going further, and in the process creating something with potentially nasty drawbacks. In this scenario, they aren't scientists (though they need the trappings of science to contain something impossible in this reality), but shaman-engineers. They understand science, and can do science, but like mages, they are prone to obsessions and fixations, and sometimes the need to build an orbital death laser is too great to be ignored. If he pushes too hard, he begins to spill out Abyssal-laced Inspiration that makes reality act in certain small ways like the flawed theories the genius needs to work with impossible things, and after awhile, said Genius can get lost in this semi-reality. <br /> <br /> Because their inventions are Abyss-laced, poking and prodding it can cause it to &quot;malfunction&quot; (when it's really working as intended, because it's the Abyss), but for awhile it can work and be used just like any other piece of technology. Even if there's not really any way it should be working. Or living. Or thinking. This is because our reality is slowly using the Genius's work to detoxify that nugget of the Abyss that's powering it. Kind of like getting tiny injections of substances you're allergic to, in order to build up a tolerance. <br /> <br /> I don't have any useful suggestions on how to address the more problematic parts you mentioned. The review was certainly an eye-opener! <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T17:22:26-07:00","id":954688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=954664#post954664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A constant refrain of mine with friends while I was taking notes and writing was &quot;The horror of the mad scientist is not that he fails, but that he might succeed.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It's difficult that sometimes, when you say &quot;friends&quot;, you mean me, and sometimes you don't.<br /> <br /> Like I think some people hate me for some comments you said &quot;friends&quot; made in the Chapter 1 review that I didn't make, but the one here was totally me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T17:26:59-07:00","id":954690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=954688#post954688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's difficult that sometimes, when you say &quot;friends&quot;, you mean me, and sometimes you don't.<br /> <br /> Like I think some people hate me for some comments you said &quot;friends&quot; made in the Chapter 1 review that I didn't make, but the one here was totally me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let that some hang.<br /> <br /> And, actually, that refrain was shared with you and my Changeling Playtest group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T17:27:47-07:00","id":954691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=954690#post954690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let that some hang.<br /> <br /> And, actually, that refrain was shared with you and my Changeling Playtest group.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean. According to you, I'm their favorite poster, so I guess we think alike.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T17:32:35-07:00","id":954696,"title":"","content":"So, I was watching a review of Rosencrantz and Guildenstern Are Dead, link <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jEdewjDYBJg\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, and it reinforced a notion I had sort of worked with while reading Genius, that it is not nihilistic but absurdist. At it's heart, the conflict seemingly revolves around trying to define a reality that is summarily can't be defined, and that the force the drives them to do so can't take no for an answer. The question, then, is how does the Genius act to enter this state, and what do they do once they have arrived?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T18:51:19-07:00","id":954722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpectacularTentacular</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=954673#post954673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see Geniuses being,in many ways, the opposite of Mages. Mages latch into the Supernal world. What if Geniuses are designed (somewhat haphazardly) to hook into the Abyss?</div> </div> </div> </div>Part of me thinks there are enough potential origins for Genius's in CoD already that you could probably have the x splats of genius's swapped for a cross-over element origin for that genius's power.<br /> <br /> One splat could hook into the abyss and use physics that do not exist (mage), another could tap into the astral through twisted but inspirational dreams (beast), another could be warped and enthralled by pyros allowing them to turn obsession into new discoveries (promethean), another might have a fragment of divine insight from some interaction with infrastructure burning technological designs that operate on occult matrixes into their soul (demon), and another could have been claimed by spirits of science/knowledge/advancement which allow the genius to create and discover things that humanity could not know but he must cling to scientific methods and societies or essence will cease to feed his inspiration (werewolf).<br /> <br /> There are many potential reasons for why geniuses could exist, and yet no justification is given....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 08-20-2016, 11:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T19:07:37-07:00","id":954736,"title":"","content":"I've had no contact with Genius outside of this thread, but I think the observations about its powers being &quot;science that cannot be reproduced&quot; makes it a better fit for the blank spaces between Promethean's Alchemists and the arcane physics of the God-Machine. I mean, some of the themes of obsession are similar to Awakening, and mages strike me as good potential foils, but maybe the constant comparison isn't a useful one. If, rather than trying to <i>replace</i> Awakening's mages, you're looking for a place where Geniuses can fill an unoccupied niche, that nexus of Alchemist, mage, and arcane physicist seems like it has some potential, especially if you adopt the &quot;random prototypes that work but can't be reproduced&quot; mechanic suggested upthread.<br /> <br /> (Dammit, Sean. I'm not even interested in mad scientists, and you and a couple other here have gotten me thinking about how to model them thematically and mechanically with the CofD engine. :-P)<br /> <br /> ETA: Or what Milo said. The concept has a lot of potential. Sounds like it might just need a mechanically and thematically bold revision.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":1094,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","user":"Eric Zawadzki","date":". 08-20-2016, 10:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T19:36:16-07:00","id":954753,"title":"","content":"Welcome to the exercise. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T19:54:36-07:00","id":954758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=954722#post954722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Part of me thinks there are enough potential origins for Genius's in CoD already that you could probably have the x splats of genius's swapped for a cross-over element origin for that genius's power.<br /> <br /> One splat could hook into the abyss and use physics that do not exist (mage), another could tap into the astral through twisted but inspirational dreams (beast), another could be warped and enthralled by pyros allowing them to turn obsession into new discoveries (prometehan), another might have a fragment of divine insight from some interaction with infrastructure burning technological designs that operate on occult matrixes into their soul (demon), and another could have been claimed by spirits of science/knowledge/advancement which allow the genius to create and discover things that humanity could not know but he must cling to scientific methods and societies or essence will cease to feed his inspiration (werewolf).<br /> <br /> There are many potential reasons for why geniuses could exist, and yet no justification is given....</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would play the shit out of that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T19:57:58-07:00","id":954759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=954753#post954753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Welcome to the exercise. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I already have one completely stupid fan project devouring my free time. Like, I've got <i>maybe</i> 10 more sessions left in the Mage game I'm currently running, so it's too late to implement a full rewrite of the mechanics and setting to...do a bunch of things I think would be cool in a variant of Awakening. It's doubly dumb because it involves such a tight marriage of homebrew CofD and homebrew Awakening mechanics as to make it pretty much non-modular and therefore useless to anyone who isn't me. It is also not helping that I don't have word count caps or deadlines to keep the project within a reasonable scope.<br /> <br /> This sort of project is basically the writer equivalent of an artist's sketchpad, and me dabbling in modeling mad scientists would just be an additional, fresh sketchpad that needs filling. *smirk*<br /> <br /> I'll watch to see where this thread goes, at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T20:00:53-07:00","id":954762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=954759#post954759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I already have one completely stupid fan project devouring my free time. Like, I've got <i>maybe</i> 10 more sessions left in the Mage game I'm currently running, so it's too late to implement a full rewrite of the mechanics and setting to...do a bunch of things I think would be cool in a variant of Awakening. It's doubly dumb because it involves such a tight marriage of homebrew CofD and homebrew Awakening mechanics as to make it pretty much non-modular and therefore useless to anyone who isn't me. It is also not helping that I don't have word count caps or deadlines to keep the project within a reasonable scope.<br /> <br /> This sort of project is basically the writer equivalent of an artist's sketchpad, and me dabbling in modeling mad scientists would just be an additional, fresh sketchpad that needs filling. *smirk*<br /> <br /> I'll watch to see where this thread goes, at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>My point was more at the many reasons I did it. &quot;I don't like this game, let's look at it and see how we'd make it interesting&quot; sometimes yield interesting results.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T20:10:42-07:00","id":954766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=954762#post954762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point was more at the many reasons I did it. &quot;I don't like this game, let's look at it and see how we'd make it interesting&quot; sometimes yield interesting results.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. My impulse tends to hit me harder when it's &quot;this is doing almost everything I want at my game table, so how can I make it perfect for my group?&quot; Like, I'm planning to run Ex3 after Mage, and while I haven't yet descended hard into fiddling with knobs, yet (only a few new artifact weapons and a modular expansion for Socialize, so far), once my gamers start talking to me about it, I know I'll find a couple things we want to tweak. TBH, I used to assume that <i>every</i> GM did this sort of thing, but apparently that is not necessarily the case, and some groups actively resent having to come up with customized powers/artifacts even in games where it is clear that certain of these are unique to individual characters and so defy an exhaustive catalogue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T22:11:23-07:00","id":954819,"title":"","content":"Alright, there's a lot of stuff in the Chapter 1 post, much of which I agreed with, but the part that's most relevant to me is the last section, so I'll mostly respond to that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=950279#post950279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><u>TL;DR-What Can We Do to Make Genius Good?</u></b><br /> &quot;Genius is cheap self-congratulatory inspiration porn, fight me&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Not gonna lie, this is probably the very best line in the entire thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Make Inspiration the Divine Fire<i>.</i></b> </div> </div> </div>I honestly had this as personal headcanon for a long time, and while I probably don'tthink it should be made <i>quite</i> so explicit as to outright state it, I do think Genius could benefit from playing up Inspiration as an actual force in the world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Commit to Science.</b> </div> </div> </div>I actually want to go in the opposite direction. It's gonna be hard to get away from the science fetishism is we keep things clinging too closely to science, and there's a lot of room for Inspired artists and creative types. There's a lot of different types of &quot;Genius&quot; other than nerds with sliderules. People whose fevered sculptures come to life, songs that enthrall those who hear, politicians with nonsensical plans of office that keep the nation afloat anyway, a martial artist who has perfected a technique lethal to victim and user.<br /> You said a lot about intelligence fetishism too, and maybe making the Genius umbrella cover more than just intellectual disciplines could help with that.<br /> <br /> Really, though, that's just my opinion on it, and if science remains the focus, it could still certainly work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Break the World. </b> </div> </div> </div>The Magnum Opus as an important was one of the first ideas I threw out there, and I'm glad you agree. Breaking the World is probably something that Genius so desperately <i>wanted</i> to do, given the pulp action angle, and it'd be nice for that to actually be possible, even if on a small scale.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Fight the Chaos.</b> </div> </div> </div>This is definitely a neat angle to take for the &quot;why&quot; of Genii, if not the &quot;what.&quot; Ultimately, the what is a way less important detail in the long run.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Don't Sweat Mage.</b> </div> </div> </div>While I've been looking a little at Mage mechanically, since they have similarly expansive and freeform powers, I really agree. Mages are philosophers who take truths and fit the world to them. Genii should take the world and try to get some approximation of truth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Kill the Statistics.</b> </div> </div> </div>I agree completely. Yes, yes, yes! Hell, some might argue that Inspiration would be <i>more</i> likely to be found in the marginalized groups, seeing as they're usually the ones who get screwed over enough to be that mix of desperate and driven, but that might have some unfortunate implications of it own.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Kill the Money.</b> </div> </div> </div>I think it'd be a good idea to replace the Resources-based stuff with actual Roleplaying-based requirements (&quot;your fancy freeze ray needs a giant diamond to work, Doctor Fries.&quot;), and I'll probably use the crafting mechanics as a start point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Bind Them to Humanity.</b> </div> </div> </div>I think one thing we'll be doing, for starters, is making the Catalysts more about people, and tying them into that. Grimms aren't angry at the world, they're angry at the Board of Directors, the Ethics Committee, and those pussies with their high-powered lawyers! Staunens don't travel the cosmos for funsies, they love seeing their normal buddies react to the crazy aliens and you geometrically impossible time machine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Redefine Lemuria.</b> </div> </div> </div>I actually kind of ignored Lemuria entirely when I played, because I could never figure how the hell they were supposed to rule anything. Maybe instead of having a unified philosophy of any kind, Lemuria is purely a construct of convenience, an archaic system of feudal hierarchy that offers the big guys quality lackeys and offers the little guys protection.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Restructure the Foundations.</b> </div> </div> </div>Foundations felt weird to me. Y-splats have usually been about outlook, but the Foundations are more about discipline and area of study. Yeah, a lot of Y-splats do that, but even relatively focused ones like, say, the Ordo Dracul have a lot of room conceptually. You could have a vampiric alchemist and an undead psychiatrist and a supernatural geneticist and they could all be under the Ordo banner. Meanwhile, the Foundations feel at least a little narrow. I might just be because of the way they're written, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Get Creative With the Sciences.</b> </div> </div> </div>I mentioned this earlier with &quot;Commit to Science,&quot; but opening up Inspiration to things other than science helps. Inspiration definitely stands on the fringes of human endeavor, so kooky fringe science, radical political theory and experimental art should definitely be the main deal. Some time and space will definitely be devoted to that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Get More Global.</b> </div> </div> </div>I agree, Genius is real eurocentric a lot of the time. That said, as an American white cis male, I might not be the best one to push this to where it needs to be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Scrub the History.</b> </div> </div> </div>Ol' buddy ol' pal, if that's the case, you are gonna <i>hate</i> the time travel section. But rest assured, that's binned.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Ditch the Insanity.</b> </div> </div> </div>You're right. And I may not have been sufficiently mindful of that in working on 2E. But I'm definitely thinking decoupling &quot;crazy&quot; from &quot;Genius&quot; is a necessary step.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i><b>AND ABOVE ALL ELSE!</b></i><br /> <br /> <b>Ignore This Asshole On Whatever Point You Want If You Disagree With Him.</b> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, that would be a real Unmada thing for me to do. You gave a lot of criticisms, and it's clear you don't like the work, but it's also clear that you're giving it a fair shot, and all the deuces you've dropped on it are pretty well-deserved.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> PS: Ayoko Von Schreber is so fake a name I wouldn't be surprised if it actually went right back around to being real. </div> </div> </div>I won't lie, I googled it. &quot;Von Schreber&quot; is a name, &quot;Ayoko&quot; is a name, but &quot;Ayoko Von Schreber&quot; is not that I could find.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T01:23:29-07:00","id":954883,"title":"","content":"I could not get through that Chapter 1 review, so I skipped to the tl;dr at the end. (I started fading during the Lemuria stuff and simply didn't process the next section.) Unfortunately, I don't remember my reading of Genius well enough to agree or disagree with anything you've said, so I'm just going to hit something else.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I've been looking a little at Mage mechanically, since they have similarly expansive and freeform powers, I really agree. Mages are philosophers who take truths and fit the world to them. Genii should take the world and try to get some approximation of truth.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there's a seed of something there. Mage is about arrogance and overreach, of course, but it might be really interesting to flip that: make Genius about false humility and self-empowerment. That, in the beginning, you lack the conviction to change how things work. It doesn't matter that your family finds out because you don't have the confidence to actually take a risk and affect things on a meaningful scale. But as you push up this stat, hell let's call it Confidence as a double-entendre of statistical error and self-assurance, you become more capable of doing things at scale.<br /> <br /> And naturally, when you make a mistake and everything blows up, your Confidence takes a hit. But really? If you try, you can figure shit out. There's no horror in it, really, but I'm okay with that. I don't need every RPG to be a horror RPG. Instead, you need to find lots of ways to boost and maintain your Confidence so that, when you throw that dice pool, it has a real shot at succeeding.<br /> <br /> I mean... oh hell with it. Let's just quote Emerson:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Self-Reliance</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I read the other day some verses written by an eminent painter which were original and not conventional. The soul always hears an admonition in such lines, let the subject be what it may. The sentiment they instil is of more value than any thought they may contain. To believe your own thought, to believe that what is true for you in your private heart is true for all men, \u2014 that is genius. Speak your latent conviction, and it shall be the universal sense; for the inmost in due time becomes the outmost,\u2014\u2014 and our first thought is rendered back to us by the trumpets of the Last Judgment. Familiar as the voice of the mind is to each, the highest merit we ascribe to Moses, Plato, and Milton is, that they set at naught books and traditions, and spoke not what men but what they thought. A man should learn to detect and watch that gleam of light which flashes across his mind from within, more than the lustre of the firmament of bards and sages. Yet he dismisses without notice his thought, because it is his. In every work of genius we recognize our own rejected thoughts: they come back to us with a certain alienated majesty. Great works of art have no more affecting lesson for us than this. They teach us to abide by our spontaneous impression with good-humored inflexibility then most when the whole cry of voices is on the other side. Else, to-morrow a stranger will say with masterly good sense precisely what we have thought and felt all the time, and we shall be forced to take with shame our own opinion from another.<br /> <br /> There is a time in every man's education when he arrives at the conviction that envy is ignorance; that imitation is suicide; that he must take himself for better, for worse, as his portion; that though the wide universe is full of good, no kernel of nourishing corn can come to him but through his toil bestowed on that plot of ground which is given to him to till. The power which resides in him is new in nature, and none but he knows what that is which he can do, nor does he know until he has tried. Not for nothing one face, one character, one fact, makes much impression on him, and another none. This sculpture in the memory is not without preestablished harmony. The eye was placed where one ray should fall, that it might testify of that particular ray. We but half express ourselves, and are ashamed of that divine idea which each of us represents. It may be safely trusted as proportionate and of good issues, so it be faithfully imparted, but God will not have his work made manifest by cowards. A man is relieved and gay when he has put his heart into his work and done his best; but what he has said or done otherwise, shall give him no peace. It is a deliverance which does not deliver. In the attempt his genius deserts him; no muse befriends; no invention, no hope.<br /> <br /> Trust thyself: every heart vibrates to that iron string. Accept the place the divine providence has found for you, the society of your contemporaries, the connection of events. Great men have always done so, and confided themselves childlike to the genius of their age, betraying their perception that the absolutely trustworthy was seated at their heart, working through their hands, predominating in all their being. And we are now men, and must accept in the highest mind the same transcendent destiny; and not minors and invalids in a protected corner, not cowards fleeing before a revolution, but guides, redeemers, and benefactors, obeying the Almighty effort, and advancing on Chaos and the Dark.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mad Science? I dunno. Transgression? Hell yes. I think it would help satisfy people who want transhumanism in Promethean, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T04:42:29-07:00","id":954906,"title":"","content":"I like the phrase of Genius thinking science has a nice butt. It's also given me a concise way to talk about what I think of Ascension's Paradigms.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T05:47:48-07:00","id":954913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=954468#post954468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Madoka Magica. Kyoko Sakura is best girl, but that's just, like, my opinion man.<br /> <br /> 2) It is true that the divides are artificial, but Genius wants it to be a point, and honestly, it's not a point I care to take away. Hell, I sort of used it a center point for the idea of the better world, whether it's usable or not.<br /> <br /> I mean, it doesn't have to, but then Genius runs the risk of relying too much on Mage-isms, and I'm fairly sure Genius fans are tired of the comparisons.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Ah, that would be why. I really should watch that series at some point. <br /> <br /> 2) While the comparisons might be tiring, its also unavoidable since the game itself has its roots in the WoD/CofD Mage editions. Now, I think the game could have really stood on its own if we delved more into having just mad scientists being one splat, and having others be things like robots/golems, human experiments like the Invisible Man, and so on. Its been a few years since I read Genius, but that was the major thing that struck me as I read through everything - it was trying its damned hardest to be a Mage-style game without actually being a &quot;mage.&quot; <br /> <br /> The game has supposedly has changed since last I saw it, but everything I've heard still sounds like it hasn't gotten away from its roots.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=954507#post954507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Factually untrue.</div> </div> </div> </div> Factually? You'll pardon my doubt. <br /> <br /> In either case, it still remains true that Genius creates a hard line between regular science, magic and Inspired particular brand of abilities, making them rather guilty of that western-culture-divide I was talking about, rather than avoiding it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T07:07:41-07:00","id":954933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=954913#post954913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Factually? You'll pardon my doubt.</div> </div> </div> </div> Moochava's views on the victorianish Sons of Ether are a matter of public record<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Etherites are obviously the Sons of Ether, with all the racism, sexism, and imperialism of the actual Victorian Age--which Ascension occasionally nodded to--and all that &quot;Science isn't about facts! It's about zap-zap-zoom!&quot; given the laughing-at it deserves. They also gobble up a lot of the &quot;pyramid power/UFO healing/*X-Files*&quot; conspiracy stuff that used to be much bigger than it is now. They sit in the epicenter of the &quot;They all laughed but I'll show them!&quot; &lt;<a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ppFVmnmpGz8\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ppFVmnmpGz8</a>&gt;vibe that runs through *Genius*. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=954913#post954913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In either case, it still remains true that Genius creates a hard line between regular science, magic and Inspired particular brand of abilities, making them rather guilty of that western-culture-divide I was talking about, rather than avoiding it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd like to see some evidence for this, give me a few quotations from the source book.<br /> <br /> The setting is full of Geniuses who defy any hard division between science and magic and draw on both for their Wonders: Oracles, Spice Litches, the Alembic aesthetic, the Hermetic Order.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=954562#post954562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> We're not challenged with inevitability, we're told the correct answer is just accept it and move on.</div> </div> </div> </div> How's that different than Promethian saying the correct answer is the New Dawn? There's still interesting stories in the journey.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 08-21-2016, 12:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T10:21:15-07:00","id":955008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=954906#post954906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the phrase of Genius thinking science has a nice butt. It's also given me a concise way to talk about what I think of Ascension's Paradigms.</div> </div> </div> </div>In Mage, it works, because aesthetics are power-the power of belief in images carries the game. It also relies on divergent images, so the shallowness is spread around.<br /> <br /> Still, the best thing about Mage 20th is that they went lengths to mitigate that. Genius could do with that too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T10:30:11-07:00","id":955014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not gonna lie, this is probably the very best line in the entire thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Credit where it's due, Gecko originally said it about Promethean. It just fit my opinion of Genius too well.<br /> <br /> I know, irony abounds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T11:56:31-07:00","id":955053,"title":"","content":"I know we've already decided to move on how to fix Genius, but I wanted to quick revisit something.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=954696#post954696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I was watching a review of Rosencrantz and Guildenstern Are Dead, link <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jEdewjDYBJg\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, and it reinforced a notion I had sort of worked with while reading Genius, that it is not nihilistic but absurdist. At it's heart, the conflict seemingly revolves around trying to define a reality that is summarily can't be defined, and that the force the drives them to do so can't take no for an answer. The question, then, is how does the Genius act to enter this state, and what do they do once they have arrived?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And here I admit I'm surprised: The absurdist streak in Genius is worn proudly on it's sleeve. The Venture Brothers and MST3K quotes were the biggest tip-off. (But then, to be fair, you probably haven't read that far.)<br /> <br /> To me, what Genius is trying to do is mine <i>horror from the absurdity</i>. Some people won't respond to it, and that's fine, but for me horror and absurdity can be (and often are) opposite sides of the same coin. They only differ in approach. That takes a certain mindset to appreciate, but I'd argue that that mindset is what draws the more rabid fans to it. Let me give you an example of what I'm talking about<b></b>: The Lemurians.<br /> <br /> Now, to understand where I'm coming from, I have to introduce the concept of &quot;gamer of a certain age.&quot; There was a time before geek hobbies were so widely accepted, a time before the Internet blew everyone's minds with geek overload. Those were magical, <i>horrible</i> times. Growing up, you carefully floated geek references to things, because if the people around you recognized it as geek-oriented, you'd get shamed for it. Sort of like living in a John Hughes/Steven Spielberg movie. So you developed a sort of &quot;hanky-code for geeks&quot;, and those who got it were part of your hidden tribe. Instant friends!<br /> <br /> But then you went to college, and/or moved out of your parent's house. Time to get a new social network. So you used your hobbies to break the ice. For roleplaying, this introduced you to God's special one-off humans on a disturbingly regular basis. (Google Al Bruno III binder of shame for examples.) It became a social network of sorts, just one where dysfunctionality (sort of) greased the wheels. This was before we all internalized &quot;no gaming &gt; bad gaming&quot;, because not all of us were convinced that we'd find others who would like us without having to endure at least some dysfunction in the relationship.<br /> <br /> So while you express disbelief that Lemuria, as written, could possibly work, gamers-of-a-certain-age remember <i>living through it</i> in their gaming groups past and maybe present. Thus, they swallow it uncritically. Consider a Genius's point of view: <i>When I tell people about my enthusiasms, they think I'm spouting gibberish. When I introduce them to my work, somehow things always go haywire in the most embarrassing way. When I tell people of things I've seen, things I've learned, they shy away from me. Maybe the cops get called. The only people I can interact with are people who do what I do, see what I see. They don't understand me, and I don't understand them, but they know what I'm going through, and sometimes that's enough. Meanwhile, real life keeps piling bills and obligations outside my door, and I don't know what to do. I don't want to function in the real world, and maybe I can't. And I'm deeply afraid that <b>this is forever, the rest of my life.</b></i><br /> <br /> Do you now see how people can be enthused by Genius? Do you see how people can believe that some group like Lemuria can function? Do you understand why the absurdity is so front-and-center? Do you now know what I mean when I say that horror and absurdity are the opposite sides of the same coin? Do you now see the <i>hell</i> I endu...Never mind. Hopefully, I've made my point. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Regardless, we all agree that Genius needs some work, some de-absurdification and cynicism-draining, and a sincere approach to the experience of actual geniuses trying to cope in a world that can't or won't recognize them while alive, and might not recognize them after they're dead. And there's numerous problematic things besides. But with the proper lens, it'll help to understand the basic work as-is, and help translate it into the game we want to play. Just some thoughts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2176,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","user":"SpectacularTentacular","date":". 08-21-2016, 02:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T12:46:03-07:00","id":955104,"title":"","content":"The thing is, I think the self-reference to geek culture is tied into what Arc was getting at with the point about &quot;you've been special all along&quot;. The fact that a game written by &quot;gamers of a certain age&quot; for &quot;gamers of a certain age&quot; features protagonists who are presented as tortured geniuses, cursed with divine inspiration and forced to endure the horror of being too smart for normal people to understand, dooming them to fail at everything forever by no fault of their own strikes me as self-pitying and self-congratulatory in equal measure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T12:58:27-07:00","id":955111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955104#post955104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is, I think the self-reference to geek culture is tied into what Arc was getting at with the point about &quot;you've been special all along&quot;. The fact that a game written by &quot;gamers of a certain age&quot; for &quot;gamers of a certain age&quot; features protagonists who are presented as tortured geniuses, cursed with divine inspiration and forced to endure the horror of being too smart for normal people to understand, dooming them to fail at everything forever by no fault of their own strikes me as self-pitying and self-congratulatory in equal measure.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I wouldn't dream of arguing otherwise. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> If there's anything to gain outside of a small chuckle at my post, it's the hope that, if we look at G:tT as it is now for what it is, we can better see where it became dissatisfying and build a better one. I wrote what I did because I was thinking about this thread this morning, and I noticed that the parallels were too striking (and ominous) to ignore. It's more of a comedy post than anything, I'll be honest, but hopefully there's enough there otherwise to be helpful. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T13:22:53-07:00","id":955127,"title":"","content":"For the record I am too young to be &quot;of a certain age&quot; and I never interpreted Geniuses as suffering because mortals misunderstood them.<br /> <br /> Quite the opposite, I felt that in Genius: the Transgression mortals understand the Inspired perfectly. When they fear a Genius or laugh at their theories, they're absolutely correct.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Genius Website</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;They all laughed at my theories! They called me mad! But now I'll have my revenge!&quot;<br /> <br /> If only it were so simple. They laughed because you WERE mad. They laughed because your inventions crumbled when unveiled and your theories turned to gibberish. You wept when you saw your equations riddled with childish errors.</div> </div> </div> </div>And Geniuses don't fail through no fault of their own. They fail because raw inspiration doesn't come with good project management skills, and often because their ideas are fundamentally bad in the first place. There's an entire group (Seattle's Atomists) who want to create a utopian fascist police state governed by all-seeing technology. That plan's garenteed to fail because &quot;utopian fascist police state&quot; is an inherently self-contradictory concept.<br /> <br /> Incidently, if they were player charachters instead of antagonists and I was the storyteller I wouldn't have them fail to build it. Frankenstein's monster turned against him, not remained lifeless on the slab. I would (assuming the players do well) have their master computer take full control by the end of act 2; act three would be all about dealing with the inevitable consequences of living in a fascist police state. Alternatively their master computer decides that the only way to make a utopia is to ditch the fascism.<br /> <br /> <br /> This all requires a fair amount of player by-in. You have to choose an unrealistic goal, or create a charachter who's likely to screw up on a reasonable goal. But there's nothing wrong with requiring by-in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 08-21-2016, 04:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T13:28:41-07:00","id":955132,"title":"","content":"Arc, I'm trying, but this is like...I just can't &quot;get&quot; what you're saying. <br /> <br /> I don't understand why you object to the continued assertion to &quot;what geniuses do isn't real science&quot;. It's a personal horror game. The idea of being a scientist and suddenly being unable to do actual science is genuinely horrifying, and it's one of the most brilliant bits of personal horror I've seen in any ChroD line. <br /> <br /> And Lemuria? They're among my absolute favorite antagonists in any fiction, because they're so obviously wrong yet still so seductive- if you were a Genius, wouldn't you want to say &quot;fuck reality, I'm right!&quot;?<br /> <br /> And the &quot;science fetishism&quot; thing...yeah. For one thing, that comic is smug and kind of douchey. Imagine if you shared a fun science fact with someone and they shot you down like that. Would you have any desire to interact with that person? &quot;Hey, did you know that chameleons don't actually change color for camouflage?&quot; &quot;Ugh, you dumb science poser. I bet you don't even own a lab.&quot; You yourself point out how often it harps on how what Geniuses do isn't science- so of course it's going to be a fetishized, false form of science. Because that's what mad scientists do, especially in horror fiction! Horror fiction basically treats &quot;mad science&quot; as magic, and Genius takes that to a beautifully absurd conclusion by crafting a world built on science-as-magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T13:35:48-07:00","id":955139,"title":"","content":"In an attempt to be serious: <br /> <br /> It seems to me that Genius currently looks at the mad scientist as it's own thing, rather than just the Victorian version of the &quot;wizard in the tower&quot;, which is further a Dark Ages stereotype of the <i>eremite</i> (hermit)--the solitary person who cannot live in the current society for personal reasons, but tries to communicate with others through...well, art, inventions, 'magic' of a sort, etc. They lead lonely lives of quiet desperation, trying to get people to understand their vision. But they cannot communicate this vision in terms that the people around them understand, so they live in tension with society, neither being truly apart nor forging a connection. <br /> <br /> The question becomes, I think, how do we widen this core experience to get the full diversity of characters possible and get it to fit within the mechanics of the Chronicles of Darkness. <br /> <br /> Or...am I missing something else that can broaden and deepen this core image even further?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T13:41:26-07:00","id":955145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955132#post955132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't understand why you object to the continued assertion to &quot;what geniuses do isn't real science&quot;. It's a personal horror game. The idea of being a scientist and suddenly being unable to do actual science is genuinely horrifying, and it's one of the most brilliant bits of personal horror I've seen in any ChroD line.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe the main problem wasn't that &quot;Mad Science isn't Science&quot;, but that the book doesn't say anything about what Mad Science is- it is not science, it is not magic, it is not some mad blessing of Chtulu or rainbow magic given by unicorn. It spends word count on saying what it's not instead on what it is. (I relay on Arc's review for this, considering I haven't read the book myself)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And Lemuria? They're among my absolute favorite antagonists in any fiction, because they're so obviously wrong yet still so seductive- if you were a Genius, wouldn't you want to say &quot;fuck reality, I'm right!&quot;? </div> </div> </div>again, haven't read the book, but it is a combination of having a full organization of mad individuals who simply can't work together which strains the suspension of disbelief together with the fact that it seems that Lemuria's oppression was, in general, a good thing and the the genii were the ones to ruin it (not to mention that the &quot;humanity should be controlled&quot; theme leaves a bad taste in the mouth)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And the &quot;science fetishism&quot; thing...yeah. For one thing, that comic is smug and kind of douchey. Imagine if you shared a fun science fact with someone and they shot you down like that. Would you have any desire to interact with that person? &quot;Hey, did you know that chameleons don't actually change color for camouflage?&quot; &quot;Ugh, you dumb science poser. I bet you don't even own a lab.&quot; You yourself point out how often it harps on how what Geniuses do isn't science- so of course it's going to be a fetishized, false form of science. Because that's what mad scientists do, especially in horror fiction! Horror fiction basically treats &quot;mad science&quot; as magic, and Genius takes that to a beautifully absurd conclusion by crafting a world built on science-as-magic. </div> </div> </div>again, the problem seems to be that the game focus only on aesthetics without any content- it use &quot;science fetishism&quot; to cover a big hole which has nothing with it. Genii do nothing to create nothing and violate rules which aren't exist using a big nothing, with the only reason you could even say they are mad scientists is because they wear white robes and googles and scream &quot;SCIENCE!&quot; every now and then, making them into a caricature of themselves.<br /> <br /> Again, never read the book, only the review- and even that has probably caused me a Breaking Point or two.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T13:51:02-07:00","id":955154,"title":"","content":"That said, I'm not one to say that Genius is without problems. That's why I'm remaking Mage and not just updating it. This thread is going to help Mage: The Transgression a lot, since the genuine problems with Genius are ones I'm going to address. For example, the statistics section and the problem of how Geniuses maintain the masquerade have always struck me as major problems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T13:56:06-07:00","id":955157,"title":"","content":"I don't care how Genius explains what Geniuses do. They can wish upon unicorn poop and that poop devours the lives of children all around the world to allow Geniuses the revelation of how to make an immortality gate, for all I care.<br /> <br /> What I care about is that there is <i>some reason</i> that Geniuses can do what they can. Genius doesn't answer that. It's not science, it's not magic, and it's explicitly a rule that no Genius know why or how any of the things they do happens. There is <i>no world</i>.<br /> <br /> Compare that to literally any gameline in ChroD-and even the fangames I bother to know anything about-where I can sit here and tell you, in generals or not an indecent amount of specific information, what is happening when the monster uses their power, how the forces at work in the monster and around the monster make that happen, and why that is.<br /> <br /> Did you know that Utterances are caused by the configuration of the aspects of the Arisen's soul, each aspect resonating in a &quot;music of the spheres&quot; sort of way, sending out a frequency that causes the Sekhem to reorder itself in accordance to that vibration and thus cause reality to shape itself in accordance to it? Whether you plague the land in darkness or rain down meteors, it's a result of your soul's harmonizing to tell the universe what to be.<br /> <br /> I can do that with any of the ChroD games. I cannot do that with Genius, because Genius is empty. It is &quot;People do Things and they Work until they Don't because Reasons.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T14:08:56-07:00","id":955165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955014#post955014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Credit where it's due, Gecko originally said it about Promethean. It just fit my opinion of Genius too well.<br /> <br /> I know, irony abounds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahahahahahahaha<br /> <br /> Hahahahahahahahaha<br /> <br /> Haha<br /> <br /> I'm sorry, but &quot;Genius is inspiration porn&quot; is what I'm going to think of whenever I need to smile on camera. This is my Bender moment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 08-21-2016, 05:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T14:14:23-07:00","id":955170,"title":"","content":"Once again, thanks for your contribution to my life. You're a gem. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T14:57:58-07:00","id":955206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955145#post955145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe the main problem wasn't that &quot;Mad Science isn't Science&quot;, but that the book doesn't say anything about what Mad Science is- it is not science, it is not magic, it is not some mad blessing of Chtulu or rainbow magic given by unicorn. It spends word count on saying what it's not instead on what it is. (I relay on Arc's review for this, considering I haven't read the book myself)</div> </div> </div> </div> There's a section &quot;The Nature of Inspiration&quot; where different groups present their theory. I'm sure Arc has a reason why that doesn't count, but a quick ctrl-f didn't find it on page 1.<br /> <br /> Still, I don't understand why it matters. Asking What Inspiration is is like asking what the Principle is. There might be an answer but you don't need it to tell the stories the game is designed for.<br /> <br /> I mean, we have no idea what the Spark in Girl Genius is, or why it lets Sparks warp reality (it's cannon that they warp reality - the novels are more explicit than the comic). It doesn't stop Girl Genius from being awesome.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955145#post955145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">again, haven't read the book, but it is a combination of having a full organization of mad individuals who simply can't work together which strains the suspension of disbelief together with the fact that it seems that Lemuria's oppression was, in general, a good thing and the the genii were the ones to ruin it (not to mention that the &quot;humanity should be controlled&quot; theme leaves a bad taste in the mouth)</div> </div> </div> </div> Lemuria used to have a leader group who's special powers let them work togeather (though the mechanics for it are massively underpowered)<br /> <br /> I've got no clue where the idea that their rulership was a good thing comes from. And there is no &quot;humanity should be controlled&quot; theme. There is a &quot;humanity cannot be controlled and even trying is foolish&quot; theme. Lemuria's control of humanity was either mostly a lie, or like Frankenstine's monster it rose up and turned against them. (Their goal was to recreate their homeland, it lasted 5 minuets before getting nuked. And it might have happened despite all their meddeling since in the origional timeline humanity didn't need to be controlled to create it). <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955145#post955145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">again, the problem seems to be that the game focus only on aesthetics without any content- it use &quot;science fetishism&quot; to cover a big hole which has nothing with it. Genii do nothing to create nothing and violate rules which aren't exist using a big nothing, with the only reason you could even say they are mad scientists is because they wear white robes and googles and scream &quot;SCIENCE!&quot; every now and then, making them into a caricature of themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly. That's like complaining that Awakening's Willworking is not &quot;magic&quot;. (I criticism I myself agree with, but I also understand the correct answer is to just play a different game with a different interpretation of magic.)<br /> <br /> This is not some shocking relivation that Arc has exposed after us fans overlooked it for years. It's stated outright in chapter one under The Broken Theory Law using the exact words &quot;Geniuses are not scientists&quot;.<br /> <br /> The mad scientist archetype is the victorian version of the wizard in his tower. Frankenstein was actually an alchemist not a scientist. The iconic wizard merlin was based on a Welsh bard. The more you examine the origins of the mad scientist archetype the clearer it is that mad scientists are a much older idea than even science itself.<br /> <br /> That's why geniuses don't do science. Not because the game lacks content, but because it uses the actual content of the mad scientist archetype, which isn't science.<br /> <br /> Instead it is the outsider perspective. The ability to look at what society considers certain fact and say &quot;no, this is not true, I can do better than that&quot;. The prophet who denies the existance of the old gods and teaches of the new is as much of a Genius as Frankenstein. The horror aspects of Genius draw more specifically from victorian to modern mad scientists.<br /> <br /> But at it's heart Genius is not about science. It's about Transgression.<br /> <br /> <br /> And you know, if that puts you off then that's fine. When I open a book about Mages I'm looking for Kaballah which has different mecahnics to witchcraft, which has different mechanics to hoodoo. Awakening isn't the mage game for me and that's fine.<br /> <br /> If you want science in your mad scientist game then Genius might not be the game for you. And that's also fine.<br /> <br /> <br /> But if you take Genius for what it is: A game about the people who challange old ideas, create new ones, then watch those ideas transform in ways they could never have convieved of (through a very thick layer of metaphor), it's not perfect but it does what it sets out to quite well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T15:26:25-07:00","id":955229,"title":"","content":"A Theory is not an assertion that this is the way the world works. A theory is a guess that may or may not be wrong.<br /> <br /> In this case, a theory is basically a way to say &quot;I don't want to commit to a vision of reality.&quot;<br /> <br /> A Genius has to be <i>something</i>. The game has a lot of ideas of what they <i>could be</i> but it never actually comes to <i>be anything</i>.<br /> <br /> And you can't put the transgression before the mad scientist when you are selling the mad scientist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T15:35:57-07:00","id":955238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955229#post955229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Theory is not an assertion that this is the way the world works. A theory is a guess that may or may not be wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, if you're talking about science, you've got it backwards. A guess that may or may not be wrong is called a Hypothesis. A Theory is an assertion of how the world appears to work based on all available evidence. Granted, it still allows for the possibility that new information could arise that refutes it, but until new information arises, a Theory is, in fact, an assertion that this is the way the world works.<br /> <br /> Some things that are Theories:<ul><li>Heliocentrism</li> <li>Evolution by Natural Selection</li> <li>Electromagnetism</li> <li>General Relativity</li> <li>Special Relativity</li> <li>Quantum Theory</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 08-21-2016, 06:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T15:37:49-07:00","id":955240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955206#post955206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">snipt</div> </div> </div> </div>considering that I personally haven't read Genius, and don't have a lot of interest at doing so (which is why I've mostly stayed out of this thread other than reading the review- which is just because readings reviews is an hobby of mine) I can't fairly discuss 90% percent of what you said- but there are two things with which I don't agree with you (which is kinda rare- I think that the last time I didn't agreed with you was somewhere in the old forums, with most chances that it was something about Witch Finders :P )<br /> <br /> The first point is that not giving an answer to how a Genius does things is ok- it's not. Now, I don't say that you have to have a definite answer. You may keep it as a mystery, but it needs to be defined somehow. If it isn't magic, and isn't science, and isn't some rainbow unicorn poop god- than what is it? If there are theories about the subject than I think its ok- things can be a mystery, because mystery creates stories. But if the Genii (I think this is the plural form. I saw people in the forums use it) don't even care about how what they do work- than all it gives you is a gaping hole in the middle of the game. You don't know what you do nor how you do it, and you don't really care. It makes it feel empty, and that kills stories. The Genii are, after all, supernatural creatures, and Mania is a supernatural energy and Inspiration is a supernatural Tolerance trait- it is ok for things to not make sense, but all of that juice comes from somewhere, and someone should try to investigate. It is better to have as many theories about the subject as there are Genii than having none.<br /> <br /> The point is, that is Arc is right, Genius suffer from a strong drive to not define itself, and there is a limit to how much interest one can have at something which is defined by being &quot;not it&quot;. Even the Principle is defined- it is the Principle, a power of change served by enigmatic beings called qashmalim. Genius, on the other hand, seem to be about people who do weird things and don't know why or how.<br /> <br /> Now, the main problem I have with &quot;Genius don't do science&quot; is this- they do science, perhaps even more than anyone else in the world.<br /> <br /> Science is not some sort of force, it is not some weird technique or way of action. Science is a way of thought- science, at its very base, is rising questions, which lead to experiments, which lead to new questions. Science, at its very core, works to disprove an existing theory by conducting an experiment. Science is not about death rays and mars colonies- it is about finding new information, making a theory and test it. In order for a Genius to not &quot;do science&quot;, he needs to not question anything, not seek after new subject to investigate, not make new theories about the world and not try to test them. Now, yes, it looks like the Genii has the ability to violate the normal rules of reality- but it doesn't mean they don't do science. It means that by being Inspired, they can disprove the laws which most of humanity- most of the universe- has to follow. They challenge the world itself, making the impossible into possible through the Mania which flows through their minds. The act of rising questions and seeking for answers is science- the constant doubt in your own theories is science. You don't &quot;do science&quot;- you &quot;think science&quot;, and as a scientist it kinda hurts me every time I read the words &quot;do science&quot; as if it is like &quot;doing magic&quot; or &quot;do miracles&quot;. If Genius do not do science, then what do they do? Building ray guns out of pure inspiration for no reason? That makes them sound kinda boring, as they don't actually do anything- just being used. That is the problem with science fetishism- when you look deep down, it is simply not that interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T15:40:12-07:00","id":955245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955238#post955238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, if you're talking about science, you've got it backwards. A guess that may or may not be wrong is called a Hypothesis. A Theory is an assertion of how the world appears to work based on all available evidence. Granted, it still allows for the possibility that new information could arise that refutes it, but until new information arises, a Theory is, in fact, an assertion that this is the way the world works.<br /> <br /> Things that are theories:<br /> Heliocentrism<br /> Evolution by Natural Selection<br /> Electromagnetism<br /> General Relativity<br /> Special Relativity<br /> Quantum Theory</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm speaking as it reads to people. Sure, I know that, and you know that, but Joe and Cledus who wander in from TvTropes might not. On top of that, even if these theories are supposed to explain Genius as people understand it right now, in the end it basically just ends up translating to....Nothing. There's no setting, there's no world, there's no rhyme or reason. There isn't a semblance of consistency.<br /> <br /> Which, again, is a <i>theme</i> but you need that theme to work against something in order to be effective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T15:46:10-07:00","id":955254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955240#post955240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, the main problem I have with &quot;Genius don't do science&quot; is this- they do science, perhaps even more than anyone else in the world.<br /> <br /> Science is not some sort of force, it is not some weird technique or way of action. Science is a way of thought- science, at its very base, is rising questions, which lead to experiments, which lead to new questions. Science, at its very core, works to disprove an existing theory by conducting an experiment. Science is not about death rays and mars colonies- it is about finding new information, making a theory and test it. In order for a Genius to not &quot;do science&quot;, he needs to not question anything, not seek after new subject to investigate, not make new theories about the world and not try to test them. Now, yes, it looks like the Genii has the ability to violate the normal rules of reality- but it doesn't mean they don't do science. It means that by being Inspired, they can disprove the laws which most of humanity- most of the universe- has to follow. They challenge the world itself, making the impossible into possible through the Mania which flows through their minds. The act of rising questions and seeking for answers is science- the constant doubt in your own theories is science. You don't &quot;do science&quot;- you &quot;think science&quot;, and as a scientist it kinda hurts me every time I read the words &quot;do science&quot; as if it is like &quot;doing magic&quot; or &quot;do miracles&quot;. If Genius do not do science, then what do they do? Building ray guns out of pure inspiration for no reason? That makes them sound kinda boring, as they don't actually do anything- just being used. That is the problem with science fetishism- when you look deep down, it is simply not that interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is actually why I favor them committing to it, and why I get super frustrated when the game tells me that whatever it is they are doing, it's not science or the use of things grounded in natural laws we just don't understand yet. It' so super easy to go and exploit that angle, and yet the game <i>doesn't</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T15:50:01-07:00","id":955256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955157#post955157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is &quot;People do Things and they Work until they Don't because Reasons.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure that one was me.<br /> <br /> No, I checked. You said it TO me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":3093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","user":"hm8453a","date":". 08-21-2016, 06:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T16:06:31-07:00","id":955263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955256#post955256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pretty sure that one was me.<br /> <br /> No, I checked. You said it TO me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I said it to everyone. It is not a unique comment. It is my number one problem with the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T16:08:44-07:00","id":955264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955254#post955254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is actually why I favor them committing to it, and why I get super frustrated when the game tells me that whatever it is they are doing, it's not science or the use of things grounded in natural laws we just don't understand yet. It' so super easy to go and exploit that angle, and yet the game <i>doesn't</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>actually, I think it is even ok for Genius to not have their abilities grounded around natural laws, understood or otherwise- they are supernatural beings, after all. Doing the impossible is in theme for them. But if thanks to Inspiration they have to ability to bend or even break the natural laws, than the game needs to at least investigate the nature of Inspiration and how it interacts with the natural laws of the universe.<br /> <br /> Mummies throw meteors on people and no one bats an eye. Genius build anti gravity skateboards and everyone loses their minds. The reason for that seems to be the main problem at the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T16:12:08-07:00","id":955266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955264#post955264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">actually, I think it is even ok for Genius to not have their abilities grounded around natural laws, understood or otherwise- they are supernatural beings, after all. Doing the impossible is in theme for them. But if thanks to Inspiration they have to ability to bend or even break the natural laws, than the game needs to at least investigate the nature of Inspiration and how it interacts with the natural laws of the universe.<br /> <br /> Mummies throw meteors on people and no one bats an eye. Genius build anti gravity skateboards and everyone loses their minds. The reason for that seems to be the main problem at the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seriously. Rainbow Unicorn Poop God, It's crap, but I'll take that over no explanation at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T16:16:10-07:00","id":955268,"title":"","content":"Hm, I might add some more to Mage: The Transgression about how Mania and the Abyss operate and allow Mages to do what they do, keeping the &quot;genius doesn't explain how geniuses do stuff&quot; complaint in mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T16:36:52-07:00","id":955279,"title":"","content":"Have you read Austin Grossman's &quot;Soon I Will Be Invincible&quot;? The treatment of the mad scientist character is very similar to Genius, and even more similar when it comes to what the review is complaining about. &quot;I was going to declare war on the world, and I was going to lose.&quot; Just having the same ideas come up in a book isn't any guarantee of quality, but if Grossman independently created something so similar, there must be a coherent archetype that they're both working off.<br /> \u200bAs for my overall opinion of Genius, the backstory and setting is incoherent, the whole Masquerade bit works awkwardly with the effects of Wonders, the Axioms are a little clunky but pretty decent, and the Catalysts are pure gold. If I was making a revised edition I'd say the first Genius appeared on November 8, 1895, and that Genii PCs are supposed to break any Masquerade and shake up the status quo. Genius: The Disruption.<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1430-gareth3","name":"Gareth3","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T17:01:05-07:00","id":955301,"title":"","content":"Actually, that discussion on how Science is way of thought gives me an idea on how to make Lemuria better;<br /> <br /> Make it so they're not insane. They're pseudo-scientists who operate off of their ability to twist facts to suit their pet theories. In bare bones, that isn't different from what they are now, but rather than organizing for no good reason/being people who literally can't comprehend things outside their worldview, they organize themselves around whatever One Perfect Theory is shared among the Baramin, while fundamentally agreeing on the general idea that said theories fit in the Theory of Everything they haven't found yet. There's a point to be made about <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crank_(person)#Crank_magnetism\" target=\"_blank\">crank magnetism</a> here-they don't work together because they have some weird authorial mandate there must be a faction, they work together because everyone else thinks they're ridiculous when they're not outright repulsive-misery loves company.<br /> <br /> Of course, this also means Lemurians are far less organized (could be that they aren't even a proper group, it's just a term the Peerage came up with to describe the Geniuses even other mad scientists think are cranks-see the actual theory of Lemuria), but that's kind of the point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T17:34:10-07:00","id":955316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955206#post955206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've got no clue where the idea that their rulership was a good thing comes from. And there is no &quot;humanity should be controlled&quot; theme. There is a &quot;humanity cannot be controlled and even trying is foolish&quot; theme. Lemuria's control of humanity was either mostly a lie, or like Frankenstine's monster it rose up and turned against them. (Their goal was to recreate their homeland, it lasted 5 minuets before getting nuked. And it might have happened despite all their meddeling since in the origional timeline humanity didn't need to be controlled to create it).</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see where the idea come from. Paired with the &quot;humanity cannot be controlled and even trying is foolish&quot; theme is the undercurrent about the bitterness (and yes, even bitter disappointment) Geniuses have towards that fact that occasionally runs through the text.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Genius the Transgression, pg 35-36, No One is in Charge</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">That, say many Inspired, is why we didn't get the future with the flying cars and the &quot;televisors&quot; and the moon bases: those things were in the works, all set for the Lemurians to hand them down to us like manna from heaven, and we were supposed to accept them and let our betters maintain them while we lived our happy, comfortable lives. But Lemuria got its ass kicked, and has your life ever been comfortable? It hasn't, say many in the Peerage, because humanity is off the rails, free from control or intellectual extortion.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Peerage don't technically regret freeing Earth from what control Lemuria had (a fact better emphasized later), but they're technologists of a sort and their attitude in this paragraph can come off as &quot;Freedom is why our level of technology (which, you'll notice, is tied into happiness and comfort by the Peerage) isn't what it 'should' be.&quot;<br /> <br /> It may be foolish to control humanity, but at the same time I feel the game can easily appeal to those who want to make Geniuses who think they can &quot;do better&quot; or who feel they they have the right to build superscience at the expense of what it does to society. Three of the catalysts - Grimm, Hoffnung, and Neid - are all on some level about imposing your will directly on other people. And I admit that certain Axioms appealed to me on that level. I don't think it's a wrong thing to explore necessarily, and Obligation and Lemuria can help provide balance if used well, but setting a tone that &quot;Your attempts to change mortal society won't work, mostly because mortals won't get it, and that <i>sucks,</i>&quot; can go into some weird places if the GM doesn't have a firm grasp on the Chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8064-mp122984","name":"mp122984","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T17:40:59-07:00","id":955322,"title":"","content":"How you frame and present a thing matters. Coherency is a thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T20:38:51-07:00","id":955385,"title":"","content":"I'm reminded of my reaction to watching the movie <i>Limitless</i>. The main character gets super-intelligence and repeatedly talks about how much good he can use it for, while other characters warn him about potential side effects of his condition and the dangers of hubris. Then the movie ends with him hand waving all the potential obstacles and consequences having pursued nothing but selfish goals. <br /> <br /> Also, I aspire to one day have &quot;Failing upwards into violation&quot; as my epitaph.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T20:57:59-07:00","id":955398,"title":"","content":"I will admit that the idea of a Chaos-Theory enhanced, Butterfly-Powered Hurricane Projector is an amusing one. It just seems a little gonzo for the world of darkness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T21:00:30-07:00","id":955402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955385#post955385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm reminded of my reaction to watching the movie <i>Limitless</i>. The main character gets super-intelligence and repeatedly talks about how much good he can use it for, while other characters warn him about potential side effects of his condition and the dangers of hubris. Then the movie ends with him hand waving all the potential obstacles and consequences having pursued nothing but selfish goals.<br /> <br /> Also, I aspire to one day have &quot;Failing upwards into violation&quot; as my epitaph.</div> </div> </div> </div>And then the sequel series almost perfectly segues into Deviant.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TidyGamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955398#post955398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will admit that the idea of a Chaos-Theory enhanced, Butterfly-Powered Hurricane Projector is an amusing one. It just seems a little gonzo for the world of darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see we both read SMBC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T21:23:02-07:00","id":955406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955402#post955402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see we both read SMBC.</div> </div> </div> </div>I won't deny it. The Weather Gun idea is actually <i>less</i> gonzo than a Retroviral Genetic Engineering Process that transfers the weather manipulation powers of the Peruvian Fractal Butterfly (who's wings have infinite length compressed into a very small surface area) to himself. But the point stands that the Enlightened Lepidopterist-Adventurer just doesn't seem to really fit into the horror <i>milieu</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T21:23:32-07:00","id":955407,"title":"","content":"It must be stated that it's kind of clear that Genius wants a certain amount of gonzo in it, and that's cool and everything, so long as it doesn't cost me the suspension of my disbelief. Gotta have so horror with your slapstick, you know-can't beat Nosferatu without Charlie Chaplin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T21:41:32-07:00","id":955418,"title":"","content":"Yeah but how do you import the horror into the genius experience? A Genius who harvests the brains of the recently dead to act as brains for her robot army is obviously prime NPC genius horror, it's Frankenstein with chrome details. So is building a ancient crystal necklace that turns you into a psychic vampire with mind control powers, or a time machine that's powered by a forsaken child, or a ray gun that shoots memory rays at it's targets that forces them to relive the most traumatic memories of their lives. But none of that is necessary, you can easily have shiny gluten-free,cruelty-free vegan tech, from what I can recall.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T00:17:51-07:00","id":955462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TidyGamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955418#post955418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah but how do you import the horror into the genius experience?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think this is the right question to ask. I think you first need to answer, &quot;Why do I want horror in my Genius experience?&quot;<br /> <br /> Because maybe you don't, and trying to import horror is the entirely wrong thing to do in the first place, and it would be good to know that before you crowbar something inappropriate into the game.<br /> <br /> Because maybe you do, but now you know <i>exactly</i> what's missing, rather than a vague genre-type that doesn't mean anything standing on its own, so you can usefully try different things to see if they successfully bring that missing piece in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T02:48:48-07:00","id":955492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955229#post955229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And you can't put the transgression before the mad scientist when you are selling the mad scientist.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;You can't put Gnosticism before the mage when you're selling the mage&quot;.<br /> <br /> From my point of view that's exactly what Awakened does. It's not a problem, it just means Awakened isn't the game for me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955240#post955240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> but there are two things with which I don't agree with you (which is kinda rare- I think that the last time I didn't agreed with you was somewhere in the old forums, with most chances that it was something about Witch Finders :P )</div> </div> </div> </div> Only two? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (I think the Witch Finders thing was this forum)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955240#post955240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You may keep it as a mystery, but it needs to be defined somehow. If it isn't magic, and isn't science, and isn't some rainbow unicorn poop god- than what is it? If there are theories about the subject than I think its ok- things can be a mystery, because mystery creates stories.</div> </div> </div> </div> So far so good, six possible explenations are presented. Which, if any, of them is true is left as a mystery.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955240#post955240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> But if the Genii (I think this is the plural form. I saw people in the forums use it) don't even care about how what they do work- than all it gives you is a gaping hole in the middle of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Geniuses do care about it. Just like there's plenty of Werewolves who care what happened to Father Wolf and Promethians who want to know what, exactly, the Principal is.<br /> <br /> Most Geniuses have accepted that they won't ever discover the truth, just like most Promethians accept they won't figure out the Principal. But that doesn't mean they don't <i>care</i>.<br /> <br /> Incidentally if they ever did figure it out they'd probably hit the equivalent of Archmastery. There is a 9th Axiom that controls Inspiration itself. Nobody knows how to use it and most Peers think it's just a myth, but Moochava has said it's real. If anything would let a Genius learn it, discovering what exactly Inspiration is would do it.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for the plural it's actually addressed in the game. Both Geniuses and Genii are acceptable. Geniuses is the more commonly used plural by the Inspired; while people who use correct Latin plurals like Genii are stereotypically old (being educated in a time where Latin was on the curriculum), or obsessive.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955240#post955240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Science is not some sort of force, it is not some weird technique or way of action. Science is a way of thought- science, at its very base, is rising questions, which lead to experiments, which lead to new questions. Science, at its very core, works to disprove an existing theory by conducting an experiment.</div> </div> </div> </div> While I mostly agree with you, I think you need to add a little something to that definition.<br /> <br /> Lets say I wanted to disprove the theory &quot;the earth is round&quot; so I conduct an experiment. I take a ball, I put it on the ground, I observe that the ball is not rolling away, so I conclude the Earth is flat. I certainly did an experiment to disprove an existing theory, but I wouldn't call it &quot;science&quot;.<br /> <br /> I'd say that to define science you need to add a couple of things: A minimum level of competence. A spirit of trust and collaboration whereby scientists share their work and let others peer review or build upon it.<br /> <br /> It's those additional criteria which disqualify a genius from being a scientist.<br /> <br /> <br /> They do experiments to disprove theories and hypothesizes. But they're not particularly competent at it (a good Scholastic could be competent). A Genius jumps to conclusions, makes basic maths errors, ignores basic precautions to keep the test subjects uncontaminated. And they don't even realize they're doing it.<br /> <br /> And that's assuming that they don't accidentally contaminate their experiment with Inspiration - it's entirely possible that a Genius trying to test the boiling point of water will accidentally come up with an innovative new heater that boils water at 80 degrees instead of 100. <hr />Now I'm not saying a Genius doesn't do anything at all. They can't just grab whatever chemicals are close to hand and mix them and suddenly have a bomb. Building wonders requires research, testing, trial runs, etc. Dots in mundane skills like Science or Medicine are a vital component of both Wonder building and Wonder use.<br /> <br /> I'm just saying that a Genius' experiments and the mental state of being a Genius are not good tools for disproving a hypothesis or theory; whether that theory is about mundane science or the supernatural.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gareth3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955279#post955279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you read Austin Grossman's &quot;Soon I Will Be Invincible&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div> I have, and I love that book.<br /> <br /> It's a great example of how you can have a great story even when failure is inevitable. Not perfect by any means, it has a lot of first-novel-errors, but it's good.<br /> <br /> Also I know some people really hate it, I would be interested to know if Arc is one of them actually.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gareth3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955279#post955279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The treatment of the mad scientist character is very similar to Genius, and even more similar when it comes to what the review is complaining about. &quot;I was going to declare war on the world, and I was going to lose.&quot; Just having the same ideas come up in a book isn't any guarantee of quality, but if Grossman independently created something so similar, there must be a coherent archetype that they're both working off.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 08-22-2016, 06:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T03:10:28-07:00","id":955499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955492#post955492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...but Moochava has said it's real.</div> </div> </div> </div>This counter-argument is fairly annoying.<br /> <br /> What Moochava said, if it isn't in the book, or isn't in some collected errata, or whatever, is meaningless to reviewing the game-as-written. How is someone that has no idea where to find all these posts/etc. Moochava has made in various places supposed to judge Genius when they read it as if they did?<br /> <br /> If there's all this wisdom from Moochava that fixes various flaws in the game, but isn't in the game, it does nothing to help people appreciate the game when they read it.<br /> <br /> This sort of thing doesn't prove Genius isn't what people are reading it as being. It proves that it needs to be fixed by going back in and changing stuff so people know what it's supposed to be instead of what it says.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And they don't even realise they're doing it. </div> </div> </div>How is this a selling point though?<br /> <br /> &quot;Genii don't do science because Inspiration makes them incapable of it on a mental deficiency level.&quot; They can't even be horrified by their inability to do science any more because they're too Inspiration-stupid to even realize that what they're doing is meaningless nonsense.<br /> <br /> And, of course, the text takes it further than this by saying that Genii have avoided major scientific events because they don't just mess things up personally; them being around is a risk to real science happening effectively.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T03:14:09-07:00","id":955500,"title":"","content":"SIWBI even has an exhaustive census of the superpowered population of Earth on the first page, going into even more detail than Genius.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1430,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1430-gareth3","user":"Gareth3","date":". 08-22-2016, 06:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1430-gareth3","name":"Gareth3","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T03:21:08-07:00","id":955502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955499#post955499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How is this a selling point though?<br /> <br /> &quot;Genii don't do science because Inspiration makes them incapable of it on a mental deficiency level.&quot; They can't even be horrified by their inability to do science any more because they're too Inspiration-stupid to even realize that what they're doing is meaningless nonsense.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is not what I meant. Geniuses are very aware and frequently horrified that they cannot do science.<br /> <br /> It's basically the same as Girl Genius' Sparks who enter &quot;the madness place&quot; when they're working. But when they stop working and leave the madness place they're very aware of their inability to do science. Roleplaying the madness place is great fun too.<br /> <br /> [edit] As Second Chances points out I phrased this really badly. Sparks can work outside the madness place. Geniuses cannot.<br /> <br /> (The obscure Austrialian kids tv show Wicked Science would probably be a better example - it uses a more subtle distinction between being in the madness place being outside it.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 08-22-2016, 01:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T09:21:27-07:00","id":955641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955502#post955502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is not what I meant. Geniuses are very aware and frequently horrified that they cannot do science.<br /> <br /> It's basically the same as Girl Genius' Sparks who enter &quot;the madness place&quot; when they're working. But when they stop working and leave the madness place they're very aware of their inability to do science. Roleplaying the madness place is great fun too.<br /> <br /> (The obscure Austrialian kids tv show Wicked Science would probably be a better example - it uses a more subtle distinction between being in the madness place being outside it.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I call (respectfully) call BS. Sparks are fully able to do science outside of the Madness Place. Agatha is unable to do science at the start of the story because of the retraining but other sparks research all the time without going into the Madness Place. It just allows the to work faster and bend the laws of reality. Or flats out break them if they can Heterodyne. When they aren't in Madness? They work on mad science at a regular pace. That doesn't mean they are all good scientists, but the Spark isn't what stop them. Otherwise Klaus wouldn't have been nearly as calm when trying to vivisect Othar (although I'm sure he would have enjoyed it just as much).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T09:42:26-07:00","id":955648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955641#post955641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I call (respectfully) call BS. Sparks are fully able to do science outside of the Madness Place. Agatha is unable to do science at the start of the story because of the retraining but other sparks research all the time without going into the Madness Place. It just allows the to work faster and bend the laws of reality. Or flats out break them if they can Heterodyne. When they aren't in Madness? They work on mad science at a regular pace. That doesn't mean they are all good scientists, but the Spark isn't what stop them. Otherwise Klaus wouldn't have been nearly as calm when trying to vivisect Othar (although I'm sure he would have enjoyed it just as much).</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, that works for a steampunk fantasy story, but having mad scientists only able to do mad science in &quot;the madness place&quot; is pretty fitting for a horror setting. <br /> <br /> People, including our friend with the incredibly appropriate icon, are saying that they don't see the horror because Geniuses can do mad science that doesn't involve stealing people's brains, but A. The rules make unethical mad science more powerful (Larva), and B. The horror isn't just about what the mad scientist does, it's what they are. It's a personal horror game, after all. <br /> <br /> The personal horror is something slightly similar to Awakening, but Genius does it way better. Devs have defended the horror potential of the Supernal by saying that it's scary because Mages see it and can never return and so on, but Geniuses have that even worse: they see beautiful visions of what the world could be, but these visions were never there in the first place, aren't even in any way real, and can't even be shared. To give an example: I'm working on an original fantasy tabletop rpg. Imagine that I became so obsessed with it, so obsessively singlemindedly fixated that I wished with every fiber of my being that it could be real and that reality could really work like that. Now imagine I wished so hard that I pulled some supernatural force into myself and broke some part of me, basically turning me into a localized wound in reality centered on my fantasy setting. Now I can temporarily make reality obey my rules, I can make things work the way they would in my fantasy world. The problem is, I can't not do that. The way I perceive and interact with the world is permanently locked into the lens of that fantasy. I can't build things or discover things or research things as they are, I can only do those things by forcing them into the worldview of my setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T09:59:54-07:00","id":955654,"title":"","content":"And about the futility thing, MtT is going to work on that, but not as much as you might want. Because most of the ChroD games are pretty damn futile. In Vampire, becoming human again is as remote a possibility as Pankosmoi. In Werewolf, you're not going to end the war you're stuck in. In Mage...well, for all the gnostic bluster about freeing the world, you're probably not going to accomplish shit, less even than the other lines. And Dave has said it's anti-transhumanist, so a Mage who wants to cure all diseases or make people immortal or create artificial wombs or a perfect method of transition is shit out of luck. And so on. But what the games do (especially Changeling, Hunter. Mummy, and Demon, my loves) is that they make it clear that you can strive for personal victories. <br /> <br /> So, in Mage: The Transgression, the players probably can't get rid of Paradox or take over the world or make it so that no one ever Catalyzes again. But you can still try to do stuff and fix things and defend people, and you can succeed in it. You might not, and you might have to pay a terrible price, but you can still do things where you can say to yourself that you accomplished something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 08-22-2016, 01:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T10:12:47-07:00","id":955660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955654#post955654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, in Mage: The Transgression, the players probably can't get rid of Paradox or take over the world or make it so that no one ever Catalyzes again. But you can protect one neighborhood of city from the Abyss or an Unmada, and it's emphasized that that's worth doing- you saved lives, and you saved the fabric of reality from taking another hit.</div> </div> </div> </div>But it's a horror game, not a magical superheroes game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T10:15:51-07:00","id":955662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955660#post955660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But it's a horror game, not a magical superheroes game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yeah, it's still that, but you have to emphasize that players can actually sometimes do positive things, or else not many people will want to play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T10:18:49-07:00","id":955665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955641#post955641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I call (respectfully) call BS. Sparks are fully able to do science outside of the Madness Place. Agatha is unable to do science at the start of the story because of the retraining but other sparks research all the time without going into the Madness Place. It just allows the to work faster and bend the laws of reality. Or flats out break them if they can Heterodyne. When they aren't in Madness? They work on mad science at a regular pace. That doesn't mean they are all good scientists, but the Spark isn't what stop them. Otherwise Klaus wouldn't have been nearly as calm when trying to vivisect Othar (although I'm sure he would have enjoyed it just as much).</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right, I said that badly. Sparks can do work outside the madness place.<br /> <br /> However Geniuses cannot. If they're building a wonder or doing an experiment then they will enter the madness place. It's only when they stop working that they can look back with clarity and realise that actually those equations are full of basic errors.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955660#post955660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it's a horror game, not a magical superheroes game.</div> </div> </div> </div>How many times have people pointed to Batman as an example of a Beast? There's plenty of horror to be found in superheroes if you look at it right.<br /> <br /> Genius' interpretation of Batman would focus on the emotional toll of him realising how little effect his long crusade actually had on Gotham. Batman vs Superman focused heavily on this angle, with the realisation causing an increasing slide into brutality and paranoia. I won't say the movie is great, but it's portrayal of Batman is basically a WoD charachter through and through.<br /> <br /> <br /> Plus. Princess dev and proud of it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 08-22-2016, 01:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T10:35:50-07:00","id":955679,"title":"","content":"I mean, I'm definitely on board with guarding against magical superheroism. It's why I'm remaking Mage and why Princess is just...well, I'm trying to be less negative so I'm not going to say anything on that matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T10:37:09-07:00","id":955682,"title":"","content":"If you don't see why Princess is horror I recommend reading Sailor Nothing. But lets not get too sidetracked.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T10:37:41-07:00","id":955684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955660#post955660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it's a horror game, not a magical superheroes game.</div> </div> </div> </div> To be fair, there is a bit of superhero undercurrent in Mage: the Awakening. One of the themes (The World is a Lie) is all about fighting the evil magical tyrants that secretly rule the world. That sounds a lot like a standard issue superhero theme to me. And the horror comes from your abuse of said power over mundanes, which is quite a common theme in comic books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T10:42:03-07:00","id":955688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955684#post955684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> To be fair, there is a bit of superhero undercurrent in Mage: the Awakening. One of the themes (The World is a Lie) is all about fighting the evil magical tyrants that secretly rule the world. That sounds a lot like a standard issue superhero theme to me. And the horror comes from your abuse of said power over mundanes, which is quite a common theme in comic books.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the same themes, with a different tone depending on the genre. Political dramas also tend to have those themes, with yet a different tone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T10:42:03-07:00","id":955689,"title":"","content":"I mean, considering that that's why I'm remaking Mage, I can totally see that objection, and Hayley's comment is a good reminder to be on guard for it. <br /> <br /> And just because you can interpret something as horror doesn't mean it's a horror archetype. You can interpret superheroes as monstrous or use them for horror, but they aren't a kind of monster or horror archetype. &quot;Dangerous vigilante&quot; is the horror equivalent, and ChroD has that very well covered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T10:43:32-07:00","id":955690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955684#post955684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> To be fair, there is a bit of superhero undercurrent in Mage: the Awakening. One of the themes (The World is a Lie) is all about fighting the evil magical tyrants that secretly rule the world. That sounds a lot like a standard issue superhero theme to me. And the horror comes from your abuse of said power over mundanes, which is quite a common theme in comic books.</div> </div> </div> </div>And thinking about it. DaveB's Soul Cage is a good example of this. It was very superhero/pulp at times. Indiana Jonesing through a lost temple. A climatic showdown involving motorbiking up the side of a collapsing tower while an army of the dead stand ready to invade the supernal.<br /> <br /> Not a criticism btw. I love the soul cage, I wouldn't say it ever horrified me, but it was very very good. It's better than most Dresden Files IMO.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955689#post955689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And just because you can interpret something as horror doesn't mean it's a horror archetype. You can interpret superheroes as monstrous or use them for horror, but they aren't a kind of monster or horror archetype. &quot;Dangerous vigilante&quot; is the horror equivalent, and ChroD has that very well covered.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh. You're factually correct, but why does it matter?<br /> <br /> If it's good horror it's good horror. Why does it matter if the WoD is the first to do it or the latest in a long line?<br /> <br /> <br /> Also. Could you not call Father Lankester Merrin (from The Exorcist) a superhero? He has strange and unusual powers (exorcism) which he uses to fight evil with equally strange and unusual powers. Eleven from Stranger Things is one costume away from being a superhero.<br /> <br /> Superheros are more a setting than a type of charachter. And the type of charachter who populates the superhero setting has analogues in works of horror.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 08-22-2016, 01:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T10:53:00-07:00","id":955701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955688#post955688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's the same themes, with a different tone depending on the genre. Political dramas also tend to have those themes, with yet a different tone.</div> </div> </div> </div> Or perhaps we should just go and admit that the superhero genre is not mutually exclusive with the horror genre. Using &quot;it's a horror game, not a magical superheroes game!&quot; is a flawed excuse because of the fact we have a game that is both. <br /> <br /> I find that using it as a way to discredit someone else's example is extremely problematic because its arbitrarily deciding what is or is not horror for different people.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955690#post955690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And thinking about it.</div> </div> </div> </div> True; that door swings both ways.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T10:53:25-07:00","id":955702,"title":"","content":"There's good horror and there's horror that's resonant and archetypal enough to hold up an entire line. But again, we're getting offtopic. <br /> <br /> To bring it back to Genius, that vision of ChroD is why I and others have pushed for it to be considered canon-caliber: because the mad scientist is such a prominent and rich archetype that it deserves an entire line. Mummies have an entire line, after all, so why not mad scientists? Mad scientists have been in more horror movies than werewolves and mummies put together. They're horror royalty. Why do you think the Monster Mash is sung from the perspective of one of them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T11:03:38-07:00","id":955713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955702#post955702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's good horror and there's horror that's resonant and archetypal enough to hold up an entire line. But again, we're getting offtopic.<br /> <br /> To bring it back to Genius, that vision of ChroD is why I and others have pushed for it to be considered canon-caliber: because the mad scientist is such a prominent and rich archetype that it deserves an entire line. Mummies have an entire line, after all, so why not mad scientists? Mad scientists have been in more horror movies than werewolves and mummies put together. They're horror royalty. Why do you think the Monster Mash is sung from the perspective of one of them?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I sent MCN a private message so we could continue the conversation without derailing this thread, which I definitely started to do. Sorry, everyone!<br /> <br /> I don't have any problem with there being a line for the mad science archetype. I just don't think Genius does a good job of it, as is. I think that's the main argument a lot of us are making about Genius here, is that whether or not we can see ourselves playing whatever game it was, we recognize that there's a place for a mad science game, we just don't like the way Genius approaches it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T11:08:43-07:00","id":955714,"title":"","content":"Here's a question for you. If you did a mad science line of your own, would you define &quot;mad scientist&quot; as, essentially, originating with Frankenstein?<br /> <br /> Or would you define &quot;mad scientist&quot; so that it includes the various archetypes that Frankenstein is descended from: The mad alchemists, cave dwelling hermit gurus, prophets, etc.<br /> <br /> <br /> There's no right or wrong answer. This is definitely a personal preference thing. I'm just curious what you'd choose and why.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T11:16:21-07:00","id":955715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955714#post955714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a question for you. If you did a mad science line of your own, would you define &amp;quot;mad scientist&amp;quot; as, essentially, originating with Frankenstein?<br /> <br /> Or would you define &amp;quot;mad scientist&amp;quot; so that it includes the various archetypes that Frankenstein is descended from: The mad alchemists, cave dwelling hermit gurus, prophets, etc.<br /> <br /> <br /> There's no right or wrong answer. This is definitely a personal preference thing. I'm just curious what you'd choose and why.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm doing the second. That's why I'm remaking Mage to deal with wizards and mad scientists- because the &quot;mage as monster&quot; archetype is pretty much indistinguishable from the &quot;mad scientist as monster archetype&quot;.<br /> <br /> And the places where I think Genius doesn't do a good job are mostly mechanical, honestly. The Wonder mechanics are pretty clunky, as are some others. There are some other things that don't work, but overall the fluff and tone have always been fantastic to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T11:16:42-07:00","id":955716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955714#post955714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a question for you. If you did a mad science line of your own, would you define &quot;mad scientist&quot; as, essentially, originating with Frankenstein?<br /> <br /> Or would you define &quot;mad scientist&quot; so that it includes the various archetypes that Frankenstein is descended from: The mad alchemists, cave dwelling hermit gurus, prophets, etc.<br /> <br /> <br /> There's no right or wrong answer. This is definitely a personal preference thing. I'm just curious what you'd choose and why.</div> </div> </div> </div>No worries at all! <br /> <br /> My areas of interest, professionally, are so recent that a lot of my field would joke that they're not history. I focus primarily on intersections of gender and class and conceptions of childhood in North America in the 17th and 18th centuries for my day job. But I've also done a lot of much earlier work. My undergraduate adviser was an historian on Anglo-Saxon and Anglo-Norman ecclesiastical and political culture, manuscript production, and the Domesday survey, and as an undergrad, I assisted her in teaching a Viking World class. I've always been extremely interested in roots, and I would definitely not define mad science as having started with <i>Frankenstein.</i><br /> <br /> (I'm going to leave it at that until you ask more questions, I'm trying to keep myself from always starting to lecture outside class settings. Sorryyyyy I know I tend to do that.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T11:17:16-07:00","id":955717,"title":"","content":"(I just realized you might have been talking to Gecko, not me. I'm sorry if you were!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T11:20:23-07:00","id":955722,"title":"","content":"I was talking to you Hayley. (You ninjaed me. Writing a reply now)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955715#post955715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the places where I think Genius doesn't do a good job are mostly mechanical, honestly. The Wonder mechanics are pretty clunky, as are some others. There are some other things that don't work, but overall the fluff and tone have always been fantastic to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. The Wonder mechanics could use a touch up. My biggest complaint about them is how similar various wonders appear. A radiation beam is very similar to a heat ray. A nanotech healer is very similar to a orgone healer.<br /> <br /> Ultimately there's not many ways to fill or empty health boxes; but if you're interested ask me about it on the Genius 2E thread and I'll explain how I plan to mitigate that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T11:20:24-07:00","id":955723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955702#post955702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's good horror and there's horror that's resonant and archetypal enough to hold up an entire line. But again, we're getting offtopic.<br /> <br /> To bring it back to Genius, that vision of ChroD is why I and others have pushed for it to be considered canon-caliber: because the mad scientist is such a prominent and rich archetype that it deserves an entire line. Mummies have an entire line, after all, so why not mad scientists? Mad scientists have been in more horror movies than werewolves and mummies put together. They're horror royalty. Why do you think the Monster Mash is sung from the perspective of one of them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Taking a hugely popular concept is actually a pretty bad reason to build something fresh for it, unless you're subverting the basic conceits somehow, which has its own pitfalls and obstacles to be overcome. Because, while you have a wonderfully rich and varied palette to design from, you're also painfully beholden to those predecessors and it's going to be impossible to serve them all.<br /> <br /> As has been noted many times, part of the threshold after which Werewolf or Mummy or Mage works is when you've intentionally discarded the presumptions that you're going to play something from the popular cultural canon and actually engage with the text <i>as written</i>, rather than as you wish it to be. Trying to play a movie-mummy or movie-werewolf or, I dunno, Gandalf, using CofD game lines is a recipe for disappointment. You can have them, but the rules aren't built for that and shouldn't have been: instead of merely trying to imitate, they've generated something that's somewhat original, even if it has clear inspirations.<br /> <br /> So, don't. Don't try to sell people on playing mad scientists from popular culture in Genius. Try to find the core of mad science as a concept and then build something new around it. Spend less time justifying everything and more time <i>making</i> something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T11:25:49-07:00","id":955734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955723#post955723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Try to find the core of mad science as a concept and then build something new around it. Spend less time justifying everything and more time <i>making</i> something.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've already tried to tell you this elsewhere, Gecko, but yeah, echoing how important it is. You know your subject. Now find your theme, and build a game cohesively around that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T11:26:48-07:00","id":955735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955716#post955716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(I'm going to leave it at that until you ask more questions, I'm trying to keep myself from always starting to lecture outside class settings. Sorryyyyy I know I tend to do that.)</div> </div> </div> </div>The obvious follow up question is, in that case how would you define &quot;mad scientist&quot;?<br /> <br /> I mean that both thematically and in terms of how their powers work. As in, I'm not sure you could &quot;double down on the science&quot; and include the &quot;Irish Wild Man&quot; archetype at the same time. (assuming you want to double down on the science in the first place).<br /> <br /> Feel free to lecture away as much as you like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T11:28:03-07:00","id":955736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955714#post955714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a question for you. If you did a mad science line of your own, would you define &amp;quot;mad scientist&amp;quot; as, essentially, originating with Frankenstein?<br /> <br /> Or would you define &amp;quot;mad scientist&amp;quot; so that it includes the various archetypes that Frankenstein is descended from: The mad alchemists, cave dwelling hermit gurus, prophets, etc.<br /> <br /> <br /> There's no right or wrong answer. This is definitely a personal preference thing. I'm just curious what you'd choose and why.</div> </div> </div> </div>Victor is the core, easily. <br /> <br /> Having studied the history of science, religion, and philosophy, alchemists are to me much closer to the archetype of a real scientist than to that of the mad scientist. You can play them that way, but that reflects the mystical aspects of their practice being cooped into fiction than what they actually practiced. As for prophets and gurus, I think I see where you are going in suggesting them as mad scientists, namely at they operate on the premise of inspiration, but I would say that it is the opposite type of inspiration of that of the mad scientist. Much like the Whirling Dervish Sufis, they are inspired in the moment through ecstasy or repetitive unthinking action. Contrast that with the academic Sufi, who achieves inspiration through careful learning and though. You can play prophets that way, but again, that is not the core of what a mad scientist is. The mad scientist lies between the two type, and while I think a mad scientist line should be able to encompass all of those ideas, the alchemist and the prophet would lie distinctly in the fringes of what that line is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T11:41:46-07:00","id":955752,"title":"","content":"A very different viewpoint to my own <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4433_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4433\" data-vbnamecard=\"4433\">Second Chances</a> (which makes your post interesting <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> <br /> Correct me if I'm wrong, but you're definining mad science by a particular mode of thought.<br /> <br /> To me the core is now how they think, but what kind of thoughts they're thinking. In short: Transgression. So in contrast to you, the guy who eats a bucket full of mushrooms and suddenly writes the communist manifesto (or challenges the old testament by writing the new testament) is more or less equivalent to the guy who carefully reads history, philosophy, economics, and then writes the communist manifesto. They both look at society, and what people consider to be certain facts of life, and say &quot;no, these are not facts, I can do better&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> I mean. I would still make the mechanics require you to have dots in Mental Skills in order to build Wonders. But all things considered I see them as more similar than different.<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Save</span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 08-22-2016, 02:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T11:46:57-07:00","id":955756,"title":"","content":"I mean, I've got the theme pretty much down: Transgression. That comes straight from Genius, and it's what makes a mage or a scientist monstrous as opposed to just someone with superpowers or gadgets.<br /> <br /> And I disagree on the archetype thing. For example, Forsaken 2e deliberately addresses it by altering Wolfblooded to allow them to stand in for various folkloric werewolf legends. Same thing with Requiem 2e- it acknowledges that VtR vampires are based on the more recent Dracula/vampire movie/pop culture concept of the vampire, and establishes the Strix as covering the &quot;demon-possessed corpse&quot; nature of earlier vampires. So you gotta keep your source material in mind. And I'd call Genius something that absolutely does something new with an archetype. Manes aren't a part of mad scientist stories, for example, but they emerge from taking the archetype to its logical conclusion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 08-22-2016, 02:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T12:03:50-07:00","id":955766,"title":"","content":"I'd say what Genius does new is the self-awareness.<br /> <br /> Frankenstein's monster turned against it's creator. Lex Luthor cannot kill superman (permanently). And how many fictional alchemists failed to turn lead into gold? But Victor didn't know he was a mad scientist. Lex Luthor doesn't know that superman cannot be killed so long as his comic books sell.<br /> <br /> But in Genius the non-Unmada Inspired know that failure is, if not truly inevitable, pretty close to it. At best your communist utopia will turn out to be a pretty nice place to live, but neither truely communist or a utopia. At worst it turns into another Stalinist dystopia. Most likely it never gets off the ground. (Just like real attempts to make communist states)<br /> <br /> That internal conflict between the Genius' compulsion to peruse a grand world changing Magnum Opus and their rational knowledge that their time is better spent on smaller personal projects (don't try to invent the cure for cancer, just sneak into the hospital and zap people with your heal ray) is Genius' unique spin.<br /> <br /> <br /> Well mostly unique. Soon I Will Be Invincible did the same thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 08-22-2016, 03:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T12:13:44-07:00","id":955771,"title":"","content":"The whole association some people seem to have between Genius and communism is pretty silly to me, honestly. It's the whole &quot;capitalism must be treated as a legitimate economic system but communism is spooooooooooky and weird and bad and scary&quot; problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T12:21:00-07:00","id":955774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955735#post955735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The obvious follow up question is, in that case how would you define &quot;mad scientist&quot;?<br /> <br /> I mean that both thematically and in terms of how their powers work. As in, I'm not sure you could &quot;double down on the science&quot; and include the &quot;Irish Wild Man&quot; archetype at the same time. (assuming you want to double down on the science in the first place).<br /> <br /> Feel free to lecture away as much as you like.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that mad science as a literary concept would be defined as opposition to the typical conception of what is possible and what is real. I don't have any problem with that approach in Genius. I think science is seen as mad until it isn't. When medicine was based on Humorism, that was science. When medicine progressed, continued study of the humors (a disproven or, depending on how you look at it, misinterpreted understanding of the way our bodies work) was &quot;mad&quot;.<br /> <br /> My saying that, and Genius' saying that (if I understand correctly that that's what Genius says) is really a deconstruction of science as understood in scientific thought, which would claim that it doesn't matter that people once thought the world was flat, the world was still round, even then.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955771#post955771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The whole association some people seem to have between Genius and communism is pretty silly to me, honestly. It's the whole &quot;capitalism must be treated as a legitimate economic system but communism is spooooooooooky and weird and bad and scary&quot; problem.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As a communist myself (a Luxemburgist, if you're curious), I assure you that that is not the problem I have with Genius.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T12:22:57-07:00","id":955776,"title":"","content":"Oh no no no, I wasn't saying that was a problem you have! It's actually something Genius fans (such as Kings) have a tendency to say. I'm a communist too, and I just find it funny/annoying when people lump communism in with death rays and robot butlers. You haven't said anything like that at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T12:30:00-07:00","id":955785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955771#post955771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The whole association some people seem to have between Genius and communism is pretty silly to me, honestly. It's the whole &quot;capitalism must be treated as a legitimate economic system but communism is spooooooooooky and weird and bad and scary&quot; problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see where people might be coming from. Communism simultaneously entails a top-down command economy ordered along predictable principles and a political elite made up of literati steeped in dense philosophical orthodoxy. It also pays a great deal of lip service to technical achievement and scientific ideas (so long as they are subordinated to the aforementioned philosophical orthodoxy). Communism revolves around a cult of expertise, and marinated in the same political stew as other Genius-friendly political ideas like Technocracy and Anarcho-Syndicalism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T12:31:50-07:00","id":955790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955771#post955771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The whole association some people seem to have between Genius and communism is pretty silly to me, honestly. It's the whole &quot;capitalism must be treated as a legitimate economic system but communism is spooooooooooky and weird and bad and scary&quot; problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are there more people than me who do that?<br /> <br /> As for my own perspective, it's not that communism is weird and bad and scary. It's just that communism has some unique traits that make it a particularly good example to illustrate certain concepts.<br /> <br /> 1) It has a highly recognisable &quot;creator figure&quot; in Karl Marx<br /> 2) It made a noticable and large impact on the world.<br /> 3) Karl Marx didn't like the form communism eventually took.<br /> <br /> I like to draw parallels between #3 and Frankenstein being destroyed by his own creation. <br /> <br /> The lack of #1 and #3 are why I wouldn't use captialism to illustrate Genius. However I could use Christianity (Jesus said turn the other cheek, but Christianity lead to crusades), or the World Wide Web (Tim Burner's Lee is very unhappy with state surveillance for example).<br /> <br /> <br /> I'll try to use a different example next time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955774#post955774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that mad science as a literary concept would be defined as opposition to the typical conception of what is possible and what is real. I don't have any problem with that approach in Genius. I think science is seen as mad until it isn't. When medicine was based on Humorism, that was science. When medicine progressed, continued study of the humors (a disproven or, depending on how you look at it, misinterpreted understanding of the way our bodies work) was &quot;mad&quot;.<br /> <br /> My saying that, and Genius' saying that (if I understand correctly that that's what Genius says) is really a deconstruction of science as understood in scientific thought, which would claim that it doesn't matter that people once thought the world was flat, the world was still round, even then.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not getting what you mean here... sorry.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T12:35:06-07:00","id":955799,"title":"","content":"I'm not going to turn this into a political debate, but jfc CP you could fill up a barn with all that straw.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T12:38:22-07:00","id":955805,"title":"","content":"Communism is actually banned in certain areas of the world, and about as hated - if not more - than fascism and it's 3rd Reich brand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T12:41:14-07:00","id":955810,"title":"","content":"I think the better way to end that tangent is to take the discussion elsewhere. Maybe a thread in off-topic or a private message section?<br /> <br /> On the topic, Genius has always sort of rubbed me the wrong way, and I do appreciate the time you've taken to seriously think about it, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a>. It has been an interesting read, and the discussion that's followed, both in sincere defense of it and the discussion of specific elements of the fan gameline has been interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T12:46:29-07:00","id":955815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955790#post955790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not getting what you mean here... sorry.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, sorry, my fault. Let me simplify--which is not a hit at you, I obviously started to ramble and if I say it in just a few sentences, maybe you can then go back and see what I meant.<br /> <br /> 1) I am discussing mad science as a literary concept, not as a real-life concept.<br /> 2) We make sense of the world around us through our interpretation of the way real things are represented by signifiers, not by how they actually are.<br /> 3) I think that mad science, as a literary concept, would be defined in opposition to the way &quot;most&quot; people interpret signifiers. For example. When people believed the world was flat, &quot;mad science&quot; would be to assert that it was oval.<br /> 4) I am saying that regardless of the reality of a situation, what matters is our interpretation of that situation through the Real and the signifier, the Real being that which cannot be understood and cannot be labeled through language, and the signifier being how we interpret the Real in the best way we can, through symbols distinct from it's meaning.<br /> 5) Therefore, mad science transgresses from typical scientific understanding at any given time.<br /> <br /> BUT I ALSO THINK THIS COULD BE KIND OF PROBLEMATIC, because of course, the world is actually oval, and the world was oval even when people thought it was flat, so it's kind of a mindfuck to hold that thought simultaneously with the deconstruction I applied above where I said that in terms of a literary understanding, that doesn't matter as much as the perceptions people hold.<br /> <br /> Cool, or still having trouble? Again, no hit at you, but deconstruction is really hard and convoluted and I have trouble with it myself.<br /> <br /> (I also reserve the right to change this in ten minutes or ten days as I think about it more.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T13:02:32-07:00","id":955823,"title":"","content":"I think I understand. To test my understanding I'm going to try and put it into my own words and see if I get it right.<br /> <br /> 1) At any given time certain scientific ideas &quot;e.g. the world is flat&quot; are accepted by the scientific community / general public.<br /> 2) Mad science is science that contradicts the currently popular ideas<br /> 3) You're not comfortable with some of the implications. E.G. it implies &quot;vaccines cause autism&quot; is neither better nor worse, neither more accurate or less accurate than &quot;vaccines don't cause autism&quot;. It implies that an arbitrary popularity fad decides which of those two is &quot;science&quot; at any one time.<br /> <br /> <br /> If I understood that right it's definitely a huge departure from Genius as it is now. Whereby mundane science is more or less the same as what we have in the real world. And mad science is a specific supernatural phenomina that probably has an objective answer to describe what exactly it is and how it works - but right now nobody knows that answer and the six or so explenations we're given might or might not be correct.<br /> <br /> So, assuming I understood correctly. What would your intended charachter arc be for a Genius? What would your equivalent of a Mage's descent into hubris and obsession be?<br /> <br /> <br /> Would you keep Genius' current concept that Mad Scientists learn that trying to force the world to conform to their vision is practically impossible and a fundamentally unhealthy goal for everyone (or fail to learn that and suffer the consequences) or do you have a different idea?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T13:07:10-07:00","id":955827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955823#post955823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I understand. To test my understanding I'm going to try and put it into my own words and see if I get it right.<br /> <br /> 1) At any given time certain scientific ideas &quot;e.g. the world is flat&quot; are accepted by the scientific community / general public.<br /> 2) Mad science is science that contradicts the currently popular ideas<br /> 3) You're not comfortable with some of the implications. E.G. it implies &quot;vaccines cause autism&quot; is neither better nor worse, neither more accurate or less accurate than &quot;vaccines don't cause autism&quot;. It implies that an arbitrary popularity fad decides which of those two is &quot;science&quot; at any one time.<br /> <br /> <br /> If I understood that right it's definitely a huge departure from Genius as it is now. Whereby mundane science is more or less the same as what we have in the real world. And mad science is a specific supernatural phenomina that probably has an objective answer to describe what exactly it is and how it works - but right now nobody knows that answer and the six or so explenations we're given might or might not be correct.<br /> <br /> So, assuming I understood correctly. What would your intended charachter arc be for a Genius? What would your equivalent of a Mage's descent into hubris and obsession be?<br /> <br /> <br /> Would you keep Genius' current concept that Mad Scientists learn that trying to force the world to conform to their vision is practically impossible and a fundamentally unhealthy goal for everyone (or fail to learn that and suffer the consequences) or do you have a different idea?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That is what I'm saying, yeah =).<br /> <br /> I'm going to think about the additional questions you added and answer them later, if that's all right. I just want to make sure I give them proper thought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T13:11:19-07:00","id":955831,"title":"","content":"Sure, take your time. Just quote me or put @TheKingsRaven when you do so I get a notification please. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I like Genius, I think it nails a lot of fundamental mad science themes, both in terms of what mad scientists meant to the readers and what it must have felt to be those mad science characters who nearly-all failed to create their Magnum Opus or saw it turn against them. (Particularly the older stuff, before we got things like Girl Genius.)<br /> <br /> But it's not the be-all-end-all of mad science and I like seeing other perspectives.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T13:20:42-07:00","id":955837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955815#post955815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, sorry, my fault. Let me simplify--which is not a hit at you, I obviously started to ramble and if I say it in just a few sentences, maybe you can then go back and see what I meant.<br /> <br /> 1) I am discussing mad science as a literary concept, not as a real-life concept.<br /> 2) We make sense of the world around us through our interpretation of the way real things are represented by signifiers, not by how they actually are.<br /> 3) I think that mad science, as a literary concept, would be defined in opposition to the way &amp;quot;most&amp;quot; people interpret signifiers. For example. When people believed the world was flat, &amp;quot;mad science&amp;quot; would be to assert that it was oval.<br /> 4) I am saying that regardless of the reality of a situation, what matters is our interpretation of that situation through the Real and the signifier, the Real being that which cannot be understood and cannot be labeled through language, and the signifier being how we interpret the Real in the best way we can, through symbols distinct from it's meaning.<br /> 5) Therefore, mad science transgresses from typical scientific understanding at any given time.<br /> <br /> BUT I ALSO THINK THIS COULD BE KIND OF PROBLEMATIC, because of course, the world is actually oval, and the world was oval even when people thought it was flat, so it's kind of a mindfuck to hold that thought simultaneously with the deconstruction I applied above where I said that in terms of a literary understanding, that doesn't matter as much as the perceptions people hold.<br /> <br /> Cool, or still having trouble? Again, no hit at you, but deconstruction is really hard and convoluted and I have trouble with it myself.<br /> <br /> (I also reserve the right to change this in ten minutes or ten days as I think about it more.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm just going to add in that part of the reason I make a distinction between gurus/alchemists and mad scientists is that the former is a real world concept while that latter is a literary concept. I find it troubling to try and say that an alchemist is a mad scientists when real alchemists would not have defined themselves in anything close to those terms. At least with Mage the gnostic overtones are close enough in both cases to that an Awakened Mage is a reasonable approximatation. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar134_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"134\" data-vbnamecard=\"134\">The Kings Raven</a> , what you have defined to me is not the mad scientist, but the visionary. Those clearly overlap, but I take issue with using real world people and real world roles as the core premise for mad scientists when mad scientists are entirely a literary construct. Visionaries, be they religious, spiritual, political, or scientific, are all around us. It is a disservice to them and potentially an erasure of culture to equate them to an entirely fictional archetype. Especially one that opts not to explain the source of the Mad Scientist's power, becuase every Alchemist and Guru I've read about has entirely coherent and passionate belief in their metaphysics. The way Genius is currently set up, those metaphysics cannot possibly work or be adapted into the game's metaphysics becuase the answer boils down to &quot;Lol! Wrong!&quot; This is my opinion, but I think OP shares it with me. RPGs, especially those set in the modern day, should exult and celebrate the cultures of the world. That is not an easy thing to do, but it has been a continuous tone with 2e, and especially with Dark Eras. Without a metaphysical hook for why Geniuses can do what they do, it's downright impossible.<br /> <br /> Sorry if that was repetitive and rambling. The tl;dr is that I don't think conflating real and literary concepts in this instance is appropriate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T13:36:32-07:00","id":955852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955837#post955837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those clearly overlap, but I take issue with using real world people and real world roles as the core premise for mad scientists when mad scientists are entirely a literary construct. Visionaries, be they religious, spiritual, political, or scientific, are all around us. It is a disservice to them and potentially an erasure of culture to equate them to an entirely fictional archetype.</div> </div> </div> </div> I honestly cannot understand this viewpoint. I cannot understand how creating a metaphor for a thing can be considered erasing it. Also aren't Changelings equated to abuse survivors? Unless I'm mistaken faeries are entirely fictional.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955837#post955837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Especially one that opts not to explain the source of the Mad Scientist's power</div> </div> </div> </div> Can you explain where conciosness comes from? Can you explain what about Jesus' words made his gospel spread further than the ancient Roman's religion?<br /> <br /> Visionaries had a huge verities of different beliefs. But underneath those diverse beliefs was a common trait: Being a visionary.<br /> <br /> Inspiration is not alchemy. It's not Kabbalah. It's not a PhD dissertation in the Luminiferous Ether. Inspiration is &quot;being a visionary&quot;.<br /> <br /> And being a visionary is practically consciousness itself.<br /> <br /> Genius doesn't need to present a world where Kabbalah is correct, because it's about the common &quot;being a visionary&quot;, not the details of the individual vision. And Inspiration can be a mystery* because consciousness is a mystery. It presents six possible explanations, they may be right, they may be wrong, but like consciousness Inspiration is still a mystery.<br /> <br /> <br /> * Honestly I still don't see why it needs a reason to make the power source one of the setting's core mysteries.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955837#post955837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">becuase every Alchemist and Guru I've read about has entirely coherent and passionate belief in their metaphysics. The way Genius is currently set up, those metaphysics cannot possibly work or be adapted into the game's metaphysics becuase the answer boils down to &quot;Lol! Wrong!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The way Mage is set up groups like Aboriginal Australians - who are explicitly included among the Awakened - cannot have their metaphysics represented because the answer boils down to gnostic Willworking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 08-22-2016, 04:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T13:40:42-07:00","id":955855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955852#post955852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I honestly cannot understand this viewpoint. I cannot understand how creating a metaphor for a thing can be considered erasing it. Also aren't Changelings equated to abuse survivors? Unless I'm mistaken faeries are entirely fictional.<br /> <br /> Can you explain where conciosness comes from? Can you explain what about Jesus' words made his gospel spread further than the ancient Roman's religion?<br /> <br /> Genius is in the same place. It presents six possible explanations, they may be right, they may be wrong, but like consciousness Inspiration is still a mystery.<br /> <br /> The way Mage is set up groups like Aboriginal Australians - who are explicitly included among the Awakened - cannot have their metaphysics represented because the answer boils down to gnostic Willworking.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always hated Awakening's policy of &quot;you can't use existing magical systems unless you're in the Free Council&quot;. It was one of the things I liked about Ascension. In MtT, there's sort of a comprise- Mages can use whatever belief system or practice resonates with them enough that they can tear holes in reality to make it work, same as with Geniuses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T13:48:42-07:00","id":955865,"title":"","content":"Eh. The compromise didn't work for me. [edit] Oops. I completely misread you. My bad.<br /> <br /> If I am going to play, say, a Kabbalist I want to have actual mechanics for Kabbalah rather than a generic mechanic with a few changes on the surface. Techne works for playing a Libertine - not so much for playing a Kabbalist.<br /> <br /> But I don't think this is some sort of moral failing on the part of Mage. It's just my personal taste.<br /> <br /> Mage does obsessive detectives through the lense of gnostic willworkers. Not every obsessive detective concept fits that game, not every concept needs to.<br /> <br /> Genius does visionaries through the lense of mad science. Not every visionary concept fits that game, not every concept needs to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T13:50:23-07:00","id":955866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955855#post955855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've always hated Awakening's policy of &quot;you can't use existing magical systems unless you're in the Free Council&quot;. It was one of the things I liked about Ascension. In MtT, there's sort of a comprise- Mages can use whatever belief system or practice resonates with them enough that they can tear holes in reality to make it work, same as with Geniuses.</div> </div> </div> </div>That... was... never a thing in Awakening? The Diamond Orders believe that Sleeper magical traditions have little nuggets of Supernal truth hidden inside them, the difficulty is ferreting them out from all the Fallen white noise that's accrued around them over time. The Free Council believes that Sleeper magical traditions are innately supernatural in and of themselves and have magical value outside of any Supernal pearls hidden within.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T14:01:25-07:00","id":955875,"title":"","content":"I don't mean on a philosophical level, I mean in terms of how you're restricted to doing magic in only a handful of specific ways. Even if you use the trappings of science or an existing magical tradition, you don't need to. I prefer the outlook that the magic mages do is fueled by their personal outlook, and that's what differentiates them from sorcerers.<br /> <br /> It was one of my favorite things about Ascension, and I love that Genius uses it while removing the consensus reality aspect.<br /> <br /> I must say, you have the most astoundingly appropriate icon I've seen on this forum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 08-22-2016, 06:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T14:14:11-07:00","id":955881,"title":"","content":"And even though the Free Council believes sleeper traditions like Christianity are magical; you still couldn't play a priest who receives power from God. Your power will come from your Will and the Supernal. Not the guy in the Old Testament.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T14:14:30-07:00","id":955883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955875#post955875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't mean on a philosophical level, I mean in terms of how you're restricted to doing magic in only a handful of specific ways. Even if you use the trappings of science or an existing magical tradition, you don't need to. I prefer the outlook that the magic mages do is fueled by their personal outlook, and that's what differentiates them from sorcerers.<br /> <br /> It was one of my favorite things about Ascension, and I love that Genius uses it while removing the consensus reality aspect.</div> </div> </div> </div>The influence of how you perform your magic has always been little more than a coat of paint in mage, just like the aesthetics of your inventions in Genius.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I must say, you have the most astoundingly appropriate icon I've seen on this program. </div> </div> </div>I mean if people stopped making shit up about other games and citing them as fact, maybe I'd have a more positive posting tone.<br /> <br /> But if you want to take jabs at each other's icons, maybe you should change yours to something more <a href=\"https://24carat.co.uk/images/1961shillingrev400.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">suitable</a> first?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T14:14:32-07:00","id":955884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955823#post955823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I understand. To test my understanding I'm going to try and put it into my own words and see if I get it right.<br /> <br /> 1) At any given time certain scientific ideas &quot;e.g. the world is flat&quot; are accepted by the scientific community / general public.<br /> 2) Mad science is science that contradicts the currently popular ideas<br /> 3) You're not comfortable with some of the implications. E.G. it implies &quot;vaccines cause autism&quot; is neither better nor worse, neither more accurate or less accurate than &quot;vaccines don't cause autism&quot;. It implies that an arbitrary popularity fad decides which of those two is &quot;science&quot; at any one time.<br /> <br /> <br /> If I understood that right it's definitely a huge departure from Genius as it is now. Whereby mundane science is more or less the same as what we have in the real world. And mad science is a specific supernatural phenomina that probably has an objective answer to describe what exactly it is and how it works - but right now nobody knows that answer and the six or so explenations we're given might or might not be correct.<br /> <br /> So, assuming I understood correctly. What would your intended charachter arc be for a Genius? What would your equivalent of a Mage's descent into hubris and obsession be?<br /> <br /> <br /> Would you keep Genius' current concept that Mad Scientists learn that trying to force the world to conform to their vision is practically impossible and a fundamentally unhealthy goal for everyone (or fail to learn that and suffer the consequences) or do you have a different idea?</div> </div> </div> </div>Know this was a directed reply, but thought I might be able to add something.<br /> <br /> 1.) The tangent plane to a convex shape is flat. Within the proper scope, the world may be treated such that it is effectively flat. This is why you can level a table in your kitchen.<br /> <br /> 2.) Galileo was mad until he wasn't. His claims didn't make sense because the level on the table worked.<br /> <br /> 3.) When looking at the entire world with the same assumptions as the small scope of say the tangent plane of your kitchen, the model falls apart. Another way to phrase it is attempting to use a statistic linear projection to make predictions about events far in the future. Models are simplified representations of reality which have utility within the scope of their construction but which begin to fail in the construction of a &quot;Grand unified theory of everything.&quot;<br /> To the level on the kitchen table, the idea that the world beneath it is round is not only ridiculous but completely irrelevant.<br /> However, to that same level the sun appears to be rotating around the kitchen, melting into nothing on the horizon and spawning again from nothing the next morning. Using a model for a grander scope invalidates the utility of a level (you wouldn't try to level a whole city, let alone the entire world!) but allows for more sophisticated analysis at that scope. For instance, recognizing the world is round allows for the better modeling of time in the day through the establishment of time zones.<br /> <br /> <br /> That's what I feel Genius should focus on; small discoveries which in the scope of their revelation are useful but when exposed to a larger model fail to properly define phenomenon. Wonders are the levels on the kitchen table. They go off the assumption the world is flat and work from there. While they can achieve results, when applied to greater scope they expose greater and greater error in statistical approximation, making their widespread use impractical, ridiculous, or downright impossible.<br /> <br /> This sort of thing extends beyond science and could cover other character archetypes (not just intellectuals and pseudo-intellectuals). For instance, perhaps an artist experiments with a new painting style and creates a portrait which has the capacity to hypnotize dogs (a prototype, or a Wonder). This genius (player character) uses the portrait to defend herself while walking down abandoned alleys because she can make stray dogs attack muggers with it. However, as she tries to use it in more situations (dog shows to win prize money, on a trip to Europe) she finds the thing has limits; it only works on three dogs at a time and won't work on dobermans. Worse, she tries to replicate the style and finds that she cannot; other paintings produced in this method do not possess this peculiar property (the prototype cannot be mass-produced).<br /> Frustrated, she decides to abandon her plans to control dogs with her art. She makes a new painting of a landscape, but now she finds that she can step through it like a portal. The cycle begins again; she sets out to make a fortune in mass transit innovation but cannot lay her finger on what exactly makes her painting do this. Or... she figures it out this time, but the variables to trigger such an effect are absurd and outlandish and must be replicated exactly. Maybe the paintings can only make portals to locations in her neighborhood. Maybe they require a specific blending of green from the corner store, left out to sit during the moonlight. Hyper-specific variable requirements prevent her discoveries from becoming part of the mainstream, and what's worse she has to experiment and dissect her efforts to find what works and what doesn't... or give up and pursue another project.<br /> <br /> Then the goal of the game becomes the experimentation on a medium and the recovery from failures. Your characters have the raw potential to do amazing and potentially supernatural things, but they struggle to find the reasons why their efforts are successful (like a real scientist would) and move on when they fail (like a mad scientist would. Have you ever noticed villains abandon a plan entirely when it fails, even if it almost exceeded? That sounds like what a Genius should do... at least to me. Baby with the bathwater sort of stuff).<br /> <br /> Such a game wouldn't even have need for an antagonist faction, but were you to form one I'd once again recommend smaller groups who discover some practical small-scope theory they have in common and use it to build power and influence. Like-minds collaborating on hypotheses which work off the assumption the world is flat, and which try in vain to MAKE the world flat so that their work can have more grandiose influence.<br /> Instead of one organization being a looming threat to the world, a Lemurian Think Tank might all agree that the gravitational acceleration is -6 meters per second and might try to force that notion on the world. By contrast, the player characters (Genii) fight against this notion and the wonders it may provide to the world because while they do NOT have a consensus on the acceleration of gravity (though they might all agree it's not the accepted norm of -9.8 meters per second) the actions of that Think Tank are causing their own wonders to misfire. Essentially, players should be the Unmada and the antagonists should have at least some manner of popular opinion (whether or not it is the accepted scientific stance or not) that threatens the player's own head-canon of reality. Players work together because--even though they may disagree with each other's hypotheses--they KNOW that the Lemurian Think Tanks pushing into their territory are WRONG (KNOW and WRONG emphasized because they've dug their heels into the sand and accepted their hypotheses as facts). Unite against the common threat and all that (and of course the Think Tank is more powerful than an individual Genius opposing them because more minds are contributing to that solipsistic reality, necessitating a team-up).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":610,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","user":"CJC","date":".  Forgot to type the end of a sentence, sorry. 08-22-2016, 05:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T14:18:21-07:00","id":955886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955881#post955881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And even though the Free Council believes sleeper traditions like Christianity are magical; you still couldn't play a priest who receives power from God. Your power will come from your Will and the Supernal. Not the guy in the Old Testament.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um there is an entire path of mages with overt divinity parallels. The Theurges all are channeling power from a heaven that is full of literal angels. <i>Lots</i> of Obrimos through the ages have seen their Awakening as god-given grace.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T14:23:06-07:00","id":955888,"title":"","content":"Go to your nearest Christian church. Show them the section on Theurges.<br /> <br /> Would they agree that it accurately represents their faith?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955884#post955884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wonders are the levels on the kitchen table. They go off the assumption the world is flat and work from there. While they can achieve results, when applied to greater scope they expose greater and greater error in statistical approximation, making their widespread use impractical, ridiculous, or downright impossible.</div> </div> </div> </div> This is explicitly how Wonders work.<br /> <br /> Wheather a Genius accepts this limitation and finds ways to do great things within those limits or spends their career railing against those limitations... well that's the question isn't it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'm not sold on your antagonists though. The Peerage encourages Geniuses to accept their limitations (but not all Peers get the message), Lemuria rails against them. I like that division as the core difference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 08-22-2016, 05:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T14:26:25-07:00","id":955889,"title":"","content":"Actually, Paradigms and Aesthetics are massively important to Geniuses, and I'd argue that they should be even more important: penalties for doing things outside your Paradigm/Aesthetic, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T14:36:42-07:00","id":955898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955888#post955888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Go to your nearest Christian church. Show them the section on Theurges.<br /> <br /> Would they agree that it accurately represents their faith?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dude. Do the same thing with the Celestial Chorus. Theurges aren't meant to be the christian mages group, they're the ready-made highway to make a character that is a devout Christian who got their power from god to slot into the game. With only a little work, you can make a &quot;devout Christian mage who believes they received their Awakening through the grace of God&quot; from any path. The Aether is supposed to be able to accommodate many character concepts from devout priests, to mechanistic atheists to people who think they were abducted by aliens.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T14:46:15-07:00","id":955905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TidyGamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955898#post955898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">they're the ready-made highway to make a character that is a devout Christian who got their power from god to slot into the game. With only a little work, you can make a &quot;devout Christian mage who believes they received their Awakening through the grace of God&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Who recieved their Awakening&quot;.<br /> <br /> It's still their Awakening, their power. You could not have a charachter who prays, then God hears the prayer and decides wheather or not to intervene. You could not have a charachter who's power is dependent upon virtueous behaviour and looses access to their magic if they behave improperly.<br /> <br /> You could do a devout Christian Obrimos easily. You could not do a charachter who's power works the way real life Christians say miracles work.<br /> <br /> That's not a problem with Mage. Mage wants to do Gnostic Willworkers, that's fine. It does Gnostic Willworkers well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T14:56:44-07:00","id":955909,"title":"","content":"I think there's a fundamental misapprehension of Mage if you think that only the Free Council use real-world occult practices for their magic. They're the group which believes that the human practices make them supernal, instead of humans discovering supernal magic in the real-world occult practices, and that is itself a chicken-or-the-egg situation. Nevermind the fact that each Mage is an individual, who may have an individual perspective on their particular practice of Awakened Magic, and said practice need not totally match the &quot;orthodoxy&quot; of their Order, if it even has some kind of strong provision that isn't just academic.<br /> <br /> On the point of playing a Christian Mage, one absolutely can, it just needs to be understood that the form of Christianity that a Mage may practice will probably differ significantly from that of a regular person. Obviously, there will be people who challenge their beliefs, but... Y'know. That's exactly how it works in real life too.<br /> <br /> One possible example of how a Mage might remain Christian and become Awakened might be to interpret their interaction with the Supernal as some form of divine communion. Much like some scientists might describe that God, to them is as much the figure in the scriptures as he is the Theory of Gravity, the process of Natural Selection, or the reaction of protons and electrons.<br /> <br /> Belief is complicated, personal and remarkably adaptable. We even have examples of Christian mages in 1st edition who have a similar perspective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T15:00:44-07:00","id":955914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955888#post955888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sold on your antagonists though. The Peerage encourages Geniuses to accept their limitations (but not all Peers get the message), Lemuria rails against them. I like that division as the core difference.</div> </div> </div> </div>Accepting limitations, finding common ground, and agreeing to work together are all matters which allow for the formation of functional social groups. They're the kind of things that allow an organization to operate in plain sight without raising eyebrows.<br /> <br /> Attempting to break limitations, though, makes you stick out like a sore thumb.<br /> <br /> Isn't that what the description in Genius's history fits? An organization of like-minded individuals could manipulate and control the development of man, but would impede those radicals who want the freedom to experiment. It's Edison and his slander squad against Tesla and his coils. Edison is the Lemurian in that scenario; he's a mad scientist but his science is mainstream. Tesla on the other hand is pushed into the shadows, flagged as crazy, and has his science constantly undermined by political attack. He's the Genius in that scenario.<br /> <br /> Having a consensus and using it to control a situation, while cowering at the notion of pushing beyond the limits of that power (for fear of losing it)... that's a villainous concept. Conversely, fighting against the consensus and trying to show that 2 + 2 != 4, while being pushed down by a world that dismisses those ravings as nonsense... that has the makings for a rebellion. And in fiction a rebellion is generally the best place to find your protagonist.<br /> <br /> I just find it hard to frame the idea that these evil scientists pushed beyond the limits of the known with violent vigor but failed to be exposed in the process. It seems the action of a lone quack. It seems something a player character would try to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T15:27:09-07:00","id":955929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955909#post955909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the point of playing a Christian Mage, one absolutely can, it just needs to be understood that the form of Christianity that a Mage may practice will probably differ significantly from that of a regular person.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, that's my point.<br /> <br /> You can play a Christian Mage, but they'd have to be different from a real world Christian. Certainly in the metaphyiscs they believe in, probably in their actual faith.<br /> <br /> And my other point is that there's nothing wrong with that. I don't think that Mage (or Genius) has any obligation to be able to accurately model the metaphysics beleived by different real world why might become a Mage or Genius.<br /> <br /> (Basically I agree with you).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955914#post955914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having a consensus and using it to control a situation, while cowering at the notion of pushing beyond the limits of that power (for fear of losing it)... that's a villainous concept. Conversely, fighting against the consensus and trying to show that 2 + 2 != 4, while being pushed down by a world that dismisses those ravings as nonsense... that has the makings for a rebellion. And in fiction a rebellion is generally the best place to find your protagonist.</div> </div> </div> </div> I disagree.<br /> <br /> There's plenty of fiction with rebel protagonists. There's also plenty of fiction where the protagonists are government agents. Neither is &quot;best&quot;, and I reject the entire concept of &quot;best&quot; when it comes to fiction. Look at Vampire, with both Invictics and Carthian as protagonist options.<br /> <br /> There is no best. Only what is right for this particular story. And when the theme is Transgression; the characters who think and reflect on their Transgressions are better protagonists than the characters who run full speed ahead without ever considering the consequences.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955914#post955914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just find it hard to frame the idea that these evil scientists pushed beyond the limits of the known with violent vigor but failed to be exposed in the process. It seems the action of a lone quack. It seems something a player character would try to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who says they weren't exposed? Lemuria lost their conflict, I'm sure there were plenty of mortals opponents as well as Inspired ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T17:18:30-07:00","id":956005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955875#post955875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I must say, you have the most astoundingly appropriate icon I've seen on this forum.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Clearly a violation of rule #1 of the forum.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">\u200bThis is literally the last warning you will get from me, next step is a permanent ban. I'm tired of the immature bullshit.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T17:45:57-07:00","id":956022,"title":"","content":"Genius or not Genius?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://dresdencodak.com/2009/09/22/caveman-science-fiction/\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"http://dresdencodak.com/comics/2009-09-22-caveman_science_fiction.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T17:48:30-07:00","id":956027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955823#post955823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would your intended character arc be for a Genius? What would your equivalent of a Mage's descent into hubris and obsession be?<br /> <br /> <br /> Would you keep Genius' current concept that Mad Scientists learn that trying to force the world to conform to their vision is practically impossible and a fundamentally unhealthy goal for everyone (or fail to learn that and suffer the consequences) or do you have a different idea?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to start by saying that I think anyone planning on making a game should watch these videos:<br /> <br /> Part 1:<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4QwcI4iQt2Y\" data-code=\"4QwcI4iQt2Y\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/4QwcI4iQt2Y/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Part 2:<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pP_qNm-96Dc\" data-code=\"pP_qNm-96Dc\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/pP_qNm-96Dc/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> You've told me you have a theme--transgression. Everything in the game should point back to that theme. Every single thing. Your abilities, the history, any kind of Magnum Opus you create, and the undercurrents and metaphors in your game (what we've been talking about here). Those videos talk about mechanics as metaphor for video game developers, but I have found everything they discuss very helpful for RPG development too. I highly recommend you watch them, and I highly recommend playing the flash game they link to. It's very short, and I think it'll give you a lot of inspiration.<br /> <br /> If I were making a mad science game, I would base it heavily on the works of Jacques Derrida and Jacques Lacan. Phenomenology and Deconstruction, along with the crash course I gave above. I think a focus on psychological horror and how we define and derive meaning from symbols has just as much potential to be really tragic as what you're talking about, and I would actually posit that it has even more of that potential. It would, in a sense, build off the work already done with Mage, while still keeping itself distinct and respectful of that text. It would fill a void I don't think is as covered in CofD, and if you kept it cohesive, I think it would have the potential to be amazing.<br /> <br /> You could still keep the concept of a battle for understanding. Kind of about who controls public perception, and who controls meaning. Or you could go a different route and make the tragic horror of Genius about trying to control that meaning, only to find that people believe what they believe, and that signifiers are too hard to change once they're established in people's minds. <br /> <br /> I would make the game much more internal, and much less focused on building Wonders. I think Wonders can still be present, there should definitely still be mechanics for them, but the mechanics in 1ed are convoluted and confusing, because they--in my opinion--don't hearken back to a cohesive theme. Start with your theme. You have your theme, as I understand it (transgression). Build out from there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T18:31:35-07:00","id":956051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955462#post955462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think this is the right question to ask. I think you first need to answer, &quot;Why do I want horror in my Genius experience?&quot;<br /> <br /> Because maybe you don't, and trying to import horror is the entirely wrong thing to do in the first place, and it would be good to know that before you crowbar something inappropriate into the game.<br /> <br /> Because maybe you do, but now you know <i>exactly</i> what's missing, rather than a vague genre-type that doesn't mean anything standing on its own, so you can usefully try different things to see if they successfully bring that missing piece in.</div> </div> </div> </div>THis is part of the problem of branding yourself a ChroD game, even a fan game. If this were just some shindig, I wouldn't have ground to gripe about being a monster or having a lack of personal horror, but as something I should be able to use right next to my Changeling the Lost in theory?<br /> <br /> The problem with setting expectations is that, sooner or later, someone is going to hold you to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T18:38:30-07:00","id":956054,"title":"","content":"I've never thought there was a dearth of horror in Genius. In fact, one of the reasons I liked it so much was that the personal horror was done better than in Mage. I admit that they themes could be tightened and that could be emphasized more, but I never thought a lack of it was one of the major problems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T18:53:48-07:00","id":956061,"title":"","content":"Can I just say that, independent of content, I'm incredibly thankful this thread has been as civil as it is?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T19:12:38-07:00","id":956072,"title":"","content":"I personally would have described it as superbly messy up to just below the surface, but that works too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T19:14:25-07:00","id":956073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=956022#post956022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Genius or not Genius?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://dresdencodak.com/2009/09/22/caveman-science-fiction/\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"http://dresdencodak.com/comics/2009-09-22-caveman_science_fiction.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a></div> </div> </div> </div>Either way, can we all just pause and admit that it is genius?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T20:33:53-07:00","id":956112,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking sometime this week I need to address my ideas about biases in reviews and provide an example to solidify my point. I might even start tonight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T20:40:26-07:00","id":956119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=956112#post956112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm thinking sometime this week I need to address my ideas about biases in reviews and provide an example to solidify my point. I might even start tonight.</div> </div> </div> </div>As long as it's not 50,000 words. If I were there, I'd spray you with a spray bottle every 1,000.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T20:41:35-07:00","id":956121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=956119#post956119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As long as it's not 50,000 words. If I were there, I'd spray you with a spray bottle every 1,000.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not have 50,000 words about biases in reviews.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T20:42:16-07:00","id":956122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=956121#post956121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not have 50,000 words about biases in reviews.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're not allowed to write more than an arbitrary number to be decided upon by David Hill and I.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T20:44:14-07:00","id":956123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=956122#post956122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're not allowed to write more than an arbitrary number to be decided upon by David Hill and I.</div> </div> </div> </div>If Dave gives me a word limit, it better either be for a contract or arbitrarily defending Twilight just because I can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T20:47:49-07:00","id":956125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955905#post955905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Who recieved their Awakening&quot;.<br /> <br /> It's still their Awakening, their power. You could not have a charachter who prays, then God hears the prayer and decides wheather or not to intervene. You could not have a charachter who's power is dependent upon virtueous behaviour and looses access to their magic if they behave improperly.<br /> <br /> You could do a devout Christian Obrimos easily. You could not do a charachter who's power works the way real life Christians say miracles work.<br /> <br /> That's not a problem with Mage. Mage wants to do Gnostic Willworkers, that's fine. It does Gnostic Willworkers well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your higher power of choice decides to intervene or not based on the success or failure of your spell, but your higher power of choice gave you this power to use, not snatch away because you aren't perfect. Yeah, you can perform your own miracles because God imbued you with some of his grace and yeah you can do things that God wouldn't approve of. but if you were a devout Christian who honestly believes that the magic you use is a gift from God, would you really use it in a manner you don't believe God would sanction? Especially when there's plenty of people in real life who believe that their higher power of choice condones things that others would consider reckless and immoral?<br /> <br /> Yeah it's not a worldview that's gonna get a lot of traction in the mainstream diamond orders, but that's what Libertines and Apostates are for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T20:53:25-07:00","id":956130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=955929#post955929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who says they weren't exposed? Lemuria lost their conflict, I'm sure there were plenty of mortals opponents as well as Inspired ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>I might be misreading, but the sense I get is that that part of the setting is, &quot;Geniuses will change the future, but they haven't caused many visible changes up to now.&quot; Which I suppose was done to create a current day setting where supernatural exists but isn't treated as known to exist by the public at large, but it becomes an oddly specific thing when you think about it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=956027#post956027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would make the game much more internal, and much less focused on building Wonders. I think Wonders can still be present, there should definitely still be mechanics for them, but the mechanics in 1ed are convoluted and confusing, because they--in my opinion--don't hearken back to a cohesive theme. Start with your theme. You have your theme, as I understand it (transgression). Build out from there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally would disagree, with the full disclosure that I'm an inventory junkie when it comes to games. There are already a lot of games with a secondary item-crafting system. Unless I'm wrong (and please correct me if I am, but Genius is the game that focuses on what the PCs can do with what they made as opposed to what they do with internal abilities. For all the game's flaws, I want the Wonders to remain GtT's version of a Mage's Spellcasting or a Beast's Atavisms or a Princess's Charms - the primary manner through which the PC works with and on the world.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8064-mp122984","name":"mp122984","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T22:38:31-07:00","id":956165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TidyGamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=956125#post956125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, you can perform your own miracles because God imbued you with some of his grace and yeah you can do things that God wouldn't approve of....</div> </div> </div> </div>And, you know, this is exactly what happens in the Bible with Moses. Moses doesn't pray and stuff happens. He's granted the ability to do miracles in the Lord's name. And he gets in very big trouble when he performs a miracle without it being in the Lord's name... even though it was one he did before.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T22:51:37-07:00","id":956172,"title":"","content":"Earlier today my thoughts came around to some of the arguments I've made thus far as I contemplate continuing on with the Genius review or if I said the mainstay of what needs to be said, and my thoughts came around to questions about whether I was blowing the depth of the misanthropy and the exclusionary nature of the game out of proportion. While I stand by those arguments, the thought occured to me that people could respond that I only made an issue of those things because I was pre-disposed to be biased against Genius, and that in fact you could probably invalidate every argument I made on the subject. While that is a position I can support points on, I feel like it ignores certain realities in favor of a sweet lie. I pondered on this long enough that I figured &quot;Hell, let's talk about it.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b><u>I Slapped God for His Throne-The Myth of the Objective Review</u></b><br /> <br /> I actually don't like arguments about subjective opinion, by and large because it ignores that creative works have a craft element to them, that there are, in fact, good and bad ways to do things, and that there are things to learn from it. More on point, I don't like it because the easiest way to dismiss someone's objections rather than consider them is to label it as &quot;just their opinion.&quot; However, when it comes to my own commentary in any sort of position of authority, I often make a keen point of reinforcing the idea that no one has to listen to me, because while I have issue with it, there's no such thing as an objective review, and even if there were, it would be useless anyways.<br /> <br /> In case you're not familiar, the idea of the objective review is basically, well, a review that relies on objectivity, on a view point distant from one's self and one's biases and judged purely on what it is. It basically posits that there is an outside authority on the subject that cannot be argued against, a universal decree of what works, what doesn't, what is good and what is bad. This can be handy when you're trying to say something negative about something beloved (like this review) or something positive about something reviled (say, Twilight)-you can shift the blame of unpopularity onto a premise that says &quot;This is the way things are.&quot; It's about having authority by not directly <i>claiming</i> authority.<br /> <br /> I imagine you already know the problem-where, then, does this objective authority come from? And you know, that is a hard question to answer, if it has an answer that isn't pure revelation.<br /> <br /> The simple fact of the matter is that, while there might some vague senses of what can make any given project successful, the fact of that matter is that, yeah, shit's too variable. Every project is unique, and people are going to react from a mountain of millions of unique perspective building conditions. An objective review would have to be something that literally every one in the world could agree on. The only reviews I think you could get of that sort might be purely compositional, like &quot;This post is an arrangement of black pixels amidst a wide field of white pixels&quot;, and I'm not even going to commit to that.<br /> <br /> Yeah, that's boring and useless. And more importantly, I personally don't want to explain my viewpoint to everyone. I don't have an interest in persuading everyone. I don't have a <i>belief</i> in persuading everyone. If I did, I wouldn't have wasted my time on Genius, because that's not a place I'm going to do it.<br /> <br /> And really, this brings up the big thing I don't believe reviews are for.<br /> <br /> <u><b>We Are All Individuals-Personal Authority and Poking People in the Eye</b></u><br /> <br /> I probably should have titled the section this: &quot;I AM NOT HERE TO TELL YOU WHAT TO THINK. THAT'S NOT WHAT REVIEWS ARE FOR.&quot;<br /> <br /> It is not my job, or the job of any reviewer, to tell the audience what to think of any given thing. It is not their job to acquire a flock of like-minded sheep who preach the word almighty about Ghostbusters or American Gods or Majora's Mask or even Genius. There are only two things a reviewer does.<br /> <br /> 1) Establish a case for their personal authority and the nature of it, and<br /> 2) Use that authority to provoke discourse that will allow the readers to deepen their understanding in some way.<br /> <br /> Or to put it simply, &quot;TRY TO HELP PEOPLE THINK.&quot;<br /> <br /> That sounds a little dismissive, but for a moment here, let's consider, well, this review. Lots of people have come away with an understanding that Genius is shit and could be so much better if some ideas were applied. Lots of other people have come away with a deeper appreciation for how Genius works and appeals to them and avenues of thought it had not revealed to them before. Some people have also realized that their own discussion techniques are overly hostile, while some people have learned that no, they can get even more in your face.<br /> <br /> Genius and I make for a messy, ugly battleground, but god damn if everyone doesn't walk away as much of a winner as they are a loser. Because, in the end, no one is winning against anything.<br /> <br /> This entire thing is a sledgehammer, forged of my expertise, my experiences, my reputation, and, above all else, <i>my biases, </i>refined in the experience of this thing we call Genius, slammed against a community to see what would <i>change</i>. That is what a review is <i>for</i>. In a certain way, it's an experiment-<i>let's tip over the rock and see what squirms there</i>, or <i>let's add fire and see if it explodes or fizzles.</i><br /> <br /> And I could do that if I wasn't biased. I could try and talk about this game completely without admitting to the fact that I kind of unfairly hated Genius to begin with, that despite all efforts I might exert to give it a fair try, I would inevitably lose to the aquifer of spite that has been filling with each and every jackass who made Genius look less and less appealing, whether directly or vicariously. I could try and leave my concerns about social justice at the door and just talk about this as a game. I could have left out my history and kindly overlook an angle people might never even think of. I could have tried any of that.<br /> <br /> But I would have failed, because I am my own authority-in fact, I am quite proud of several of the ways I have built that authority, and I have pangs of guilt of when I have abused that authority. I cannot rely on anything beyond it. And honestly? Why pull away when those biases, unfair though they might be, provide a way for people to look at something? To look closely at it and go &quot;Really? Are you worth it?&quot;. Even if they walk away with a deep conviction of a worth I don't believe in, <i>the examination happened</i>. And that's <i>worth it</i>.<br /> <br /> Still, I don't want to make it sound like all negative reviews are worth reading. They're not. I'm not even going to tell you <i>mine</i><i> is</i>. it's entirely possible that, yes, I am full of shit. I'm sure there's an number of you walking in who already knew that and don't feel like you need to rediscover it(I even jab some of you for it, because I can). And I'm sure you have your own metric for how you can tell.<br /> <br /> Still, I'm gonna give two main keys I look for in a useful negative review. And, okay, yeah, I'm also going to propose these are reasons why I'm not. I can only admit to possibly being ass for so long.(I mean, don't get me wrong, I'm a jackass, but I'm not ass.)<br /> <br /> <b><u>Given and Denied-Credit Where It's Due and Reason Where It Stands</u></b><br /> <br /> When I listen or read a negative review of something, two things usually mark it of at least some worth to me.<br /> <br /> 1) Does it at least pretend to try to understand where the piece was coming from?<br /> 2) Does it at least pretend to decently explain it's points to me so they may be plain?<br /> <br /> Truthfully, I'm a lot harsher than that, but at a <i>bare minimum</i>, I want to see reviewer at least talk about trying to comprehend why a choice was made and as clearly and in as much detail why they think the problem is there. These things together mean to me, if nothing else, that a genuine effort was made to establish the authority worth investing into, to establish that the questions are not just idle throw arounds, but actual conundrums.<br /> <br /> The willingness to postulate good reasons why someone made a poor choice, the empathy to consider that, is a matter of good faith. It may be useful to hate a thing and to let the anger flow, but that anger has to be tempered by consideration. If you ask a question of why a thing was done, it doesn't hurt you to try and answer why <i>you </i>would do that thing and come up with an answer that you could actually conceive of applying to yourself. It saves time and makes you look less like a fool, if nothing else-it's one thing to say &quot;This thing is wrong&quot; and it turns out it was something obvious, where at least &quot;This thing is wrong, even if I can see them doing because of this&quot; is a whole 'nother thing because it fills that &quot;you missed the obvious&quot; with a different thought. Being willing to concede that it may not have started with bad intentions makes people inclined to listen to you, which is important if you want anyone other than those who cheep along with you to at least consider the subject-it puts them in a frame of mind to consider hings themselves. And, honestly, it just becomes a new avenue for discovering problems.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the willingness to go in depths and explain your position, to try and account for all the variables and exactly how and why something doesn't work translates into meat and power. The more thoroughly you explain the problems as you see it, the less places it has to go for defense, for justification. <i>Any idiot</i> can dismiss a simple &quot;It's terrible&quot;, or even &quot;It's terrible because it has terrible characters, terrible aesthetics, and terrible gameplay.&quot; Terrible doesn't <i>mean</i> anything on it's own there, any statement requires building up.* But you say &quot;It's terrible because it's characters are all selfish, one dimensional stereotypes(and here's how, rarble rarble), the aesthetics are a mis-match of eras that defeat each other's intended atmosphere( and here's how, rarble rarble), and the gameplay completely favors these characters with zero incentive to play anyone else(and here's how, rarble rarble)&quot;, and all of sudden, just by sheer virtue of mass, a person has to weigh things carefully, if for no other reason than seeing if it's right. An even better argument weaves those points together and demonstrate the intersectionality of these problems, how one feeds into another, meaning one has to address the whole picture. All of this together creates questions, and whether they agree with it or not, they have to own their personal biases and experiences and leverage them into a viewpoint that someone can learn from. Thoroughly exploring and explaining your points means you create a labyrinth of people to explore that, by the time they get through, causes them to have their own labyrinth where there might not have been one before. And that's how dialogue is created, that's how we learn.<br /> <br /> *By the way, the same applies to declarative statements, and even better, this is where you get diversity-even as you build along the lines, you can make clear concessions to other answers once that pillar well and truly stands<br /> <br /> Now, it's a joke, now, just how much I did that second one(23,500+ words, how the fuck do I have <i>that much problem with anything?!</i>), but I don't think any can argue that I at least tried to provide context and view. I explained a hell of a lot about my viewpoint-and a big part of that viewpoint was the inclusion of why some of these choices seemed like obvious things to do. In fact, while it's not present in every section, if you go back and read, I start almost all of my sections with, first, some kind of explanation why doing this thing must have seemed the most obvious thing in the world from the point of view of the mad scientist, and what were the things I was talking about before I going into how they mishmashed. Sure, it's not always perfect-for example, in the statistics section, I explain what the section is doing first and then pull a sort of &quot;got'cha&quot; argument with what that means to someone the world is tilted against, and even though I do go back and explain why that's a thing, it's not the best way to have done it. But even if I flub? I think it's clear I tried <i>something</i> on both fronts. Was it enough? Well, probably not-there's a substantial amount of feedback that suggests the contrary.<br /> <br /> But a review that doesn't have any of that? It's not there to provoke thought or deeper appreciation, it's just... Venting. It's all flash no substance, nothing but steam. And often times, the only thing you'll get from that is burns. Not everyone is worth listening to, it is worth repeating. <i>I may not be worth listening to</i>. I can't tell you that. I won't tell you that. You have a brain, you can decide that for yourself.<br /> <br /> <b><u>TO BE CONTINUED-Wait, what?</u></b><br /> <br /> It seems like I'm wrapped up here, but I think a question remains. Sure, I can argue bias is a good thing. But can it be a bad thing?<br /> <br /> Well, yeah, the answer is yes. The better question is &quot;How widely can bias vary an opinion, and at what point can that bias unfairly swing other's opinions?&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm not going to read Genius again for a while, and really I don't want to read anything, but, you know, I think I have a subject we can talk about. Something that, really, honestly, could be okay or could be terrible, depending purely on your bias.<br /> <br /> See you tomorrow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 08-23-2016, 09:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T22:57:00-07:00","id":956173,"title":"","content":"Possibly semi more back on topic - Maybe a means of horror theme can be expressed through tragedy? Playing off the Inspiration angle, maybe Genii are cursed with the inspiration they find in the world around them that allows them to make so much out of seemingly so little, but the tragedy is finding out that the rest of humanity is blind to the inspiration that surrounds them (and every attempt to force them into becoming aware of it doesn't actually open their eyes, it just blinds them with the Genius' own personal Inspiration and turns them into Igors).<br /> <br /> Maybe a newly catalyzed Genius made something inconsequentially charming for his teenage children because he loves them and wants to share the fruit of his inspiration with them in the hopes that they too will find the same joy he does and they can connect like they used to before his wife left him (because none of his inventions ever amounted to anything before and after ten years of arguing about all his junk she couldn't sit by and watch him fail any more). And at first it seems like it works, they love whatever it is and they want to spend more time with dad in his workshop and they want to tinker with some of his leftover ideas. Only it soon becomes clear that they aren't <i>Inspired</i> the way dad is, they just want to see what he makes next. It's all they can think about. They start skipping class to spend more time in dad's workshop. To a Genius, Inspiration is a lantern that is invisible to everyone but themselves. It guides the way for them, but everyone else is doomed to wander in the dark forever, unless they blindly follow the Genius.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T23:38:54-07:00","id":956182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mp122984</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=956130#post956130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I might be misreading, but the sense I get is that that part of the setting is, &quot;Geniuses will change the future, but they haven't caused many visible changes up to now.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> Not really.<br /> <br /> Genius has a current day setting, but the Inspired have at least partial responsibility for that present day setting. To give one example, in the real world one of the most famous conspiracy theories is David Ike's theories about secret lizardmen overlords.<br /> <br /> The leaders of Lemuria actually were lizardmen; so chances are in Genius: the Transgression David Ike's books were written about Lemuria. So that's one small example of Geniuses causing visible changes. There's no list or anything in the book, but it should be easy for a creative storyteller to fill the setting with more examples.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mp122984</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=956130#post956130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which I suppose was done to create a current day setting where supernatural exists but isn't treated as known to exist by the public at large, but it becomes an oddly specific thing when you think about it.</div> </div> </div> </div> Actually there is some mention that the public is aware of inspiration. With the official 2E lines being more explicit that actually mortals know Genius could probably be more open about that too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=956027#post956027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could still keep the concept of a battle for understanding. Kind of about who controls public perception, and who controls meaning.</div> </div> </div> </div> Isn't that Mage: the Ascension?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=956027#post956027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Or you could go a different route and make the tragic horror of Genius about trying to control that meaning, only to find that people believe what they believe, and that signifiers are too hard to change once they're established in people's minds.</div> </div> </div> </div> This feels like taking the existing Genius and narrowing it down.<br /> <br /> If you take a Genius who's Magnum Opus is something along the lines of &quot;make my interpretation of Lord of the Rings the common understanding&quot; you're pretty much get a horror game about trying to control meaning only to find that people believe what they believe.<br /> <br /> <br /> But another way of saying &quot;narrowing it down&quot; is &quot;focusing on&quot;; so basically, best of luck to you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=956027#post956027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would make the game much more internal, and much less focused on building Wonders. I think Wonders can still be present, there should definitely still be mechanics for them, but the mechanics in 1ed are convoluted and confusing, because they--in my opinion--don't hearken back to a cohesive theme. Start with your theme. You have your theme, as I understand it (transgression). Build out from there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wonders do tie into the theme of Transgression. Remember that Transgression and Visionary are two sides of the same coin. Society has rules about what kind of thoughts and ideas are considered acceptable. By definition if you're not breaking those rules, you're not a visionary.<br /> <br /> Genius is about Transgression because Geniuses are visonaries. And Wonders represent the, well, visions that a visionary has.<br /> <br /> A visionary sees something that other people cannot. Wonders let a Genius build that thing, place it in the world among all the people who haven't yet looked &quot;outside of the box&quot;, and see how they react.<br /> <br /> <br /> So while there are some changes to the Wonder rules I'd like to make, I don't think you can say a lack of connection to the theme is why there confusion. Actually I don't think they're confusing at all, but I am a programmer - I deal with far more complex systems every day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T06:32:28-07:00","id":956289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=956182#post956182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wonders do tie into the theme of Transgression. Remember that Transgression and Visionary are two sides of the same coin. Society has rules about what kind of thoughts and ideas are considered acceptable. By definition if you're not breaking those rules, you're not a visionary.<br /> <br /> Genius is about Transgression because Geniuses are visonaries. And Wonders represent the, well, visions that a visionary has.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's all very well to say so, but it's not supported by the text. The Genii in Genius are neither transgressive nor visionary. Wonders aren't built by crossing the limits of acceptable behavior that society sets, and they don't fail because society rejects them; they work because a Genius has successfully deluded himself, and they fail when he can't sustain the delusion any more. Mad science isn't a system of shattering truths that only the strongest minds can understand; it's a magic of seductive, comforting nonsense that dies at the first touch of sober reality. The game says so explicitly and repeatedly - whatever is happening when Inspiration strikes, it is <i>not</i> a true understanding of the world and does <i>not</i> qualify as science even by analogy.<br /> <br /> If transgression is the theme of Genius, Mage - especially in its second edition - is a better Genius than Genius. Supernal magic meddles with the forms and archetypes that give structure and meaning to reality; it treats the fundamentals of all existence as playthings. <i>That</i> is transgression.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T06:36:48-07:00","id":956291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=956289#post956289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's all very well to say so, but it's not supported by the text. The Genii in Genius are neither transgressive nor visionary. Wonders aren't built by crossing the limits of acceptable behavior that society sets, and they don't fail because society rejects them; they work because a Genius has successfully deluded himself, and they fail when he can't sustain the delusion any more. Mad science isn't a system of shattering truths that only the strongest minds can understand; it's a magic of seductive, comforting nonsense that dies at the first touch of sober reality. The game says so explicitly and repeatedly - whatever is happening when Inspiration strikes, it is <i>not</i> a true understanding of the world and does <i>not</i> qualify as science even by analogy.<br /> <br /> If transgression is the theme of Genius, Mage - especially in its second edition - is a better Genius than Genius. Supernal magic meddles with the forms and archetypes that give structure and meaning to reality; it treats the fundamentals of all existence as playthings. <i>That</i> is transgression.</div> </div> </div> </div>But...Michael...it's just super complex. You just don't get it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T06:40:49-07:00","id":956293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>Genius is about Transgression because Geniuses are visonaries.</i> </div> </div> </div>Their culture <i>literally tells them to regard what they do as nonsense</i>. <i>Nothing</i> about that is <i>visionary</i>.<br /> <br /> Just saying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T07:29:40-07:00","id":956308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=956289#post956289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it's a magic of seductive, comforting nonsense that dies at the first touch of sober reality.</div> </div> </div> </div> Which is exactly why I like it.<br /> <br /> The idea that the World Wide Web would usher in a new era of egalitarianism where everyone had an equal voice was seductive and comforting, and it was also nonsense; the moment sober reality hit we saw that the web was just more of the same as meatspace in a more convenient packaging.<br /> <br /> <br /> I don't know if visionaries who's ideas turned out to be seductive nonsense are more common or less common than visionaries who turned out to be right about everything. But they're prominent enough in both real science and the mad science archetype that you can base a game of them. Genius chose to do so; it's magic of seductive, comforting nonsense makes perfect sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=956289#post956289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If transgression is the theme of Genius, Mage - especially in its second edition - is a better Genius than Genius. Supernal magic meddles with the forms and archetypes that give structure and meaning to reality; it treats the fundamentals of all existence as playthings. <i>That</i> is transgression.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see messing with forms and archetypes to be transgressive. The underlying principles of Awakened magic is too abstract to give me that same instinctual revulsion I'd get if I saw somebody cutting up another human being for parts or posting a dissertation explaining why racism is good.<br /> <br /> But each to their own.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=956293#post956293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Their culture <i>literally tells them to regard what they do as nonsense</i>. <i>Nothing</i> about that is <i>visionary</i>.<br /> <br /> Just saying.</div> </div> </div> </div>To use Changeling 1E as an illustration. Changeling's have an entire culture, the Spring Court, based around denial of the trauma of Arcadia. Does the Spring Court's existance imply that Arcadia was not traumatic or does it imply that Arcadia was traumatic?<br /> <br /> Genius culture is based around convincing the Inspired that they're not visionaries. The fact that they put so much effort into convincing themselves suggests that they are in fact visionaries. Albeit ones who have a very good reason to try and convince themselves they're not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 08-23-2016, 10:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T07:39:32-07:00","id":956312,"title":"","content":"Honestly, Sean, I thought this thread was for your review. At the beginning, I went out of my way trying to help Gecko and TKR, only because they said they were here for revision of Genius, as they're rewriting versions of their own. But you told me not to help, because we would be disregarded, and you were right. It's become nearly twenty pages of, honestly, back and forth with one side reading past the other, and, at times, saying offensive shit just for the sake of it. Your players said I was being more helpful than they deserved, and now I think they were right. I spent a lot of time thinking critically about the questions TKR asked, and I spent a lot of time composing my answers and finding resources to provide, but you and your players were right, it was a waste of my time. I propose that we stop letting the thread get derailed, and talk about your review critically, and nothing else.<br /> <br /> Honestly, both Gecko and TKR: if you don't like the suggestions you've been provided with because you think they'll change your games too much, fine. We're not writing them, you are. I honestly couldn't give a shit what you change and what you don't. You asked us questions about how we would do the game, and we've been answering. We've told you what games we would play and what we wouldn't. Maybe you don't care. A game can't please everyone. Maybe you don't care if we're the ones you don't please. But you are the ones who came here asking for how we would handle it, and we've told you. You say these changes would affect the game too much. Yeah. That's why we're recommending them. Because the game is convoluted, loose, disorganized, and does not revolve around the central theme you keep repeating. <br /> <br /> Maybe you disagree. That's fine. Again, you can't make everyone happy. But it's pretty clear at this point that the group of us over here agree on pretty much everything we're telling you. It's been presented to you over the course of twenty-two pages. Let's talk about what we're talking about or not. This is SEAN'S thread to review the product, and you came to TELL Sean that the thread would be helpful for you for development. This is not your thread to defend Genius. This is SEAN'S thread to review Genius. Take it or leave it, or start your own thread. Twenty-two pages is enough of a derailment, I'd say.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T07:45:35-07:00","id":956314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=956312#post956312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, both Gecko and TKR: if you don't like the suggestions you've been provided with because you think they'll change your games too much, fine.</div> </div> </div> </div> Wait? You thought I was here to get ideas for a revision?<br /> <br /> In retrospect I suppose I shouldn't be suprise, it's a big thread so it's easy for stuff to get lost; back on Page 11 I said Arc's revisions would probably make a good game but it wouldn't be Genius.<br /> <br /> But basically, I'm not here for ideas on how to fix Genius. I'm hear to learn more about other people's viewpoints, because agree or disagree, your views are still interesting and worth hearing more about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T08:16:43-07:00","id":956327,"title":"","content":"I came to see if Genius was worth my time, and after Chapter 1 I'm pretty sure it's not. That said, it's also helping me get a gameline of my own started, and seeing what Sean has said has been helping greatly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T08:38:07-07:00","id":956341,"title":"","content":"I came here (and subscribed) to see what an indepth review would be like (even if it started out, in my opinion, in bad faith). I responded when I saw others stating things that seemed unsupported in the material (ideally to foster a better understanding - it looks like some people are commenting without having actually read it themselves, just basing their points on hear-say).<br /> <br /> (I dropped out of commenting because the thread has run away and I've had to deal with Comcast &quot;Customer Service&quot; - but that's beside the point)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=956327#post956327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I came to see if Genius was worth my time, and after Chapter 1 I'm pretty sure it's not. That said, it's also helping me get a gameline of my own started, and seeing what Sean has said has been helping greatly.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And this is why (accurate) reviews matter. Someone sees smoke, and avoids reading for themselves.<br /> <br /> (<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1923_4.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1923\" data-vbnamecard=\"1923\">BigDamnHero</a> it is probable that you and ArcaneArts's preferences align enough that their grievances are enough, but I'm talking generally in the above sentence, even though I'm quoting you directly in this post.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T09:10:22-07:00","id":956360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=956341#post956341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1923_4.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1923\" data-vbnamecard=\"1923\">BigDamnHero</a> it is probable that you and ArcaneArts's preferences align enough that their grievances are enough, but I'm talking generally in the above sentence, even though I'm quoting you directly in this post.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, Changeling has never managed to light my fire, so I'm pretty sure Arts's and I's preferences don't align <i>that</i> much. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Some of our biases match though: I'm not attracted to the concept of the mad scientist, and I think if you have a game about mad science then actual science needs to be a part of it (whether that means naturalists, Greek philosophers, or Marie Curie). From what I saw in the review, and TKR and Gecko's responses, Genius <i>doesn't</i> do that. Also, I really don't like Ascension because I think the Consensus is...I don't have anything kind to say about it. I don't think character belief should affect <i>anything </i>unless you're playing a really abstract game like <i>Wisher, Theurgist, Fatalist</i>. I thought Paradigms were fine as a concept, but Awakening does it better than Ascension because in Ascension, your belief actually had an effect. In Awakening, your style is more about your preferred system of mnemonics, which I think is the best way to handle something like that.<br /> <br /> I've never touched English from an Academic standpoint: I'm a computer scientist with a major in information security. When I first checked out Genius back in the day, I thought it looked fun because I was in the middle of my degree and it seemed like a natural fit, but a skim didn't grab me. Being older and more knowledgable about game design, now that I've read Sean's review I'm still not seeing anything work going back for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T09:23:08-07:00","id":956375,"title":"","content":"Okay so here's some rambling thoughts that I've tried to trim down into a narrative that makes sense about a way to do horror in genius.<br /> <br /> Divorce Inspiration from mental illness while still maintaining a thematic connection. Inspiration strikes without warning, without regard to any identifying features at all (race, age, sex, etc), but it doesn't make you <i>crazy</i>. What it does is make you <i>dysfunctional</i>. Just because you are Inspired, it doesn't make you a Genius - that's status only comes once you've made a Wonder. Instead, you're constantly distracted by the potential in the world that you can't articulate to anyone else. Inspiration's first great tragedy and horror is that it isolates it's heralds. The second great tragedy and horror is that Society sees these people and it throws them away because they get labeled &quot;defective&quot;, children inaccurately get labled with hyperactivity or attention deficit disorders that they don't have (or simply as problem children). Adults are likewise labled with mental illnesses they don't have (or simple laziness), while the elderly get diagnosed with dementia.<br /> <br /> Society punishes them for circumstances beyond their control. The <b>Transgression</b> isn't Inspiration driving you insane, it's society <b>gaslighting</b> you because of it. In ideal world, being forced to carry the burden of an inescapable and inarticulatable creative urge wouldn't be a social death sentence. Ideally, society would recognise that there's some sort of untapped talent and the Inspired would gravitate to positions where creativity is celebrated - many would become artists or musicians or similar things. Instead, you're told that you are broken and defective* and you're left to fend for yourself in a dark world. That kind of thing builds up a great deal of emotion. Mixing that emotion and your Inspiration and <i>sometimes</i> that catalyzes into your first Wonder. Congratulations! You are now a Genius, capable of articulating your Inspiration to others.<br /> <br /> Only, you can't share this with Society any more than you could have before! Your theories inspired by your Inspiration make no sense to the un-Inspired, and they mock you for them. Your devices short out and break when you try to reveal them to the teeming masses. Maybe there's some heretofore inexpiable force that breaks your Wonders in the face of un-inspired scrutiny in a manner that makes the wreckage look like mundane tech with some special effects mixed in (your broken ray gun looks like a pistol rigged up with lights now), some Genii struggle against this process by trying to raise the general technological level to the point where what they do falls into what the un-inspired can accept (before guns were invented, a broken Wonder that worked like a gun would look like a fancy crossbow or something under un-inspired scrutiny). The third great tragedy and horror of Genius is now the nagging worry that Society is somehow correct, that you and all your peers are somehow delusional. The <b>Transgression</b> Society commits against you now forces you to deal with the urge to gaslight yourself.<br /> <br /> *depending on how deep you want to take it, you can also dig into racism and classism when dealing with this. A six year old Inspired from a rich white new england family that can hire all the best tutors gets more support for their creative and bright child, while the poor dark skinned six year old with a single mother taking care of them gets labeled with an attitude problem and failed by the system. Digging into that further than what I just did is beyond the scope of this post (and I don't want to derail the thread through a discussion of the injusties of society)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T09:53:54-07:00","id":956386,"title":"","content":"You know, I have mentioned in quite a few of my posts areas in which I planned to take inspiration from Sean's criticisms, so that's not really fair. I have explicitly said that: I am going to do away with the statistics and demographics section, I am going to further explain why geniuses don't break the masquerade, I am going to explain why players should bother trying despite the atmosphere of hopelessness, and so on. Sure, there are things Sean wants to change that I think are fine and won't change, but you can't say I haven't acknowledged some of his criticisms and taken inspiration from them. Also, I am one hundred percent certain that if/when Sean reached the gameplay and Wonder mechanics he would have criticized those, and the main reason why I made a new game instead of just updating Genius was because of how badly the mechanics needed an overhaul. I was genuinely looking forward to seeing his suggestions for how to make Wonder creation and other things less of a massive pain. <br /> <br /> I have to say, I find it quite funny that Sean ends his essay on bias (which I'm not sure was necessary- everyone's biased. I can deal with that. If no one could review something they were biased towards, no one could review anything.) by saying that Genius could be &quot;okay or terrible&quot; based on perspective, while knowing full well that many people consider it to be neither okay nor terrible, but, in fact, amazing. <br /> <br /> In fact, to summarize and keeping in mind that Genius came out during 1e ChroD, I'd say that it's along my top three, with Changeling and Mummy. 1e ChroD was a mess of good and bad mixed together, and is best evaluated in hindsight in terms of potential. And Genius' good shined so brightly to outweight the bad, and its potential was unmatched.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T10:43:06-07:00","id":956410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=956308#post956308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To use Changeling 1E as an illustration. Changeling's have an entire culture, the Spring Court, based around denial of the trauma of Arcadia.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really disagree with your reading of Changeling 1e. Do you have a better example?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T11:08:56-07:00","id":956434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=956410#post956410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really disagree with your reading of Changeling 1e. Do you have a better example?</div> </div> </div> </div>I won't go of topic trying to convince you about Changeling,<br /> <br /> I'm sure I could dig out a post by changeling's lead dev agreeing with the stages of grief interpretation though, so I'm comfortable sticking to Spring=Denial as an example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 08-23-2016, 02:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T11:10:06-07:00","id":956436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=956308#post956308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To use Changeling 1E as an illustration. Changeling's have an entire culture, the Spring Court, based around denial of the trauma of Arcadia. Does the Spring Court's existance imply that Arcadia was not traumatic or does it imply that Arcadia was traumatic?</div> </div> </div> </div>The spring court is based on a lot of things, but not that. It's saying &quot;We were traumatized, but now we get to define ourselves how we want to be defined&quot;. It's saying &quot;I don't want to suffer any more, I want to have fun&quot;. It's saying &quot;I spent seven years chained at the bottom of the ocean, now that I've escaped I'm trying to make up for lost time by eating so much pussy that I'm gonna be shitting clits&quot;. It's saying &quot;Yo there's a horrible part of me that really really wants to go back because arcadia is like a drug, so whenever I get stressed I have to numb myself with whatever drugs are handy to drown out the horrible intrusive thoughts telling me to go back&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T11:12:20-07:00","id":956437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=956434#post956434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I won't go of topic trying to convince you about Changeling,<br /> <br /> I'm sure I could dig out a post by changeling's lead dev agreeing with the stages of grief interpretation though, so I'm comfortable sticking to Spring=Denial as an example.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really care about your reading of Changeling, but it's detracting from your point about Genius.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T11:26:27-07:00","id":956444,"title":"","content":"I think I did get a lot of this thread. As an example of how I'm deliberately using the criticisms people have brought up, the comments about sticking to a theme helped me do something I'd been struggling with for a while: incorporating the Atlantis/Golden Age mythology from Awakening into the backstory. I knew I wanted Atlantis to be a significant Bardo, as well as Lemuria, but the idea of sticking with the concept of transgression gave me a burst of inspiration.<br /> <br /> Also, I'm going to just slightly tweak my description of the Abyss for that theme. The new Abyss has a strong theme of &quot;breaking things&quot; or &quot;corrosion&quot;, and I'm going to emphasize that what the Abyss does is essentially transgression stripped down: it's ultimately the primordial root of what Mages do. It breaks things not because of some higher purpose or desire, but because they're there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 08-23-2016, 02:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T12:08:27-07:00","id":956478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=956172#post956172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b><u>TO BE CONTINUED-Wait, what?</u></b><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like if you were one of the old school White Wolf writers, your special thanks nickname would be, like,<br /> <br /> <b>Sean </b>&quot;What Even Is Brevity? Brevity is said to be the soul of wit, but in truth, this an arguable constraint on the creative process, in that sometimes the words must fit the idea, in that the magnitude of the idea, qua idea, needs to be reflected by the quantity of words. This isn't to say filler is a virtue (fuck no), but as Hideaki Anno said, in reference to the fickle nature of fan reaction--I'm repurposing the thought, yeah, but--&quot; <b>Steele</b><br /> <br /> TL;DR: Hayley get the spray bottle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T12:58:34-07:00","id":956505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TidyGamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=956436#post956436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The spring court is based on a lot of things, but not that.</div> </div> </div> </div>What the hell. I went and dug out that post.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?567853-NWOD-The-NWOD-as-a-reaction-to-itself&amp;p=13699141#post13699141\" target=\"_blank\">Here it is</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ethen Skemp, Changeling: the Lost Developer</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The incredibly smart Rob Donoghue once observed, quite to my surprise, that the Five Stages of Grief are represented almost explicitly by the four Courts -- who, of course, are social coping mechanisms writ large. <b><u>Denial is Spring</u></b> (not 100%, but quite arguable)</div> </div> </div> </div>Feel free to disagree, everyone can have their own interpretaion. But if you want to say Spring=Denial isn't even a valid interpretation when the developer says that it is. I'm just going to disagree with you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T13:06:11-07:00","id":956506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=956072#post956072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally would have described it as superbly messy up to just below the surface, but that works too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup, and because of that, it's time for me to nope on out of here. Thank you Arc, the review of the first chapter was interesting and the tl;dr was supremely helpful in terms of my own writing. I will periodically check the first page for the other chapter reviews. Good luck!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":4433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","user":"Second Chances","date":". 08-23-2016, 04:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T14:29:31-07:00","id":956553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=956505#post956505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What the hell. I went and dug out that post.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?567853-NWOD-The-NWOD-as-a-reaction-to-itself&amp;p=13699141#post13699141\" target=\"_blank\">Here it is</a><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Feel free to disagree, everyone can have their own interpretaion. But if you want to say Spring=Denial isn't even a valid interpretation when the developer says that it is. I'm just going to disagree with you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Denial in the sense that most spring courtiers are trying to put their time in arcadia behind them through pursuing things THEY want to do is totally not the same thing as Denial in the sense that they believe Arcadia wasn't traumatic though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T17:51:27-07:00","id":956655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=956478#post956478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel like if you were one of the old school White Wolf writers, your special thanks nickname would be, like,<br /> <br /> <b>Sean </b>&quot;What Even Is Brevity? Brevity is said to be the soul of wit, but in truth, this an arguable constraint on the creative process, in that sometimes the words must fit the idea, in that the magnitude of the idea, qua idea, needs to be reflected by the quantity of words. This isn't to say filler is a virtue (fuck no), but as Hideaki Anno said, in reference to the fickle nature of fan reaction--I'm repurposing the thought, yeah, but--&quot; <b>Steele</b><br /> <br /> TL;DR: Hayley get the spray bottle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh stop it.<br /> <br /> Like I would even quote Hideaki Anno.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, Brevity is for work. Length is for pleasure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T18:03:40-07:00","id":956663,"title":"","content":"Look guys. I don't care if you disagree with me or not. I have invited you, time and time again, to tell me I am wrong, and even to say I am an asshole. You have that right, and I'm not going to tell you no.<br /> <br /> However, don't be an asshole about it. And if you catch someone being an asshole about it, flag them.<br /> <br /> PS: Previous version lacked tact in regards to my friendships, in case you were wondering.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 08-23-2016, 09:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T18:12:08-07:00","id":956667,"title":"","content":"Completely over it today.<br /> <br /> And my name is spelled with two y's, everyone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":3093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","user":"hm8453a","date":". 08-23-2016, 09:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T18:18:09-07:00","id":956669,"title":"","content":"&quot;The behavior and reactions of fans is part of the exercise&quot; man trying to pull a &quot;just according to keikaku&quot; never works. That's my advice for you. See you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Ge