"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T19:53:06-07:00","id":956712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=956705#post956705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've never even seen an episode, really.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you care about anime culture, it is a must because of a shit ton of reasons. By itself? I won't tell you no, but don't rush to it either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T19:56:59-07:00","id":956714,"title":"","content":"While we're on this tangent... people do realize Hideaki Anno has done other things than Evangelion, right?<br /> <br /> And he's actually said a lot of things worth paraphrasing (direct quoting can get problematic... he's not that careful about certain terms), esp. regarding the creative process/design.<br /> <br /> Something that he's said that I think it very relevant to RPGs, and the kind of stuff that gets discussed in reviews and advice, is that it's really important to go back and experience the classics; even if you're probably not going to like it. Knowing why D&amp;D remains so influential has a lot of lessons even if you don't want to make something anything like D&amp;D.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T20:38:44-07:00","id":956751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=956714#post956714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While we're on this tangent... people do realize Hideaki Anno has done other things than Evangelion, right?<br /> <br /> And he's actually said a lot of things worth paraphrasing (direct quoting can get problematic... he's not that careful about certain terms), esp. regarding the creative process/design.<br /> <br /> Something that he's said that I think it very relevant to RPGs, and the kind of stuff that gets discussed in reviews and advice, is that it's really important to go back and experience the classics; even if you're probably not going to like it. Knowing why D&amp;D remains so influential has a lot of lessons even if you don't want to make something anything like D&amp;D.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is impossible to bring up Anno without mentioning Eva, though.<br /> <br /> Not the least of which being that he keeps going back to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T21:00:24-07:00","id":956764,"title":"","content":"Herein lie tangential thoughts unrelated to Genius in any way.<br /> <br /> Eva was the first anime for me to be rendered unwatchable by its fans (though far from the last). Were I to have experienced it in its own right I imagine I could have potentially appreciated it for what it was. Having had it so impossibly overhyped to me by its legions of slavish adherents only to subsequently be pilloried for failing to comprehend its manifest greatness, it exists to me forever as an extension of that fandom and what I perceive to be its militant shallowness. Evangelion is the Whole Foods of anime. <br /> <br /> D&amp;D for better or for worse defines what RPGs are. That is not to say that it defines the limitations of the medium in any way, but rather that it acts to define what our baseline is. All RPGs at some level exist in conversation with D&amp;D, whether in asserting how they are similar to it or in asserting how dissimilar they are to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T22:11:24-07:00","id":956783,"title":"","content":"Follow up Bias thingy tomorrow, I am having good roleplay in Changeling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T22:11:36-07:00","id":956784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=956663#post956663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look guys. I don't care if you disagree with me or not. I have invited you, time and time again, to tell me I 