>There's always Facebook ^_^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T07:22:56-07:00","id":957607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=957586#post957586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Y'all want me to review something, like actually review it o.0?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd be fine with a small comment after each episode. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T07:36:24-07:00","id":957613,"title":"","content":"Just don't read about it or ask questions. Consume it with empty mind. It's a show watched best when knowing nothing about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T11:17:14-07:00","id":957723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=957421#post957421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just on one point, we go three radically different views of the game, and even that's not true because it's all my speculation. There's no objectivity there-there's just bias and whether or not you think the bias is worth the consideration.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still, isn't that the true purpose of a review? Objectively every product is consumable to at least one party (the person who created the product at the time of its creation, though arguably that person may cease to exist as art is static and people are not).<br /> <br /> Subjectively, reviews allow other parties to tell whether or not a product is palatable (regardless of its edibility) by comparing their biases against those of the reviewing author. If the review is too short (as you've discussed), the prospective reader doesn't learn enough about the reviewer and thus cannot gauge similarities. However, if the review is thorough (as you've done for Genius and now Princess) readers can use the power of the writer's language to establish a percentage of common ground and then decide what percentage of reaction is likely to be shared.<br /> <br /> That's why lots of reviews from different parties are more useful than a singular review, even one as in-depth as yours. That way the prospective reader can piece together bits of review from multiple perspectives to tailor an impression appropriate to their interests.<br /> <br /> To that end, don't try to hide your bias. Make it apparent with the knowledge your review will be one component in a larger collage of consumer opinion. If anything, being transparent about your first impressions is helpful.<br /> <br /> <br /> I found the part about the city Alhambra and tip-toeing through the darkened alleys of an inter-dimensional acropolis (which I took as a shortcut through hell) quite intriguing, despite the fact that anime and specifically magical girls are kind of meh for me. That to me indicates that there might be some meat to the game's cosmological setting, even if the character concepts aren't ones that mesh with my preferences. So your bias in favor of the genre didn't stop me from drawing positive conclusions from the review, even though my own tastes differ from yours. In fact, your critical examination of the setting coupled with your bias indicates that perhaps the game might be geared closer to people who are less dedicated to Anime as a cultural medium.<br /> Hmm... I seem to have rambled my way into a corner. Do I just delete this whole paragraph? ...Nah, I guess it's relevant.<br /> <br /> Anyway, in conclusion bias is good as long as its presence is clear. It allows the review's reader to properly assign weight to praise and criticism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T12:45:38-07:00","id":957779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=957723#post957723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still, isn't that the true purpose of a review? Objectively every product is consumable to at least one party (the person who created the product at the time of its creation, though arguably that person may cease to exist as art is static and people are not).<br /> <br /> Subjectively, reviews allow other parties to tell whether or not a product is palatable (regardless of its edibility) by comparing their biases against those of the reviewing author. If the review is too short (as you've discussed), the prospective reader doesn't learn enough about the reviewer and thus cannot gauge similarities. However, if the review is thorough (as you've done for Genius and now Princess) readers can use the power of the writer's language to establish a percentage of common ground and then decide what percentage of reaction is likely to be shared.<br /> <br /> That's why lots of reviews from different parties are more useful than a singular review, even one as in-depth as yours. That way the prospective reader can piece together bits of review from multiple perspectives to tailor an impression appropriate to their interests.<br /> <br /> To that end, don't try to hide your bias. Make it apparent with the knowledge your review will be one component in a larger collage of consumer opinion. If anything, being transparent about your first impressions is helpful.<br /> <br /> <br /> I found the part about the city Alhambra and tip-toeing through the darkened alleys of an inter-dimensional acropolis (which I took as a shortcut through hell) quite intriguing, despite the fact that anime and specifically magical girls are kind of meh for me. That to me indicates that there might be some meat to the game's cosmological setting, even if the character concepts aren't ones that mesh with my preferences. So your bias in favor of the genre didn't stop me from drawing positive conclusions from the review, even though my own tastes differ from yours. In fact, your critical examination of the setting coupled with your bias indicates that perhaps the game might be geared closer to people who are less dedicated to Anime as a cultural medium.<br /> Hmm... I seem to have rambled my way into a corner. Do I just delete this whole paragraph? ...Nah, I guess it's relevant.<br /> <br /> Anyway, in conclusion bias is good as long as its presence is clear. It allows the review's reader to properly assign weight to praise and criticism.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure Sean included that section in response to someone specific, I might be wrong.<br /> <br /> Then again, I'm pretty sure the <b>Princess </b>review in general was for someone specific (and not me, that's not what I mean).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T13:22:26-07:00","id":957805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=957779#post957779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm pretty sure Sean included that section in response to someone specific, I might be wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I interpreted it as a sense of self doubt about the utility of the review due to the bias being present, and I was trying to reassure that bias is a very important component of the reviewing process. After I posted it I realized that the original review of Genius said in as many words that the bias was necessary because objective reviews lacked much utility.<br /> <br /> I'm now embarrassed that I've contributed nothing to the conversation, so I'm just going to be quiet over here for a while.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T13:41:01-07:00","id":957819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=957805#post957805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, I interpreted it as a sense of self doubt about the utility of the review due to the bias being present, and I was trying to reassure that bias is a very important component of the reviewing process. After I posted it I realized that the original review of Genius said in as many words that the bias was necessary because objective reviews lacked much utility.<br /> <br /> I'm now embarrassed that I've contributed nothing to the conversation, so I'm just going to be quiet over here for a while.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No! No no, I didn't mean that!<br /> <br /> I just meant. Like, I was saying wow about the <b>Princess </b>review in general because it seemed like a reaction to a particular poster on this thread who says mean things about other posters just because they like particular games (one of which is <b>Princess</b>). And that poster has made comments on these forums and elsewhere about Sean's bias, like it's a problem that Sean has a bias (meanwhile, as you say, literally everyone is biased and literally everything is politics).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T17:37:09-07:00","id":957949,"title":"","content":"I said in this thread that I wasn't even sure the bias section in the original review was necessary, because all reviewers are biased. I do not care about bias.<br /> <br /> I'm human shit, but I'm not the type of shit that whines about bias. <br /> <br /> Rereading Princess, I'd like to apologize, actually. It's isn't awful, it's a perfectly serviceable magical girl game. I just happen to think that ChroD doesn't need that: or, if you wanted magical girls in ChroD, you could either incorporate them into an existing line or majorly alter the universe. I honestly would like Princess better if it made major changes to the setting and said outright: we know the original setting isn't meant for this, so we changed it and now it is. I'm fine with the stuff in Mirrors. If you want magic superheroes, have you considered making a &quot;World of Dark Heroes&quot; thread?<br /> <br /> Anyway, what I'm apologizing for is how hyperbolically I've complained about Mage and Princess when, if I'm being honest with myself, the only actual I problem I have with them is that I don't think they fit. I think they're both actually quite nice on their own, though neither really interests me. I don't know why things &quot;not fitting&quot; pushes me into being a rage-fueled unproductive dumbass, it's just a thing I have, that I should admit is a thing that's wrong. <br /> <br /> Anime Was Still A Mistake, though. Except Jojo. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> If you have been on tumblr, you know what I've been going through, so I'll try to leave for a while. I just got sucked back today because I ended up writing up a bunch of Mage stuff and figured I might as well post it. I don't know. About anything, I mean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 08-25-2016, 08:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T18:48:04-07:00","id":957982,"title":"","content":"I used it as an example because the nature of bias was a big enough issue I felt like addressing it.<br /> <br /> That the discussion means more to some than others is just icing on the cake.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T18:58:56-07:00","id":957989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=957949#post957949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I said in this thread that I wasn't even sure the bias section in the original review was necessary, because all reviewers are biased. I do not care about bias.<br /> <br /> I'm human shit, but I'm not the type of shit that whines about bias.<br /> <br /> Rereading Princess, I'd like to apologize, actually. It's isn't awful, it's a perfectly serviceable magical girl game. I just happen to think that ChroD doesn't need that: or, if you wanted magical girls in ChroD, you could either incorporate them into an existing line or majorly alter the universe. I honestly would like Princess better if it made major changes to the setting and said outright: we know the original setting isn't meant for this, so we changed it and now it is. I'm fine with the stuff in Mirrors. If you want magic superheroes, have you considered making a &quot;World of Dark Heroes&quot; thread?<br /> <br /> Anyway, what I'm apologizing for is how hyperbolically I've complained about Mage and Princess when, if I'm being honest with myself, the only actual I problem I have with them is that I don't think they fit. I think they're both actually quite nice on their own, though neither really interests me. I don't know why things &quot;not fitting&quot; pushes me into being a rage-fueled unproductive dumbass, it's just a thing I have, that I should admit is a thing that's wrong.<br /> <br /> Anime Was Still A Mistake, though. Except Jojo. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> If you have been on tumblr, you know what I've been going through, so I'll try to leave for a while. I just got sucked back today because I ended up writing up a bunch of Mage stuff and figured I might as well post it. I don't know. About anything, I mean.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for apologizing. I told you on Tumblr that I was there for you if you needed psychological or emotional support, and like I told you in my reblog of your post, I really meant that. I was there to help you until you attacked my friends just because you didn't like them. I told you, and I meant it--if someone, anyone, my friends included, had actually HURT you, I'm the first person to expel toxic friends. But that wasn't what was going on, and I felt like you were taking advantage of me. Thank you for apologizing to Sean, and for holding yourself accountable. Disliking a game is fine. Thinking it doesn't fit is fine. I'll be there for people through all of that, but not through uncalled-for rudeness to people I care about. If you need to talk, let me know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T19:07:27-07:00","id":957993,"title":"","content":"Despite being an anime fan, I can definitely agree with anime being a mistake.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T19:33:04-07:00","id":958005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius?p=957553#post957553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your review of Princess is making me really want to see a proper 2E &quot;Chronicle&quot; treatment for it, Arcane.</div> </div> </div> </div>The <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/home\" target=\"_blank\">site the game is on</a> is still updating, and <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?718445-Princess-the-Hopeful-Elsa-s-Elegant-Eighth-Thread\" target=\"_blank\">discussions</a> on updating, adding, and tweaking things here and there are ongoing.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8064-mp122984","name":"mp122984","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T22:07:46-07:00","id":958060,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry to hijack your thread, Arc, but I just had to say that I was pretty objectively an unreasonable and pointlessly antagonistic shitbag and I'm sorry for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 08-26-2016, 02:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","cou